(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to extend the stamp duty exemption for home buyers with a value of less than or equal to US $ 70,000 until the end of December 2021 from a housing developer registered with the Ministry of Economy and Finance and / or Or at the Department of Economy and Finance.
The decision to extend the stamp duty exemption for home buyers under $ 70,000 until the end of 2021 is seen by experts as a good and timely strategy at a time when the world as well as Cambodia is facing an economic crisis. Kovid-19.
Mr. Chrek Soknim, President of the New Association of Cambodian Real Estate Appraisers and Agents (CVEA) for the 7th mandate in 2021, emphasized that after the Royal Government decided to extend the stamp duty for another year, it will make the sale of houses below 7 Ten thousand dollars will have a lot of current.
Mr. Chrek Soknim said that during this period, it is a challenge for the economy if the trade flow is not allowed to be strong. Both the economy and the government will make the flow of the economy not work well.
The president of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors added that the Royal Government's vision of exempting the stamp duty on home purchases below $ 70,000 would improve the livelihoods of the middle and lower middle class.
Along with the continued stamp duty exemption, the government has also called on all housing developers to join the government in lowering house prices as much as possible.
Please be informed that in February 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced a stamp duty exemption for houses worth less than $ 70,000 for one year, from February 2020 to January 2021. But now, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to extend the favor for another year until the end of 2021.
