Her Majesty the Queen Visits Chinese Embassy in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): In response to the visit of Mr. Wang Vinthean, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, on January 14, 2021, Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia in Freedom, Dignity and Happiness, was pleased. King Yeang completes the royal visit and cuts the ribbon to inaugurate the "Cambodia-China Friendship Park" at the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia.
Her Royal Highness Princess Norodom Arunrasmey, Supreme Personal Adviser to the King, His Royal Highness the King of Cambodia, His Excellency Srung Kear Kong Sam Ol, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Royal Palace of Cambodia, Ms. Zuo Wenxing, Political Adviser of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia, and many other diplomats. Presence and presence in the inauguration ceremony above.
Before the start of the ceremony, Her Majesty the Queen had the permission of the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia to bow down.
The Queen Mother said that she was very pleased to respond to the Chinese Ambassador's homage to preside over the inauguration ceremony.
He added that His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King Father, the father of independence, territorial integrity and national unity, and he himself was an old friend of the Chinese people. He was thrilled that Chinese President Xi Jinping presented him with the Friendship Medal of the People's Republic of China.
The Queen Mother also said that this great honor is not only his, but also a great honor for all Cambodians. Today, he is also very excited after seeing the mango tree, which is a precious gift from His Majesty the King and himself to the Chinese Embassy, has grown well, branched, green and rich. With many fruits.
The Queen thanked the embassy officials of all generations for taking care of these two mango trees with the utmost care, and she will continue to deepen the friendship between China and Cambodia to another level.
The Chinese Ambassador, on behalf of all officials in the Embassy, expressed his deepest gratitude to the Queen for taking the time to preside over the inauguration ceremony held at the Chinese Embassy.
The ambassador said that "the previous generation planted trees, the next generation received shade", as well as the friendship between China and Cambodia, which is under the careful care of His Majesty the King and the Chinese leadership. In the past, only the two countries could become "steel friends" and a common destiny community as they are today.
Wang Winthean said that China has a saying, "Drink water, do not forget the well digger" as a remembrance and a good memory for the noble deeds of the two countries in nurturing the friendship between the two countries. This is also for the younger generation to find out more and continue to develop this friendship even better. The Chinese Embassy has named the garden with the two mango trees "Cambodia-China Friendship Garden".
In the presence of the Queen, the Chinese Ambassador said that the Chinese Embassy will continue to take care of these two mango trees with the utmost care and strive to cultivate more new shoots so that the mango trees, which are The symbol of China-Cambodia friendship continues to grow from generation to generation.
