(Phnom Penh): Due to the crisis of the spread of Kovid 19, the tourism sector in Cambodia has been severely affected as more than 200 hotels, guesthouses, nearly 300 locations and many tourism businesses have been closed. .
The Ministry stated that throughout 2020, 259 hotels with 14,453 rooms and 294 guest houses with 3,171 rooms will be closed in the whole year. They include Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Svay Rieng, Kampot, Banteay Meanchey and Battambang.
The Ministry of Tourism said that so far no hotel or guest house has reopened, only more closed.
Ms. Khay Chenda, President of the Cambodian Hotel Association (CHA), said that almost throughout 2020, resorts and tourist sites of the members of the Cambodian Hotel Association did not have foreign tourists to stay and visit only tourists in A few districts that stay during festivals, but still can not afford to spend enough in hotels.
She said that in the face of the crisis, some hotels were forced to close, while others remained open but had to reduce their salaries to keep their jobs.
Please be informed that in addition to the impact on tourism above, the employment sector in Cambodia is also very seriously affected. In the face of this, the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided to release all budgets and measures to support these two sectors. Which has suspended employment contracts in these two sectors 45 times.
