Minister Veng Sakhon Establishes Working Group to Prevent and Suppress the Transportation of Fishery Products, Import, Export and Transit Without Permission
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, decided to establish a working group to prevent and suppress the transportation of fishery products, import, export and transit without permission. This is according to the decision that Fresh News received on the afternoon of January 14, 2021.
The working group is co-chaired by Mr. Nao Thuok and Mr. Has Sareth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Agriculture, accompanied by 2 Vice-Chairmen and 8 other members.
According to the decision, this working group has the following tasks:
* Conduct operations to prevent and suppress the transportation of agricultural products, export, import and transit without permission throughout Cambodia.
* Search for perpetrators and stakeholders to prepare a case file for fisheries crimes according to the procedure
Take action according to the procedures of the Fisheries Law and relevant legal standards
* Cooperate with relevant authorities and capital-provincial administrations for work efficiency
* Promote and strengthen the work of the Fisheries Authority of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Capital-Province on the transportation of fishery products, import, export and transit without permission.
* Summarize the result report to the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries
