Chhay Sophal, the author of the book, described that this book shows the events in Cambodia from 1970 to 2020, where Cambodia goes through all tastes, especially when the Western and Asian powers are competing in terms of weapons, technology, economy, trade, ideology. Political Science and Geography.
Mr. Chhay Sophal, who is also a professor of information, stated, "Indeed, Cambodians, including foreigners, know who Samdech Techo Hun Sen is, but they are unlikely to be aware of the many interconnected issues that Cambodia has gone through." "Bloody genocide, killing each other in the flames of war, including genocide itself, until the country is at peace so far."
He added that although the book cited Samdech Techo Hun Sen as a character, the book also described political, military and internal social events in Cambodia, as well as foreign affairs related to Cambodia.
According to Chhay Sophal, the war in Cambodia is not just a Cambodian issue, but a regional issue, as well as the sowing of ideologies by world powers such as the United States, some countries in Europe and Asia. And Asia Pacific.
He stressed that ending the war by bringing peace to Cambodia is the happiness and development of Cambodia itself and the peace of the nations in Southeast Asia.
The book also mentions that Samdech Techo was the Prime Minister who went through life as a plantation boy, a pagoda boy, a small trader in the village, a military officer, a commander across the battlefield, a prisoner, a savior, a minister and a deputy prime minister. Despite being assassinated several times, the killers did not succeed.
Through his experience as the Foreign Minister and the youngest Prime Minister in the world, especially the longest-serving Prime Minister, Samdech Techo strives to advocate with superpowers for national sovereignty and the interests of the people based on the principles of equality and equity. Interfering in the internal affairs, at the same time, he strengthened the unity and defense force under a win-win strategy to maintain the hard-won peace.
The book launch would also like to commemorate the 42nd anniversary of the January 7, 1979 Victory Day, the 36th anniversary of Samdech Techo's official inauguration as the Prime Minister on January 14, 1985, and the 22nd anniversary of the end of the war. Completely bring peace to the whole country, celebrate the first drop of oil in Cambodia, the 45th wedding anniversary of January 5, 1976, and also celebrate the 22nd grandson of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
So far, Mr. Chhay Sophal, a veteran journalist, has written more than 10 books in Khmer, English and Chinese. Australian Embassy Provides Kampong Chhnang Health Department Equipment to Prevent and Prevent the Outbreak of Kovid 19
(Kampong Chhnang): Australian Ambassador Mr. Pablo Kang and Prof. Ngy Meng, Director of the National Eye Health Program, on the afternoon of 13 January 2021 visited and brought materials to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 to be distributed to all referral hospitals and health centers in the province.
These items were prepared by the National Eye Health Program under the auspices of the Australian Government through the Fetflo Fund, including: 46,100 masks, 1560 liters of alcohol, 54 thermometers, 505 bottles of hand soap. 15,700 Riels for gloves and 402 masks. In addition, the National Eye Health Program through the Australian Aid also provides additional equipment to hospitals and provincial health departments.
Meanwhile, Dr. Prak Von, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department, stated that so far, hospitals and health centers throughout Kampong Chhnang Province have provided eye examination and treatment services to thousands of people by 2020, despite the world facing 19 cases of Kovid. Anyway.
Mr. Am Sophea, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, expressed his deep gratitude to the Australian Embassy and the Director of the National Eye Health Program for taking the time to bring important assistance today to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department for the people of Kampong Chhnang Province. Used to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 better.
At the same time, he also praised and thanked all the health officials and officials of hospitals and health centers who have worked together to fight and prevent the disease in the past. Do not let any patients die.
