As we all know, the world today considers the whole of Angkor as one of the largest religious centers. In ancient times, Angkor was the capital of the Khmer Empire for more than 600 years, from the 9th to the 15th century.
Most of the temples were built to dedicate to the deities in Hinduism, such as Shiva, Vishnu, etc., making this ancient Khmer capital a great mythical city in the world, such as Angkor Wat was built. In the 12th century to dedicate to Vishnu. This proves that Angkor is one of the largest Hindu temples in the world today.
The huge temple covers an area of 2,520 square meters, is shaped like an eight-story pyramid and has 504 Buddha statues placed in each stupa. It is recorded that this large Buddhist temple originated from the diligence of the Javanese people and the wisdom in arranging large volcanic rocks in the form of a great temple in the traditional Javanese style.
The exterior of each floor, in addition to the fancy carvings on the volcanic rock, also carries images depicting 1,300 beautiful Buddhist stories and legends. If this picture is connected in a single line, it will be up to 4 km long.
Borobudur Temple was inscribed on the UNESCO World Heritage List in 1970, while large-scale renovations were carried out between 1975 and 1982. The world's largest Buddhist temple has become one of Indonesia's most iconic heritage sites. International Analysis: Will North Korea Re-Test ICBMs and Nuclear Weapons?
