(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, this morning, 14 January 2021, chaired a meeting on the current cooperation on the clearance of unexploded ordnance (UXO) in a ship that sank in the river in the district. Srey Santhor, Kampong Cham Province.
The meeting was attended by General Neang Phat, Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense and Chair of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group to Study and Solve Unexploded Ordnance Disposal in Shipwrecks, as well as Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State for relevant ministries and institutions. The National Police Commissioner, the Director General of the relevant General Department under the Ministry of Interior and the leadership of Kampong Cham Province.
Speaking at the ceremony, General Neang Phat said that as the chair of the inter-ministerial working group, he always led a joint working group, including provincial and district authorities, to directly inspect and find solutions to the recovery of sunken warships. In this water surface as soon as possible to end the worries as soon as possible in the coming days.
In addition to the direct inspection at the site of the sinking above, General Neang Phat also encouraged and encouraged the team to work hard to complete this task to complete the mission to restore the sinking ship. This is successful according to what is set and so on.
40 unexploded ordnance clearance technicians from the National Center, 5 sharks (sea sharks) from the Special Forces Command, 10 diving specialists and 10 ship landing technicians.
Up to now, the operation has found the location of the shipwreck and is carrying out sand dredging operations to remove and remove ammunition from the ship, as well as the restoration work to remove the logs and bamboo stumps that are stuck around the ship, which is an obstacle. To the operation to extract the bullets from the ship.
As a result of the operation for the past 3 months, the specialized force has cleared 912 bullets underwater and in the villages around the operation area. The ammunition is stored in a safe location away from the riverfront town and has a 24-hour guard. This operation will have to work hard to find all possible ways to be completely successful in early May, before the rainy season arrives.
The operation to restore the 27-meter-deep submarine was carried out by the UXO Clearance Force of the National Peacekeeping Force Management Center, clearing mines and war remnants, and operating a complex and risk-averse operation. This underwater unexploded ordnance (UXO) clearance operation is carefully divided according to the management's recommendations.
The warship is 8 meters by 40 meters long and weighs more than a hundred tons. It is estimated that there are no less than a hundred tons of munitions, or there may be chemical bombs.
