The land was cut off in exchange for the construction of a three-story light headquarters building and the installation of necessary equipment on nearly 1.6 thousand square meters of land owned by Mr. Lon Hak and Ms. Chhun Chanthy in Srah Chak commune, Daun Penh district.
However, on January 13, 2021, the Royal Government again decided to cancel both the letter on the demarcation of Boeung Ta Mok to Mr. Lon Hak and Ms. Chhun Chanthy and the letter on the construction of the light headquarters building.
Please be reminded that on January 5, 2021, the Royal Government also decided to reclaim about 30 hectares of Ta Mok Lake land for conservation. This 30-hectare land is used for the construction of the Ministry of Rural Development, the National Committee for Disaster Management, the Cambodian Authority for Mine Action and Mine Action, and the Cambodian Human Rights Committee.
