The Microfinance Association of Cambodia and the Association of Banks in Cambodia congratulate HE Chea Chanto on the occasion of being selected as the Outstanding Banker of the Central Bank in 2021 for Asia-Pacific.
The selection of nearly 100-year-old media is based on the successful leadership of the financial sector in Cambodia through the obstacles in 2020.
This newspaper also highlights the efforts of the National Bank of Cambodia to help improve the financial sector through Kovid 19, especially the introduction of a circular on credit restructuring, the promotion of the digital banking system as well as the promotion of the Khmer Riel. The domestic economy is expected to grow 1.9 percent. Mr. Chea Chanto named the Central Bank of the Asia-Pacific Central Bank in 2021 for better management of the banking system
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, has been named the Central Bank of the Asia-Pacific Central Bank in 2021 for better management of the banking system and contribution to growth and economic stability in the affected areas of Cambodia. From the effects of the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
The rating was given by The Banker, a global economic and financial data collection and dissemination agency, after evaluating the achievements of the National Bank of Cambodia in the past.
The Banker highly appreciated that under the leadership of Mr. Chea Chanto, the National Bank of Cambodia has succeeded in managing the banking system well at a time when Cambodia as well as the world is facing a crisis in 2020.
Credit restructuring is allowed up to three times without affecting the credit rating. Additional provisions include: Reducing interest rates and waiving fees. The issuance reduced non-performing loans to a low of 2.5%. Cambodia has also promoted the use of digital banking.
The National Bank of Cambodia officially launched the Bakong system in October 2020, which has contributed to improving the financial environment in Cambodia, as many private companies still pay their employees in cash.
The Bakong system is built using blockchain technology and can process payments in both KHR and USD via mobile phone, allowing users to scan codes or enter the recipient's phone number. The Bakong system has about 20 member banks.
On the other hand, the national currency is also strongly encouraged to promote sustainable growth and develop an efficient banking system, and in particular reduce the reliance on the US dollar. Payments of less than US $ 100 are now made in riel, while the use of smaller US dollar denominations has been steadily declining.
