WASHINGTON: Democrat-controlled US House of Representatives is preparing to prosecute and oust outgoing President Donald Trump for a second term just over a year after Trump was assassinated. He resigned in 2019 over a scandal with Ukraine.
The US Constitution authorizes the US House of Representatives to proceed with the removal of a president without specifying how many times it can be. Given the current political situation in the United States, Donald Trump is widely expected to become the first president in history to be twice indicted by the House of Representatives.
However, the US Senate still has another authority: to vote by a simple majority (50 plus 1) to disqualify or ban Trump from running for president forever, and this is what the party Democracy wants the most.
