(Phnom Penh): Vital and Mey Cheat co-organized a charity event "Sharing to provide warmth for the 5th time" on the morning of January 13, 2021 at Pracha Barmey Park in Chroy Changvar Sangkat to distribute gifts of food, medicine Sangkho and some funds also provide haircuts for Mr. Cyclo, the elderly and nearly 300 poor people in Phnom Penh.
The charity event was held in the presence of Ms. Chheng Sokuntheavy, General Director of Vital Drinking Water and Noodle Products, with the participation of the company's management, people, youth, volunteers and many working groups.
This is the fifth time that Vital and Mey Cheat Drinking Water Company has held this event in order to expand the culture of sharing in the principles of love, tolerance and sincere respect. In addition, the charity program also shares the hardships and warmth of the needy, especially in the stressful context of the global Kovid 19 pandemic.
On this significant occasion, the CEO of the company said, "Autumn has arrived, it is very difficult for the elderly, uncles, aunts, brothers and sisters who have a poor life. "Some of them do not have proper shelter, some do not have enough equipment and some can not afford to buy food and medicine."
"For this reason, Vital and Mi Cheat continue to organize this event, and the company hopes to be able to share some of the difficulties and provide warmth to the grandparents, uncles and aunts who have difficulties," she said. .
It should be noted that the gifts that the company distributed today include rice, drinking water, vital noodles and kits, including blankets, scarves, medicine and some money. The elderly and the majority of the participants are subsistence farmers, such as cyclo drivers, brooms, sharpeners, knives, scales, and the disabled.
Vital & Mi Cheat is a local company that has received strong support from the Cambodian people for its philanthropic and social work for more than 10 years. Both companies also called on the public, young people of modern times to participate in charitable activities and society more broadly for the sake of our society. Ratanakkiri Provincial Governor Urges Students to Study Hard to Be Good Students and to Stay Away from Social Mischief
(Ratanakkiri): Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, instructed all students to study hard to be good children, good students, good citizens, good friends and to stay away from other evils that cause insecurity to society.
Mr. Thong Savun made this remark on the morning of January 13, 2021 on the occasion of presiding over the opening ceremony of the new school year 2020-2021 at Bou Thong O'Chum High School in O'Chum District, Ratanakkiri Province, with the participation of the Force Commander. Three types of weapons, Mr. President - Deputy Director of relevant departments, education staff and about 300 students.
Mr. Thong Savun said that the opening of the new school year took place at a time when Cambodia was working together to fight Kovid-19. Therefore, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has developed a new way of life in educational institutions in accordance with the SOP standards for school operations in the context of Kovid-19 and strengthen the implementation of measures to prevent and prevent Kovid-19.
At the same time, Mr. Thong Savun also asked teachers to make more efforts by providing educational services to students equally without discrimination.
On this occasion, Mr. Thong Savun also donated 1 million Riels and distributed certificates of appreciation to 6 teachers and 5 outstanding students.
