(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Cults and Religions has called on the leaders of the Department of Cults and Religions, the leaders of the temples and the Cambodian Buddhists to decorate and participate in the celebration of Meak Bochea with adherence to the spirit of prevention of communicable diseases. 19.
This year's Meak Bochea Festival will be held for two days on Thursday, January 15, and January 1, 2021. Meak Bochea is one of the major festivals in Buddhism that Buddhist countries around the world always celebrate.
Every year, Cambodian Buddhists celebrate this Meak Bochea festival in all pagodas throughout the country, considering it as the most precious merit.
The Ministry of Cults and Religions has instructed all provincial and municipal departments of cults and religions to assign pagodas to organize Meak Bochea ceremonies in accordance with national customs and traditions, and to select any pagoda to officially celebrate Meak Bochea.
The Ministry also called on philanthropists, Buddhists and people to participate in the fulfillment of merits in a transparent manner for the benefit of preserving the national identity, traditional Buddhism and approving their respective monks.
