2020 Volunteer lawyers for the Human Rights Committee perform their duties efficiently and quickly for the poor
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, stated that by 2020, the volunteer lawyers of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee have fulfilled their duties effectively and quickly to Poor people who can not afford to rely on private lawyers for free.
With regard to human rights work, Mr. Keo Remy pointed out that the Human Rights Committee has sent a team of volunteer lawyers to defend Pich Soneth, who was sentenced by the court to 166 years in prison. 8 cases. The acquittal of the eight charges leaves the woman with only two cases to serve, serving a 19-year sentence.
The chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee said that so far three young children have been imprisoned by their mothers and have been brought in to stay with the Cambodian Child Development Organization for education. Like other children who can make their lives brighter in the future.
With this successful achievement of providing free legal assistance, Mr. Keo Remy encouraged the lawyers and lawyers of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee to continue their efforts to fulfill this task. For the benefit of the whole society, including the maintenance of justice in the society.
In addition, the Cambodian Human Rights Committee (CCHR) has decided to provide a free defense lawyer to a female detainee with a small child at Correctional Center 2 (M2), where a 5-month-old baby girl died at the hospital. Severe pneumonia.
Mr. Keo Remy stated that with the support of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the working group of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee participated in solving the case of torture of prisoners in Banteay Meanchey province to the point of loss of life and bring the perpetrators to justice. Legal and other cases are well handled based on the principles of law and human rights.
