The victim, who was nominated by a woman as a team of poor lawyers and relatives of the leaders to swindle money in Rattanak Mondul district, Battambang province, came to court to explain the story.
(Battambang): Two women living in O'Lun village, Plou Meas commune, Rattanak Mondul district, Battambang province, who were defrauded of nearly $ 4,000 by a woman named Khin Sivan, appeared in the morning of January 12, 2021 in front of a representative. The prosecutor accompanied the provincial court on behalf of the plaintiffs to describe the above story.
The women said they were questioned by court officials for about half an hour in connection with the case. After questioning, court officials said they would seek legal redress and seek justice for the two.
It should be noted that the two women were cheated of a woman for thousands of dollars by relying on to help run and defend their case because she set herself up as a grassroots team as a lawyer for the poor. And a relative of the leadership in the judiciary.
After defrauding them of nearly $ 4,000, the victims sought justice by filing a complaint with the Battambang Provincial Court and seeking the intervention of a group of government volunteer lawyers to help them settle the case. This is really hard to find through farm work in their village.
The woman who was accused of swindling the money was told by the victim that her name was Khin Sivorn, about 58 years old, and she lived in Sre Saang village, Sre Saang commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
The victims, Moul Saudy and Chheng Lang, stated in their complaint that Khin Sivan claimed that she was able to defend and run the case in the Battambang Provincial Court because she knew the court. At all levels, they lost trust and sent money to this woman in a row until almost $ 4,000 without repaying.
(Tbong Khmum): Dr. Cheam Chansophoan said that as a quality bamboo vine full of knowledge, all students must pay attention and continue to study hard to acquire knowledge from teachers for themselves, their families and The whole society.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, said this while presiding over the opening ceremony of the new school year 2020-2021 on January 12, 2021 at Hun Sen Tuol Sophy Secondary School in Tuol Sophy Commune, Ou Raing Ov District, Tbong Khmum Province.
Dr. Cheam Chansophoan stated that young people in the peace era have all kinds of opportunities to study and choose their favorite skills. With this great opportunity, I would like to ask all of you to work hard to learn how to become a successor to lead a country full of ability, with both knowledge and skills, to continue to develop the country to grow even more under one roof. Peace that Samdech Techo Hun Sen strives for.
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, has decided to establish the first Public Works and Transport Skills Training Institute in Cambodia to increase human resources on public works and transportation skills, focusing on road construction and road skills training. Bridges.
The first Public Works and Transport Training Institute in Cambodia is called "Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport". Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport has partnered with the Institute of Technology of Cambodia (ITC) to strengthen the quality of training in public works and transportation.
The signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding to strengthen cooperation between the two institutes was held on Tuesday afternoon, January 12, 2021. The signing ceremony was presided over by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, and Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports.
Dr. Hang Chuon Naron stated that education and training of human resources is the highest priority and priority given by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. However, for Cambodia until now, Cambodia does not have any training institutes on public works and transportation.
On behalf of the Minister of Education, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron was pleased to see the initiative of the Institute for Training in Public Works and Transport.
The Minister of Education underlined, "I commend the Senior Minister for his vision in training human resources for public works and transport. "This is the first time we have an institute for technical training in public works and transportation."
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol recalled the many works that Khmer ancestors built during the Angkorian period, such as temples and bridges that are thousands of years old in Siem Reap. But why can't Cambodians today build bridges across the Mekong, Bassac, and Tonle Sap rivers?
According to Mr. Sun Chanthol, he was upset that he could not see Cambodian children capable of building a bridge across the river, so he tried to establish this institute.
Mr. Sun Chanthol also mentioned that currently, due to the lack of technical experts, every time a road or bridge is built, foreigners are often hired to build it. Therefore, this institute will contribute to training Cambodian children in building roads and bridges without relying on foreign experts.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also expressed strong hope and confidence that the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport and the Institute of Technology of Cambodia will work together to provide high quality training to Cambodian students on public works and transportation.
Both Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and Dr. Hang Chuon Naron shared the same hope that graduates of the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport will be able to build bridges across the Mekong, Tonle Sap and Tonle Bassac rivers. Proud for Cambodian children.
Dr. Um Romney, Director of the Institute of Technology, said that the first step of training at the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport, about 200 students will be selected from the Institute of Technology of Cambodia for five years.
Separately, human resources on training will be taken from Techno School, Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport and the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. In addition, experiments will be conducted at both educational institutions as well as internships at various construction sites of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
At the signing ceremony of the training cooperation between the Institute of Public Works and Transport and the Institute of Technology of Cambodia, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol announced his full support for both institutes in terms of spirit and needs.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also announced the provision of job opportunities in the construction of roads and bridges to students graduating from Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport.
Officials demolish 1358 old car number plates in Svay Rieng after new ownership
(Svay Rieng): The old number plates that people bought one after another and requested to transfer ownership of the car in accordance with the law, 1358 plates were destroyed. This is according to Mr. Prum Pho, Director of the Transportation Office of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Svay Rieng Province, said this morning, January 12, 2021.
The demolition of the old license plates took place inside the Svay Rieng Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, with the participation of Mr. Nuon Ly Hourn, Director of the Department and Deputy Director of the Department, Director of the Office and officials involved in various responsibilities. Another picture, too.
He said that the Department of Public Works and Transport of Svay Rieng Province has demolished the old license plates left over from the people's request, and the ownership has been transferred in accordance with the law and has been completed since receiving the instructions from the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. On the transfer of ownership of vehicles that can not find the original owner was issued on March 12, 2020.
Mr. Prum Pho continued that today, people who have not yet transferred their car ownership are still working every day at the Svay Rieng Provincial Public Works Department, and our professional officers have tried to facilitate the documents to facilitate the transfer of ownership. .
Please note that the transfer of ownership of the vehicle that can not find the original owner of the people who are occupying the vehicle to buy and sell the original owner can not be found to apply for the transfer of vehicle ownership. Required documents: The application for transfer of ownership of the vehicle must be fingerprinted by the applicant and stamped with a valid Cal (body or license plate) from the vehicle, vehicle identification card (original) and vehicle identification plate.
On December 30, 2020, Mr. Sam Rainsy was sentenced to two more years in prison in the case of "incitement to commit a crime," which he posted on Facebook accusing Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister. Ministry of Interior. In addition to the two-year prison sentence, the court also ordered Sam Rainsy to pay 2 billion riels in damages and damages to the plaintiffs.
In addition, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court also ordered the authorities to arrest Mr. Sam Rainsy and punish him according to the law, while the prisoner has been fleeing abroad.
However, at the time of announcing the verdict, the court also gave one month for the parties to file a legal appeal to the Court of Appeal.
In addition to the two years in prison in the above case, on December 30, 2020, the court also sentenced Sam Rainsy to another two years in prison, for inciting people not to pay bank debts.
Convict Sam Rainsy has a case tomorrow in Cambodia, including a final verdict and some proceedings. At the same time, in June 2020, he was also convicted by the Paris Criminal Court of France on charges of "public defamation of a person" in a lawsuit filed by Commissioner General Divis. Deputy National Police, the son of Hok Lundy.
King issues royal decree setting conditions, procedures and procedures for commutation and pardon of prisoners in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree on the Mitigation and Pardoning of Prisoners in Cambodia.
This Royal Decree aims to determine the rituals, conditions, procedures and procedures for commutation and pardon of prisoners for the purpose of reintegrating them into society or for humanitarian purposes.
This Royal Decree also covers the commutation of sentences and pardons for all prisoners convicted by the Judgment or Final Judgment of the Courts of Cambodia and for convicts sentenced to imprisonment by the jurisdiction of a foreign state. Sent to serve his sentence in Cambodia based on an agreement between the Kingdom of Cambodia and a foreign state.
According to this Royal Decree, every year, there are 5 ceremonies that can request pardon and pardon for prisoners, including:
1: Victory Day on the genocidal regime 2: National New Year 3: Vesak festival 4: National Independence Day 5: Water Festival, floating lanterns and worshiping the moon Ok Ambok.
