Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi tells all private security agencies that upon arresting the perpetrators, they must immediately report to the local police, which prohibits the use of violence.
(Phnom Penh): Lieutenant General E Sok Khi, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, on January 12, 2021, told all private security agencies that when any perpetrator is caught, he must immediately report it to the police. The nearest special administrative police station and the use of violence is strictly prohibited.
At the Closing Ceremony of the 30th Private Security Agency Training Course organized by the Department of Private Security Management, Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi instructed all private security agencies that in addition to reporting upon the arrest of perpetrators, private security agencies There is also a role to participate in maintaining and protecting the scene to facilitate the police force to carry out research work.
The Deputy Chief of the National Police also reminded all security agents that when performing their duties, they must wear the uniforms of the company or enterprise that they have designated, especially the clear badges as well as the equipment that must be worn on them. And especially to be an example to the people.
In addition, Lt. Gen. Ey Sok Khi instructed the private security agents who have been trained for the past two days to use the knowledge gained to perform their duties properly and avoid committing wrongdoing and Contrary to the rules set.
In addition, Lt. Gen. E Sok Khi emphasized that private security agencies must contribute to maintaining security and social order, especially to jointly implement the policy of the Royal Government, which has issued a policy of safe villages and communes to prevent crime that occurs at the local level. .
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department, said that the 30th Private Security Agency Training Course will be held for two days from 11 to 12 January 2021.
The Director of the Department said that this training course aims to meet the needs of capacity building to become a private security agent who has the skills and qualifications to participate in the activities to maintain and protect security, safety, order and security. Live the life of the people as well as improve the policy of safe villages and communes.
Minister of Commerce Continues Meeting to Examine Preparations for the 1st Asia-Europe Economic and Business Forum
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the meeting, on January 12, 2021, convened another meeting to review the progress of the work of the Secretariat Committee and the working group on the forum "Economy and Asia-Europe Business ”for the first time to be held in Cambodia.
During the meeting, the Minister of Commerce highlighted that the Asia-Europe Economic and Business Forum is one of the seven accompanying forums of the Asia-Europe Meeting (ASEM).
In addition, the meeting also contributes to the development of Cambodia's human resources in both the public and private sectors and the promotion of people-to-people exchanges in a context where Asia-Europe is increasingly interconnected. ⁇.
On the other hand, currently in the midst of an epidemic, COVID-19 must consider safety equipment to prepare for this important forum, as well as the number of guests attending the meeting, safety gaps, alcohol or hand gel and temperature sensors. In accordance with the measures of the Ministry of Health. In particular, be prepared for a doctor to come to the rescue when something goes wrong.
Minister Pan Sosak expressed his appreciation and appreciation for the efforts of the officials in the Secretariat Committee, as well as the working group and representatives from the Council for the Development of Cambodia who have spent many months preparing Organize this forum to be successful and fruitful in the future. APSARA Authority continues to improve the area in front of the Terrace of the Elephants to facilitate visitors and protect ancient buildings
(Siem Reap): After receiving the approval of ICC-Angkor Adhoc Experts, APSARA Authority has continued the project to improve the area in front of the Terrace of the Elephants with a sidewalk and drainage system and planting grass. Beautiful greenery to enhance the value of the entire Angkor Thom complex.
According to historical documents, in 1909, the front of the Terrace of the Elephants had no road signs for vehicles. In 1912, there was a road parallel to the Sour Prat temple. The road next to the Terrace of the Elephants was only built in 1928.
The location to be completely improved is from the northern corner of Bayon Temple to the front of the Leper King pavilion. The team will close the site in stages so as not to disturb the travel of residents and tourists, and this work is scheduled to be completed in six months. Mr. Sun Chanthol: Educated but not willing to serve society well (Video inside)
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, reminded his officials that serving the society without the means and knowledge, but lacking high will, can not serve the society well.
At the signing ceremony of the training cooperation between Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport and the Institute of Technology of Cambodia for training on public works and transportation on January 12, 2021, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that he can Provide materials and seek to impart knowledge to his officials, but he can not give them the will to serve the motherland.
Mr. Sun Chanthol said that the will is an important element in serving the society better. In this regard, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister who is dominating the national service in the role of manager and leader of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, called on his officials to be highly willing to serve the motherland to make the nation prosperous and Glorious.
Mr. Sun Chanthol told his officials, "We can not give the will, only the suggestion that we all have a high will to serve our motherland. The will is very important, there is knowledge and means, but if we do not have a high will to build a nation, we can not do. Thus, we must have the highest will to serve our motherland.
With the establishment of the first Public Works and Transport Training Institute in Cambodia, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol urged the Techo Sen Institute of Public Works and Transport to cooperate with the Institute of Technology of Cambodia to better train Cambodian students.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment, on January 12, 2021, confirmed that in the whole year 2020, 605 natural resource crime cases were sent to court. In 2020, there were 857 transferee fines for offenders and 2,946 offenses for education and contracting.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment said, "In 2020, 605 cases of natural resource crimes were sent to court, and by 2020, there will be 857 transferee fines for offenders. There are 2946 cases of education and contracting. ”
According to the Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment, most of the crimes cracked down on were logging, encroachment, illegal occupation of forest land, hunting and trapping.
Mr. Net Pheaktra said: "The increase in crime suppression and prevention shows the more effective implementation of the law and shows the efforts of community park rangers, protected areas and stakeholders without fear of exhaustion." "Forest and biodiversity protection patrol."
Mr. Neth Pheaktra added that in the patrol and crime suppression operation in 2020, the rangers of the Ministry of Environment confiscated 4,004 chainsaws, an increase of about 500 chambers in 2019. There are 3,494 units.
