(Pursat): Workers at the Tai Ezi Garment Factory in Krakor district erupted in protest demanding two working conditions and benefits, after mediation by the Pursat provincial governor, they accepted the settlement and dispersed the strike to their homes.
The incident happened at 12:20 pm on January 12, 2021 at the Tai Yi Garment Factory in Tonsay Koul village, Anlong Thnout commune, Krakor district, Pursat province.
According to Brigadier General Pen Tung, Deputy Commissioner for Security Planning, at the time of the incident, more than 5,000 garment factory workers had gone on strike demanding two working conditions and benefits, including: 1- Seniority allowance, 2- Annual leave allowance.
Brigadier General said that immediately after the explosion, a group of workers gathered on National Road 5 in front of the factory, causing traffic jams from 1:30 pm to 2:30 pm. Same year.
Brigadier General Deputy Commissioner for Security Planning added that with the attention of Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Provincial Board of Governors to coordinate and resolve the conditions and benefits demanded by the workers. That.
After the settlement, the provincial governor coordinated with the factory owner to make an urgent settlement on January 15, 2021 on the first condition, "seniority bonus", to be paid to all workers as required. . As for the second condition, "annual leave allowance", you should postpone and check the possibility with the relevant departmental team.
