Despite the Kovid 19 crisis, the General Department of Taxation is still able to collect $ 2.889 billion in revenue for the national budget, an increase of 3.73% by 2020
(Phnom Penh): On January 11, 2021, the General Department of Taxation held a meeting to review the results of tax collection for December and 2020, as well as the main work results achieved in 2020 and the main measures for implementation. Continuing in 2021 of the General Department of Taxation under the chairmanship of Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance.
Mr. Kong Vibol stated that this proud result is inseparable from the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, especially the full and effective management of the situation of Kovid-19 in 2020. In the past and under the wise guidance and sharp planning of the General Secretary, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance.
The main achievements in 2020, which the General Department of Taxation has achieved are as follows: Revenues to meet the growth of the national economy and address the challenges raised by the private sector.
* Reformed the management of tax debt collection through the introduction of the Prakas on the management of tax debt to strengthen the efficiency of tax collection management, solve challenges, provide clarity and accuracy in recording, tracking tax credits and easy taxpayers. Monitor and implement fiscal obligations.
* Implemented the online tax filing management system (E-Filing) in conjunction with the electronic tax payment function and the banking system to strengthen the efficiency, transparency and accuracy of tax filing management, as well as To make it easier for taxpayers by reducing the time and challenges of completing tax returns and tax payments.
* Participated in the preparation and implementation of the business registration mechanism through the Information Technology (IT Platform) and strengthened the tax registration mechanism through the Prakas on tax registration and updating taxpayer information.
* Participated in the preparation and implementation of Inter-Ministerial Prakas No. 264 of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport on Procedures and Procedures for the Transfer of Vehicle Ownership between the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Ministry of Economy and Finance, which provides a stamp duty payment service mechanism. On the transfer of vehicle ownership by providing additional options, citizens can apply and pay taxes online.
* Introduced to test the data sharing automation system between the General Department of Taxation and the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia * Participated in the preparation and implementation of the Royal Government's measures related to taxation to manage the impact on key sectors of the economy in The context of the Kovid-19 crisis.
* Continued to modernize information technology management systems in order to strengthen the efficiency and effectiveness of taxpayer services. By 2020, 18 systems have been developed, 4 programs have been updated, and 23 systems and programs have been updated since 2014. 2020 There are a total of 86 systems and programs developed.
* Contributed to the successful and effective implementation of the 2020 plan within the framework of the 2019-2023 revenue collection strategy and the Royal Government's public financial management reform program.
* In the wake of the global economic situation as well as the Cambodian economy is not yet certain, especially those severely affected by the spread of Kovid 19, implemented the management of revenue collection in excess and exceeding the financial plan for 2020 and Participated in the preparation of the Financial Law for the management of 2021.
* Continue to push for the completion of updating the tax law in response to the growth of the national economy, ensure the clarity, efficiency, effectiveness, legitimacy and consistency of tax revenue management.
* Prepare to implement the tax revenue management mechanism in the beer production sector by adjusting the tax revenue management management using modern automated equipment.
* Continue to strengthen the management of tax revenue collection in potential sectors to ensure transparency and competitiveness, including the telecommunications sector, the beer and beverage sector, the tobacco and tobacco sector.
* Continue to modernize the tax debt management system, which will record and maintain a clear tax debt history, have accurate tax debt risk analysis and provide high capacity for the tax administration to manage tax debt collection.
* Ready to launch a mobile property tax payment application that will make it easier for taxpayers to check their property information and pay property taxes on their mobile phones.
* Prepare to introduce online tax payment for all types of means of transportation and vehicles, which will make it easier for taxpayers to pay taxes online, and the tax administration will send tax receipts to your home. Tax at once.
* Continue to modernize information technology systems and applications through the development and updating of new systems and applications.
For 2021, the Deputy Prime Minister supported the measures taken by the General Department of Taxation and made the following key recommendations:
* Carefully review and study the possibility of other potential revenue collection, taking into account both fiscal and non-fiscal revenue aspects to ensure full fiscal compliance and revenue collection. Revenues from e-commerce, new potential oil, mining and other potential sectors.
* Revise regulations to define small and medium enterprises and promote the promotion of small and medium enterprises into the system in order to promote growth and create economic opportunities.
Strengthen tax registration and promote the fulfillment of fiscal obligations for enterprises in the casino sector to ensure maximum tax transparency and tax revenue management.
* Continue to implement the institutional reform of the tax administration-information technology system, ensuring user-friendliness for taxpayers and officials, as well as strengthening tax compliance to promote efficiency and interconnection in the collection management mission. Tax revenue.
* Continue to carefully implement the Royal Government's revenue collection strategy 2019-2023.
Strengthen and pay attention to the audit in accordance with the content of Prakas No. 270 MEF.PrK dated 13 March 2019 on Tax Audit, which is a scale to measure the compliance of the enterprise and avoid causing difficulties for taxpayers.
* Continue to promote and mainstream the culture of paying taxes, strengthen the dissemination and implementation of new tax-related regulations to tax enforcement officials and the public to explain and solve the difficulties and questions of the people.
* Continue to cooperate and consult with relevant sectors to receive input into the study, prepare and improve the necessary relevant regulations.
