General Department of Taxation announces to start inspecting tax declaration on means of transportation from February 1 onwards
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Taxation on January 11, 2021 issued a notification on the inspection of tax declaration on means of transportation and all types of vehicles for the year 2020 from February 1, 2021. Coming soon.
The General Department states that in case the vehicle owner fails to declare the tax on means of transportation and all kinds of vehicles for the year 2020, please hurry to declare the tax and pay the fine according to the law in force.
According to the General Department of Taxation, "Capital-Provincial Joint Working Group led by tax officials in cooperation with sub-national competent authorities will inspect the tax declaration on all means of transportation and vehicles for 2020 at the target. Some on the main roads of the capital-province from February 1, 2021 onwards.
Please be informed that the date for collecting tax on means of transportation and all types of vehicles in 2020 was completed on November 30, 2020. Siem Reap Governor Urges Teachers and Students to Continue Self-Defense and Implement Royal Government Measures Against Kovid 19 in the New School Year
(Siem Reap): Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, participated in the opening of the new school year (2020-2021) as a symbol for the whole of Siem Reap Province, which was held at 10 January 1979 High School. The event was attended by hundreds of government officials, department heads, departments, institutions, teachers, students, and the event was on a new path in education by taking measures to prevent Kovid-19 disease.
He stated that in the school year 2019-2020, the results of the lower secondary school diploma exam, a total of more than 13,000 students and high school students, more than 9,000 students are set to pass 100% without any lecture.
The provincial governor also urged teachers and students to continue to protect themselves and follow the government's measures to fight Kovid 19 in the new school year.
"I would like to remind and call on teachers, guardians, students, nieces and nephews to participate in the fight against the spread of Kovid 19 by cleaning regularly by washing hands with soap or alcohol and Wear the right mask for our health, our school and our society.
He also said that under the shadow of peace, Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid the highest attention in the field of education and provided school buildings everywhere for the children to study and pay attention to improve health and hygiene. And measures to prevent Kovid-19 to prevent the entry into the school must ensure safety, health, study, maintain a safety gap of 1.5 meters and food safety.
Meanwhile, Siem Reap is currently planning to build 38 roads in Siem Reap under the Prime Minister's funding for the development of the city's road infrastructure during the Kovid-19 crisis, as well as the Siem Reap River Development Project. Also.
He also asked all students to be very careful while the province is building 38 roads that affect the traffic of people and students to avoid traffic accidents. He instructed the children to study hard to become good children, good students, good citizens and to stay away from drugs, to obey traffic laws and to participate in social work.
On that occasion, the provincial governor also distributed certificates of appreciation and prizes to students of all grades who excelled and ranked first and second. Spokesman for the General Commission: On January 11, 2021, another 903 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson, within 11 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to January 11, 2021, the traffic police across the country inspected and A total of 9,889 vehicles were fined, including 7,354 motorcycles and 2,535 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kimkhoeun said that for the past 11 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for violating vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law in the past, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
