(Siem Reap): Citizens, government officials, traders, tourists and the general public living and visiting the historic tourist city of Siem Reap-Angkor have expressed support for the implementation of measures against gangsters riding motorcycles equipped with loudspeakers and children. Hippos ride motorcycles at excessive speeds of the road traffic laws, which disrupt and affect the lives and entertainment of citizens and tourists.
The announcement of support for this action came after on January 8, 2021, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, ordered the police force to cooperate with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to investigate and identify the big motorbikes. Make noise to the people.
Residents of Siem Reap City stated that they hope and believe that the authorities in Siem Reap will take the strictest and most effective action against gangsters in accordance with the words of Samdech Krala Hom to implement the policy of safe villages and communes. .
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also stressed that the case of big motorbikes causing noise must be eliminated and must not continue in society. General knowledge: When did Cambodia first appear on the world map?
(Phnom Penh): Some ancient maps have been found to date from 16500 BC until the 6th century BC, when the ancient Greeks began to draw the first world map on paper. Later, the world map was also revised until now, but do you know when Cambodia was first included in the world map?
During the European colonial period, especially the older colonies such as Portugal, Spain, the Netherlands, etc., they first arrived in Southeast Asia, in 1498 AD, Portuguese troops invaded the Indian state of Goa and continued to arrive. Southeast Asia in 1511 AD to conquer Malacca.
During the late 15th and 16th centuries, Cambodia was between the late Chaktomuk and early Longvek periods, which were in turmoil due to war with each other and war with the Siamese in Ayutthaya.
Historians record that in 1515, King Chan Reach (1515-1566) ordered 150 Canon cannons and 2,000 special artifacts, as well as some modern weapons to fight. Army of King Srey Chetha - King Kan. It was not until 1525 AD that King Chan Reachea defeated King Srey Chetha and moved the capital to Longvek, now in Longvek commune, Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province.
At the beginning of the Longvek period, Cambodia began to strengthen close ties with the Portuguese and continued to have relations with other European colonies such as the Netherlands, France and so on.
