Interior Ministry Spokesman: 67 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses
(Phnom Penh): At least 67 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on January 11, 2021 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News this morning, January 12.
General Khieu Sopheak added that of the 67 suspects, 25 were arrested in 13 criminal cases and 42 were arrested in 14 drug cases.
At the same time, he called on all citizens to implement the slogan "3 do not 1 report", which means "do not be involved, do not intervene, do not exempt in various crimes and help report drug offenses and other crimes. US Secretary of Homeland Security resigns after criticizing Tram over riots at the Capitol
According to a letter sent to Homeland Security staff member Chad Wolf, who is in charge of providing security for Joe Biden's inauguration, he will step down at midnight on Monday. This makes him the third person to walk out of the Donald Trump administration after pro-presidential insurgents stormed the House of Representatives last week.
In the same letter, Wolf said he intended to remain in office until after Biden was sworn in. However, he was forced to resign due to recent events, including a court ruling that he was not legitimate to sit as Minister of Homeland Security.
