(Phnom Penh): Brigadier General Eng Hee, spokesman for the National Gendarmerie on January 11, 2021, confirmed that the man who pulled out a gun from a young man in a traffic accident around Phsar Thmei in Phsar Thmei First, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, at 4:30 AM on January 10, 2021, was not a military police officer. This is according to the explanation letter of the spokesperson of the Royal Gendarmerie, which was received by Fresh News.
(Phnom Penh): It has been two years since the European Union imposed tariffs on Cambodia's rice exports. Around the tax under the pretext that to help its farmers, the Cambodian Rice Federation still said that it is unfair and did not help the European farmers themselves.
Oknha Song Saran, president of the Cambodian Rice Federation, said that the imposition of tariffs on Cambodian rice has resulted in Cambodia losing about 6-70,000 tonnes of white rice exports, and the countries that have replaced it are India and Vietnam.
According to the president of the Cambodian Rice Federation, Cambodia has been hit hard by white rice, falling by about 70,000 tonnes in the year the EU decided to impose tariffs. In particular, fragrant rice is still standing, with an annual export of about 200,000 tons.
Duke Song Saran said that the European Union should not continue to harm small countries, and that it is unfair for small countries, and he believes that in 2022, the European Union will reconsider whether the 2019 decision on Cambodia On taxation.
Oknha Song Saran added that Cambodia continues to explain to the European Union that Cambodia is a clean country and that the imposition of tariffs on Cambodian rice is not as beneficial as the EU wants.
