Microfinance Association of Cambodia: As of January 2021, more than 280,000 clients received $ 1,382 million in credit restructuring
Mr. Kaing Tong Ngy said, “As of January 3, 2021, members of the Cambodian Microfinance Association, which has received deposits from 6 microfinance institutions, 69 non-deposit microfinance institutions, financial leasing companies. "Eleven objects, 19 rural credit institutions and four banks have refinanced US $ 1,382 million in loans to 285,234 families out of 303 593 applicants."
He said loan refinancing requests had dropped to a steady level in the last four months, with more than a thousand applications per week.
Kea Boran, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Microfinance Association, has stated that credit restructuring has helped many clients, especially those affected by Kovid 19, as businesses and employees in some sectors have suffered. Impact on their income, so if the loan is not reorganized, the customer will face the consequences of repaying the original contract.
He said the credit restructuring provided customers with the opportunity to repay the new rate and when the situation returned to normal, they would be able to repay the original contract.
He said that the reorganization of credit also helps people to have some cash to expand their business and business.
Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong continues to help children with disabilities and poor people without stopping
In fact, a three-story building for deaf children with a height of 12 rooms, which the Hor Namhong-Borei Hor Foundation contributed to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. Hopefully, this new building and electronic equipment will facilitate the study and accommodation of all students in Kampong Cham Special Education High School.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong also confirmed the reasons for the continued success in helping children with disabilities, young people, young women and the poor of the "Hor Namhong-Borei Hor" Foundation, he set a good example by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, both Samdech always pay attention to help the difficulties of the disabled and the poor.
"Therefore, I follow the noble example of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who always helps the poor and needy all the time. I follow the noble and noble path of Samdech Techo."
It should be noted that the Hor Namhong-Borei Hor Foundation was established in January 2019 and to date has supported 305 orphans, the mentally retarded and the mentally ill, as well as 305 blind and deaf children. Phnom Penh National Infant and Child Borey and Special Education High School in Kampong Cham Province with a financial support of 960,000,000 Riels per year.
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, on January 11, 2021, ordered the police force of 14 districts in Phnom Penh to suspend the seizure of motorbikes with loud cement pipes. Causing temporary disturbance to the people.
It should be informed that Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, this morning, January 08, 2021, ordered the special police force in Phnom Penh to cooperate with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to investigate and identify the big motorbikes that caused the accident. Noise to the people.
The order of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng came after Samdech observed that there were cases of some gangsters riding big motorbikes, processing the cement pipes with the wrong technical characteristics of the original format, and there was a loud noise, disturbing the people, especially Samdech himself. Also disturbed by the sound of the cement pipe.
The new order of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng was made during the chairmanship of the inter-ministerial meeting to adjust the qualifications of the policy of safe villages and communes on the morning of January 08, 2021. The meeting was held at the Ministry of Interior with the participation of the Minister, the Secretary of State, the Under Secretary of State, the relevant ministries and the heads of many other institutions.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng noted that in the past, these big motorbike riders were riding fast and some of them disturbed the local people and sometimes disturbed the sleep of the leaders, so the police officers had to monitor and cooperate. With the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to identify and address all these motorcyclists.
