* Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Success in the fight against Kovid 19 does not depend on developed countries or strong health systems, it is important to manage and manage the situation, security, order and prevention of noise are hot topics. In the meeting of Phnom Penh Unity Command
(Phnom Penh): The maintenance of security and public order for the people in Phnom Penh and the prevention of noise in public places were discussed at the meeting of Phnom Penh Unity Command on the morning of January 11. This year 2012, in the presence of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor and Chairman of the Phnom Penh Unity Command.
The meeting was also attended by Lt. Gen. Thet, Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, and was attended by 14 district governors and other departments under the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that the issue of security and public order is an issue that the Phnom Penh Municipal Authority, the 14 Khan authorities and the two types of armed forces must pay attention to regularly to prevent any crime from gaining trust. Trust by the people in Phnom Penh.
Mr. Khuong Sreng urged the 14 district authorities to continue to visit the Boreys in Phnom Penh as a force and if there is a problem that can be solved immediately to the people and if the problem can not be reported. Phnom Penh level so that the capital level can continue to solve for the people.
Regarding the big motorbikes that caused noise as well as the motorbikes that processed the cement to disturb the people, Mr. Khuong Sreng confirmed that to prevent the noise motorbikes, the authorities as well as the competent force arrested 60 motorbikes. .
The Governor of Phnom Penh urged the relevant departments, especially the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh and the Department of Environment of Phnom Penh, to visit the detained places this afternoon to inspect the technical characteristics and environmental impact. Will be returned to the owner of the motorcycle. However, he confirmed that the motorcycle with the wrong speakers is still kept waiting for instructions from the Ministry of Interior.
Lt. Gen. Thet stated that in Phnom Penh, there is better security and order, but nevertheless, we still have some challenges that we must continue to pay attention to: the drug problem that we all Be together to prevent.
He also stated that most of the crimes that occurred, most of the perpetrators were drug addicts. Some Boreys still have the crime of stealing and looting houses, which we, the competent forces, must continue to pay attention to these crimes.
In addition, within a month or two, the crime started by the gang also resurfaced, with the group rallied with swords and knives, causing anarchy and fighting. We have also cracked down on this case. However, as a force must strive to prevent the warmth of the people in Phnom Penh.
