Campaign "Defend now, do not wait for tomorrow" is launched with the opening of the new school year
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, with the support of UNICEF, has announced the implementation of the "Defend yourself now, do not wait for tomorrow" campaign with the opening of the new school year 2020-2021, which is in the context of harassment and intimidation. By Kovid 19.
The campaign aims to encourage Cambodian children to return to school and continue to adopt safe behaviors to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 as the new school year begins and Cord-19 remains a global challenge. This new campaign is important in ensuring that the school environment is as safe as possible.
The campaign also aims to disseminate information to families and children whose learning has been disrupted by the disease, encouraging them to prioritize learning despite adversity.
Educational messages related to the fight against and prevention of Kovid 19 in the school environment will be produced in the form of videos, posters, radios and text messages with innovations for dissemination throughout the country.
Promotional materials are also printed as leaflets and games for children to take home so that educational messages can reach families and communities. In addition, a handbook for teachers and principals on safety guidelines, as well as checklists and tips for distribution to more than 16,500 schools, has been produced so that teachers can begin to prepare. Full for the new school year.
"Now that the new school year has begun, we want to make it clear that we want our children to return to school and that we want them to know that we are working hard," he said. Lots to protect them from this infection. "They also need to fulfill their role by properly following the guidelines published in this campaign."
The campaign is funded by the European Union and the Global Partnership for Education (GPE). The campaign will be based on the success of the campaign launched by the Ministry and UNICEF in September 2020, with the aim of announcing the reopening of schools after being closed for six months.
The Ambassador expressed her appreciation for the strong partnership between the EU and Cambodia in the field of education, which began more than 15 years ago, by contributing to the implementation of national education reforms aimed at ensuring that children All Cambodians have access to quality education.
"Education is a fundamental and necessary right to ensure a prosperous future for our country and our people," she said.
The Minister of Education said this on the occasion of the opening of the new school year, which took place this morning, January 11, 2021 at Kampong Cham Special Education High School, Kampong Cham Province. The opening ceremony, which took place in Kampong Cham province, was presided over by Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong.
Mr. Hang Chuon Naron also said that currently Cambodia has about 18,000 kindergartens and general education institutions, both public and private. There are 3,000 community kindergartens, 13,500 public general education institutions and 1,500 private educational institutions.
There are 125 higher education institutions nationwide, of which 48 are public and 77 are private. There are about 210,000 students studying in higher education, about 46% of whom are female.
The Minister of Education also emphasized that in order to ensure a better education in the context of Kovid 19, the Ministry has issued guidelines on the implementation of curricula and study schedules for kindergartens, community kindergartens, primary schools and public secondary schools for School year 2020-2021, focusing on preparing students in the classroom, the division of curriculum and lessons and the implementation of the curriculum.
In addition, to ensure the effective and safe operation of public educational institutions in the context of Kovid-19, as well as to participate in the prevention and control of the spread of Kovid 19 during the school year and the run of the 2020-2021 school year. Guidelines on the implementation of educational safety measures in the school year 2020-2021 for public general education institutions as well.
Please note that the school year, which used to take place in November of the end of each year in the school year 2020-2021, was postponed and rescheduled for the morning of January 11, 2021. The opening ceremony was held as planned in the new social environment, an environment that focuses on the implementation of the rules of the Ministry of Health to prevent Kovid 19.
In his opening remarks at the start of the new school year, Samdech Techo stated that although this year, Cambodia as well as the rest of the world are fighting against Kovid 19 and there is still no clarity regarding Kovid-19. The Royal Government of Cambodia is still celebrating the opening ceremony of this important new school year 2020-2021.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted a number of measures taken by the Royal Government in the previous school year to ensure the process of education in the context of Kovid 19.
Samdech Techo also highlighted that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has also implemented measures to temporarily suspend educational institutions where there is a risk of Kovid-19 infection and to allow reopening in stages, which can ensure both The safety and health of teachers, students and ensuring the learning of students until the 2019-2020 school year is announced to be closed by the end of November 2020.
With the opening of the New Year in the social situation still plagued by Kovid 19, Samdech Techo Hun Sen introduced 12 recommendations to the Ministry of Education and relevant authorities to implement to ensure the educational process. Better.
