Thailand has already built a road to connect with Thmor Da, Veal Veng district, Pursat province, the road connection makes Veal Veng district have higher economic potential
(Pursat): Finally, the Thai government has built a road connecting Tha Sen village, Lem commune, Kat Moeung district, Trat province to Thmor Da border checkpoint, Veal Veng district, Pursat province of Cambodia. The one-way connection is the creation of a new economic corridor between Cambodia and Thailand. In particular, Veal Veng district, Pursat province has another level of economic potential.
This section of road is constructed of 14-meter-wide AC pavement, nearly 2 km long, divided into four lanes.
The decision to build the road section was approved by the Thai Parliament and after Mr. Chhat Prachai Phornmonlead, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior of the Kingdom of Thailand, signed the request of the Governor of Trat Province on November 27, 2019 regarding the expedited Open this international border crossing.
The connection of this road is the desire of the Royal Government of Cambodia as well as the Pursat Provincial Administration itself to create a new economic flow between Thailand and Cambodia. Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, regularly met with the Thai side to discuss the economic connection between Pursat and Trat provinces through this border crossing.
Veal Veng district, Pursat province, a remote area in the past, is becoming a high potential area for tourism and agriculture after a national road, National Road 55, was completed and inaugurated last year. 2020 has passed.
Veal Veng district, Pursat province, is a tourist destination with waterfalls and mountain ranges, while Moeung district, Trat province, Thailand is a seaside tourist destination. Easier road connections between Cambodia's Pursat and Thailand's Trat via the Thmor Da Strait will further attract tourism between the two provinces.
Currently, at this rocky outcrop on the Cambodian side, there is a lot of investment in housing, hotel and leisure development.
Apart from tourism, connecting the two provinces through the embankment will facilitate the exchange of goods between the two countries. Former California Governor: "The mob that stormed the Capitol is no different from the Nazis, Donald Trump has been named the worst president in history."
