Midwives and patients working in Oddar Meanchey province thank doctors, within 20 days, more than 3,000 workers through the O'Smach International Port
(Oddar Meanchey): Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Health Department, Dr. Khlok Huot, said that from December 20, 2020 to January 10, 2021, the workers who returned from Thailand through O'Smach International Port in Sangkat. Osmach, Samrong City, has a total of 3,135 people and is doing 11 schools in schools.
Remarks by the Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Health Department on the occasion that he led the team on the afternoon of January 10, 2021 to visit women workers who are giving birth and preparing to give birth, as well as other patients who are He spent 14 days in school and was sent to the Provincial Referral Hospital for treatment.
Dr. Khlok Huot said that all workers who come through O'Smach International Airport are sent to the school of our choice, and when workers are sick, we send them to a referral hospital for further treatment and care. So far, there are a total of eight labor patients, including two obstetricians, one prenatal surgeon, one colorectal surgeon and one asthmatic patient.
The director of the Department of Health said that to take care of workers in the referral hospital, we have set up a separate place under the care of doctors and there is no charge. Under the guidance of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Governor Pen Kosal, all workers were provided with a kit and three meals a day.
At the same time, the director of the provincial health department also requested the workers who are staying in Oddar Meanchey province to be willing to cooperate with health officials and other relevant officials to maintain proper health rules.
In particular, for workers who are staying in Thailand, please continue to stay in Thailand, do not travel if not necessary, because travel is high risk for various diseases, especially Kovid 19.
Mrs. O Vandin and a representative of the World Health Organization led a team to encourage and provide technical support to the referral team in Banteay Meanchey.
This morning, a team from the Ministry of Health visited the Cambodia-Japan Friendship Hospital, Mongkul Borei, a referral hospital in Banteay Meanchey to encourage and provide technical support as well as further training to the referral team of the province.
On the morning of January 11, 2021, the Ministry of Health issued a press release on the discovery of another Cambodian worker from Thailand infected with the Kovid 19 virus, thus increasing the number of patients. There are a total of 8 people staying at the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Referral Hospital, including 6 women and 2 men.
After completing the work at Banteay Meanchey Provincial Hospital, the team of the Ministry of Health, led by Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, accompanied by Dr. Ly Ilan, WHO Representative in Cambodia, continued its journey. To check the work in Battambang and Pailin provinces as well.
