Many beaches in Sihanoukville have been cleaned and beautified to accommodate national and international tourists.
(Preah Sihanouk): For 5 days, from January 5 to 9, 2021, the authorities of Sihanoukville and other departments have carried out cleaning forces along some beaches, such as Ochheuteal Beach and Otres Beach. Along with the clean-up, the beach has also been improved by cutting down dead trees and filling sand in some places, making the beach area more attractive to wait for tourists to visit. Have fun.
Mr. Kouch Chamroeun noted that “garbage comes from people. Some packed food to eat on the beach, but a small number of people did not pack properly when eating and returned, leaving litter to harm the coastal environment. "It's a bad habit that should change."
He called for participation in improving the beauty of our beaches and changing bad habits, throwing litter in the open, and taking good care of our belongings before leaving the restaurant. In addition, the Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province has instructed the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to cultivate oysters to be planted along the coast to provide aesthetics to attract national and international tourists.
