Two people were seriously injured when a mine exploded in a plantation in Pursat province
(Pursat): An excavator stepped on a mine and exploded like lightning while digging in a field at O Bek Chan point in Ekpheap village, Thmor Da commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province. Serious injuries.
The source said that while excavators were digging the mine floor, the victim, 39-year-old Joy Lin, living in Sbovrik village, Leach commune, Phnom Kravanh district, was walking behind the excavator. Fragments and smoke cause serious injuries to the eyes, face and body.
After the incident, the victim was sent by relatives and friends to the emergency room at Pursat Provincial Referral Hospital.
Death news! The mother of Lt. Gen. Kim Vanna, director of the Military Strategic Research Center, died on the night of January 9 at the age of 91.
(Phnom Penh): Disciple Mey Pong, the biological mother of Lt. Gen. Kim Vanna, Director of the Military Strategic Research Center, passed away at 11:18 pm on January 9, 2021 at the age of 81 at her home 35, Street 183, Sangkat Tumnup Teuk, Khan Boeung Keng Kang.
According to the family of the corpse, it was confirmed that on January 10-11, the corpse was kept at the house with the above address, next to the fence of the Technical School of Nursing (Russian Medical School). On January 12, at 7:00 am, the funeral procession left the house to the burial site at Wat Sophy, called Wat Koh, Kandeung Commune, Bati District, Takeo Province.
