(Phnom Penh): Due to the crisis of the 19 epidemics of Kovid, which is seriously affecting the world, the garment sector in Cambodia has been severely affected, by 2020, 129 garment factories will close. Outages that affected more than 70,000 workers.
Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training Heng Sour told Fresh News that as of the beginning of 2021, the general situation of the labor sector has gradually improved. Better than the beginning of 2020, when some factories were suspended and closed, leading to some impact on garment workers.
However, for 2021, Cambodia expects the number of newly established factories to be similar to that of 2020, while by the end of 2020, the Council for the Development of Cambodia (CDC) has approved a series of factory investment projects that will The construction process in 2021.
Regarding the raw materials for the production process in the garment sector, Mr. Heng Sour confirmed that there is no shortage, that is, there are enough raw materials according to the needs of production. Exports of garments have declined somewhat, but travel products have increased despite the Kovid 19 crisis.
According to a spokesman for the Ministry of Labor, "the entire garment sector in Cambodia may return to normal after the end of the Kovid 19 crisis."
On December 23, 2020, the Royal Government of Cambodia also announced to support the textile, garment, footwear, travel products, bags and tourism sector for another three months until March 2021. Svay Chrum Primary School is striving to clean the yard and strengthen the quality of education to become a model school.
(Svay Rieng): Svay Chrum Primary School, located in Svay Kngor Village, Svay Chrum Commune, Svay Chrum District, Svay Rieng Province, is a model school that has attracted the attention of the general public, with a well-designed environment and teachers and students to grow many kinds of vegetables. Fish planting trees make this school full of beautiful scenery that attracts students to study.
The teacher confirmed that in the school year 2019-2020, the school received three major awards: First. The award, accompanied by a gold medal, is the Cambodian Environmentally Friendly School from the Ministry of Environment. Second. 3rd ASEAN Environmental Friendly School Gold Award Clean School Award from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, 1st place.
He added that the school also has a number of other activities such as growing vegetables, raising fish, planting trees, making compost for watering crops and collecting garbage on campus, and these activities are joint work that the school requires students to Grades 4 to 6 are practiced every Thursday and are considered life skills lessons.
He added that the future direction of Svay Chrum Primary School will strive to improve the school environment, will continue to communicate with stakeholders and philanthropists to raise funds to improve the school environment, as well as strive to strengthen the quality of teaching and learning. Students receive quality education, efficiency and environment and get to be a good director, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Award and Model Public Service School Award in the academic year 2020-2021.
He said that along with this growth, there are also some challenges, including the school lack of school buildings with a large number of students and a school building 5 rooms in a dilapidated condition with broken doors and windows. Lack of budget for construction materials of more than 4,000,000 Riels, wedding fee outside the school fence.
The principal also appealed to the Seventh Committee of the National Assembly to provide a two-story school building equal to 10 rooms, as well as to repair a school building equal to 5 rooms, as well as provide funds to pay for construction materials.
Please note that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports will organize a clean school competition program that will take place every month, providing opportunities for all public schools across the country from kindergarten to grade 12 to participate in the competition.
Deputy Prime Minister Ke Kim Yan Builds a House for Poor Families in Poipet
(Banteay Meanchey): Seeing the hardships of the people, Mr. Ke Kim Yan, Chairman of the Royal Government Assistance Team in Banteay Meanchey Province, built a house for the poor grandparents in Poipet City to be a suitable shelter in Living while the grandparents are getting older and having seven children in the family.
The above poor families are the families of Mr. Yean Sarith and Mrs. Pov Chenda, whose old house was destroyed by fire on the afternoon of January 1, 2021. The new wooden house is 4 meters by 5 meters with a galvanized roof.
After the construction was completed on January 9, 2021, Mr. Keat Hul, Governor of Poipet City, accompanied by Colonel Sao Saroeun, Poipet City Police Inspector, together with local officials, handed over the family on behalf of Mr. Ke Kim Yan. Give some more gifts as well.
On that occasion, the Governor of Poipet City also brought a message from the management and donated food and some money, in which the Poipet City Police Inspector also donated some personal money to join the group. The delegation handed over the work to Mrs. Pov Chenda and her grandfather, who is disabled and responsible for raising seven children in the house.
