Ms. O Vandin: 7 points that private health services must implement for the progress of the public health sector in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Dr. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, stated that the participation of private health services is very important to join the Ministry of Health in helping to increase accessibility and accessibility. Health services in each area or place according to the decision of the patient or the patient's family in order to jointly make progress in the field of public health in Cambodia.
She made seven recommendations for implementation at all private health care facilities for the advancement of public health in Cambodia:
1: In the context of the fight against Kovid-19, we must work together to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 with the Ministry of Health, as well as with the Royal Government, in accordance with the guidelines of the Ministry of Health, without allowing private services to diagnose and treat Kovid-19. And requires the participation of private health services in the investigation of Kovid-19 suspected cases using the Kovid-19 suspected case when customers come to use the service at their place.
This is in accordance with the high recommendation of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who addressed his compatriots on December 15, 2020 and it is necessary to send the suspects to public hospitals and follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health on Measures to prevent infection in its place in accordance with the Instruction No. 103 OPSMP dated 25 December 2020 and Instruction No. 104 OPSMP dated 29 December 2020.
3. The Association of Private Health Service Providers must be able to clearly plan its annual activities to be implemented every year, striving to maintain a balance between quantity and technical quality, which is our concern.
4: Must be able to develop medical technology using a computer or online system to join the Ministry of Health in the registration of private health care licenses electronically in the future to facilitate the management and monitoring of implementation and can Towards future quality assessment (Accreditation).
6: Treat patients with respect to the ethics of non-discriminatory medical professionals with high responsibility and continue to strive to strengthen further knowledge to ensure capacity building to strengthen techniques in the treatment of diseases. Better and develop medical technology to be appropriate and up-to-date.
7: Please call on the owners or responsible persons of all private health care facilities in Cambodia, such as private hospitals, polyclinics, clinics, laboratories, laboratories, dental clinics, cosmetic centers and clinics, please be united. Join as a group, volunteer to become a member of the Association of Private Health Providers for everyone.
In addition, to cooperate with this association to be a strong force to help each other and share experiences as well as information of the Ministry of Health, encourage this association to be active in order to jointly develop the health sector to grow further. In addition, for the benefit of improving the health of the general population, contribute to the development of a prosperous nation.
This statement was made by Ms. O Vandin on the occasion of the official launch of the Association of Private Health Providers in Cambodia at the Sunway Hotel this morning, January 9, 2021.
She added, "On the occasion of the Association of Private Health Providers in Cambodia, which has never been before, now it has just been organized in 2020 and launched today. Please join the Association to promote respect for health professional ethics and Follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health.
On that occasion, she also appreciated and thanked the efforts of the founders of this association, which has organized the Association of Private Health Providers in Cambodia until it is launched now. Kampot Governor Provides Automatic Alcohol Meter and Water Dispenser to 99 Primary Schools and Kindergartens
