In order to provide food for Cambodian workers returning from Thailand and to be required to work for 14 days, Samdech Techo Hun Sen provided a series of budgets and food to the Thai border provinces.
On January 08, 2021, Samdech Techo decided to increase the total budget of 700 million Riels to 4 border provinces to prepare for the work of Cambodian workers returning from Thailand. Pailin province received an additional 200 million riels, Battambang province received 200 million riels, Banteay Meanchey province received 200 million riels and Oddar Meanchey province received an additional 100 million riels.
In addition to the additional budget, Samdech Techo also supplied 8,000 kits to the four provinces, with 2,000 kits in each province.
On January 2, 2021, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also decided to provide an additional budget of 650 million Riels and some materials to the above four border provinces to prepare for the Lattisak.
The four provinces are responsible for preparing for the repatriation of Cambodian workers returning from Thailand, as Thailand has been plagued by the 19 19 outbreak of Kovid in Samut Sakhon province.
Reports indicate that more than 6,000 Cambodian workers have returned from Thailand and are being interrogated. At the same time, a total of 22 Cambodian workers were diagnosed with Kovid 19.
