Thai military sends 48 Cambodian workers back to Cambodia through Chakrei corridor, Sampov Loun district, Battambang province
(Battambang): On the evening of January 8, 2021, a total of 48 Cambodian male and female workers were sent back by the Thai military through the Chakrei corridor in Teuk Phos village, Ang Ban commune, Sampov Loun district, Battambang province.
The sending of Cambodian workers through the above corridors cooperated with the Border Police Force No. 817 and the military force of the 501st Brigade, waiting to receive all those workers to be vaccinated to prevent and prevent Kovid-19 disease.
Sources from local authorities said that the sending of Cambodian workers back to Cambodia twice on the same day, the first time: at 3:15 there were 24 people and the second time: 24 people. At 6:20 last night.
Currently, all 48 workers have been collected by the authorities to stay at Koun Phnom 32 Secondary School in Sampov Loun District, Battambang Province for 14 days so that a team of doctors can take samples to check for Kovid-19 disease.
In particular, if all workers are not infected with Kovid-19 disease, the authorities as well as doctors will allow them to return to their hometowns.
