Ministry of Agriculture issues press release on suspension of fish imports from neighboring countries to boost domestic farming
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on January 08, 2021 issued a press release on the suspension of fish imports from neighboring countries to promote local fish farming.
First, the Fishermen's Association of Cambodia shall prepare to provide information related to the type of aquaculture products that are due to be harvested in each month to traders who collect, export, import and export fishery products for harvesting. Those locally produced fishery products to supply the local market.
Second, representatives of exporters and importers of fishery products agreed to suspend the request to import fish species that are highly cultivated by aquatic farmers, such as trout, catfish, catfish and catfish, as well as some other species of fish that can be raised locally. Notification of the Hydropower Association of Cambodia.
Third, representatives of exporters and importers of fishery products agreed to establish associations and groups of collectors of fishery products in the area to collect locally produced fishery products.
Fourth, for the transit of fishery products, the representatives of exporters and importers of fishery products ensure that there will be a registration at the beginning and end of the competent fisheries officials and ensure that there is no drop in the distribution of fishery products. This does not enter the domestic market.
The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries sincerely hopes that all aquaculture traders, exporters and importers of fishery products, the public as well as the media, please cooperate with the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to better fulfill this task. In order to contribute to the development of aquaculture in Cambodia, 8 forest protection communities in Chep district, Preah Vihear province received equipment for forest patrols.
