Touk Kang "Changhan Huy" has a history of more than 400 years of successful warfare and is still worshiped by the people in Boribo district, Kampong Chhnang province
(Kampong Chhnang): The boat "E" named Preah Tinang Saray Andet Changhan Huy in Wat Vihear Luong, Phsar village, Phsar commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, more than 400 years ago, was a very fast boat that was used by the king to fight The water war was successful, making the enemy afraid to surrender, and there was also a great power festival, and the people worshiped and prayed for peace until today.
Sometimes, one night, an old woman, who is the guardian of the eight precepts that the villagers, men and women, who are afraid to respect the precepts in the village, dreamed of a white-clad man who came to explain the dream to her, telling her not to let anyone hurt her. Anyone who wants a mighty wooden statue floating on this water, please do not use ropes and chains to do anything, just do the eel prayer ceremony and take the seven strands of thread by hand.
It should be noted that at that time, the king who reigned was named Preah Bat Srey Sokunthap and the Grand Viceroy ruled the army as his younger brother named Chan Reachea, which was in 1511 AD, 2055 AD.
The floating seaweed boat was built by Chief Inspector Mongkul Setha Chey at Wat Vihear Luong during 1561, but at that time it was a boat with a capacity of 36 people. Very fast.
He added that since the cooking boat has been built, the boat has competed and competed in the Water Festival 9 times, of which 8 times won the first place. And once ranked second. Separately, Touk Kang Chan Huy also received a total of 11 awards, including the number one beauty award in Cambodia.
