On that occasion, Mr. Theng Sothol brought greetings and memories from Mr. Khuong Sreng, Chairman of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee, Phnom Penh, especially Samdech Kittipritthbandit, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, who always pays attention to The well-being of the poor, the vulnerable and the victims of various disasters, regardless of race, color or political affiliation.
At the same time, the sub-branch president also called on all people to take care of good health by adhering to clean eating, drinking and living clean to clean the environment around the house.
In addition, Mr. Theng Sothol asked people to pay attention to hygiene on a regular basis to avoid other infectious diseases, especially Kovid-19, which is a deadly epidemic. The world, as well as Cambodia, is concerned, following the simple steps taken by the Ministry of Health.
Observing that this is the dry season, the district governor called on the people to be careful about the fire. Original. Mr. Theng Sothol also told the people that if there is any problem in the local area, please contact the Sangkat Administration or the Khan Administration directly so that the Sangkat-Khan Working Group can solve it for you in time.
After the visit, Mr. President and members of CRC Sub-Branch, Chamkar Mon District provided some materials such as: 1 bag of rice, fish sauce, soy sauce, fish, noodles, soap, mask and continue to distribute gifts. Directly to the people living in the prosperous community in the backyard as well.
Interior Ministry Spokesman: 75 people arrested for criminal and drug offenses
(Phnom Penh): At least 75 suspects were arrested in criminal and drug offenses across Cambodia on January 08, 2021 yesterday. This was confirmed by General Khieu Sopheak, spokesman for the Ministry of Interior, to Fresh News this morning, January 9.
