Mr. Kim Santepheap chaired a meeting to review the results and raise the direction of the first working group of the campaign to resolve the case congestion.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice and Chairman of the First Working Group of the Steering Committee for the Campaign to Resolve Case Congestion at the Capital-Provincial Court (DPC), chaired a working group meeting. 1 To review the results and raise the direction for the implementation of the campaign to resolve the case congestion for 222 days from May 18 to December 25, 2020 of the Court and the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The meeting was attended by the President in charge of Area 1, as well as the working group in charge of the Court and the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, the President of the Court of First Instance, the Prosecutor and the Deputy Prosecutor of the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, the Secretary of the Secretariat, the Deputy Chairman of the Secretariat. Clerk and Secretariat of the Court of First Instance and the Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
During the 222 days of 2020, during the implementation of the campaign to resolve congestion cases in the capital-provincial courts throughout the country, the commission resolved more than 35 congested criminal cases, both at the prosecution stage, the investigation stage and the trial stage. , 100 cases account for 89% of all congested criminal cases.
Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Justice and Chairman of the 1st Working Group Leading the first working group to hold a meeting to review the results and raise the direction for the implementation of the campaign to resolve the case congestion at the court and the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
Mr. Chea Chanto: The spirit of victory on January 7 is still alive in the consciousness of the Cambodian people, never to be forgotten!
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Chea Chanto, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the National Task Force for Stong District, said that the spirit of the January 7 victory is still alive in the minds of the Cambodian people and will never be forgotten.
Mr. Chea Chanto made this remark during the celebration of "Celebrating the 42nd Anniversary of January 7 Victory Day, the Second Birthday of the People and the Country of Cambodia, Saved and Liberated from Democratic Kampuchea". Participation from members of the Cambodian People's Party, Stong district, Kampong Thom province.
A gathering to celebrate the 42nd anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day of the members of the Cambodian People's Party in Stong District was held on January 8, 2021 with the direct participation of Mr. Chea Chanto.
Mr. Chea Chanto read a message from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, to the ceremony that from the day of victory on January 7, the people raised the flag of national unity, overcoming all obstacles to protect their survival and rebuild the country from Zero is a step-by-step change until now.
The message emphasizes that the spirit of January 7 has immortal values for the nation and the people of Cambodia to move forward on the path of independence, peace, freedom, neutrality, democracy and social progress.
Mr. Chea Chanto stated, "This year, due to Kovid 19, Cambodia did not celebrate the 42nd anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day on a large scale, but the meaning and spirit of the January 7 Victory will remain alive in the minds of the Cambodian people and will never be forgotten." "
He added that we clearly remember that over the past 42 years, the country and its people have gone through many obstacles for the survival and development of the nation. In general, one hand protects and the other hand builds and builds the nation until we achieve fruitful results in all areas up to now.
He added that no one knows more than the hardships we have been through. Therefore, the victory of January 7 is in the heart of every citizen and also a symbol of national unity and the great Khmer family as immortal under the shadow of eternal peace.
