(Phnom Penh): Noodles are a popular food and easy to cook. According to the World Instant Noodles Association, the number of instant noodles consumed in the world will exceed 100 billion in 2019. What are the ingredients of instant noodles and how?
Choosing instant noodles to eat for health is really important. In particular, know the right source and know about production and quality. National noodles are an achievement of Khmer instant noodles made by Japan's latest machines and techniques.
The ingredients are carefully selected from domestic and foreign. The main ingredients are wheat flour, rich in fiber to support the body and protein, and use natural oils extracted from plants that are very good for health. There are also other ingredients that are rich in nutrients to provide energy and support the body.
Noodles are produced with proper inspection and recognition by the Ministry of Health and relevant institutions of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Noodles are also recognized and included as a member of the World Instant Noodles Association, which so far is the only instant noodles representing Cambodia recognized by this World Association. .
Noodles focus on quality, increase convenience and meet the needs of the people. What is new about noodles? Do not forget to follow up soon.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Donates to 720 Poor Families in Kamchay Mear District
(Prey Veng): Mr. Steng Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Kamchay Mear District, Prey Veng Province on the morning of January 7, 2021 to bring rice as a gift from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister. Interior and Lok Chumteav to distribute to 720 more poor families in three communes in Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province.
On that occasion, Mr. Steng Sokhom brought a message from the leaders of the Royal Government of Cambodia. In particular, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group visited Prey Veng Province to wish all the people with nostalgia and concern for their well-being.
Mr. Steng Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, explained to the people there that the donations given now are in two forms. Part of that is the budget of the Royal Government, which has invested in the construction of major national roads, large irrigation systems, school buildings, schools, hospitals, health centers. The other part is the support or gifts of philanthropists and CPP leaders to the people of Kamchay Mear district.
"The purpose of this investment and assistance is that the Royal Government as well as the leaders aim to improve the lives of the people through interconnection within the country by building national roads, roads and trails for thousands of kilometers to create It is convenient for you to travel from one province to another to earn a living, which provides time and money savings. Mr. Steng Sokhom confirmed.
Mr. Steng Sokhom said on that occasion that the Royal Government not only connects within the country, the Royal Government also connects the main national roads with neighboring countries in order to enable people to do cross-border trade with neighboring countries. Side and job search abroad.
It should be noted that according to the identification, there are 5,176 poor families in Kamchay Mear district out of a total of 25,801 families in the district. There were 3,842 poor families in Level 1 and Level 2 before Kovid 19, and 1,346 poor families in Level 1 and Level 2 during Kovid 19.
Seeing the hardships of the people affected by Kovid 19 and other victims, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and Lok Chumteav donated 45,680 kg of rice to Kamchay Mear district to distribute to the needy people. Daily life.
Donations from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and Lok Chumteav now include: 25 kg of rice, 1 bottle of soap and 1 T-shirt for each family. 720 families came from Cheak commune, Krabao commune and Kranhong commune, Kamchay Mear district, Prey Veng province.
