"It is a disgrace and a tragedy that the United States itself has proclaimed itself the father of democracy and that the credibility of its electoral system for hundreds of years has been shattered by the insurgency. "The Capitol, the US House of Representatives, is a testament to America's shame to the world."
He believes that democracy in the United States is going backwards because of the crackdown by the authorities and the violent insurgents seem to be in a country without rules.
"The United States seems to have lost its role because of what has happened, which sets a bad example for the nations of the world, and its pride in claiming to be the father of democracy is worthless." This is Mr. Kin Phea's additional confirmation.
He analyzed that the loss of this role was due to the first: the loss of trust in the United States, the second: disrespect for the will of the people, and the last thing is the rise of violence, a message to the world that the United States Has lost its role as a democratic leader.
