General knowledge: Radium is a rare metal in the world and is very useful in medicine.
(World): Radium (Radium) is a rare metal in the world, it was first discovered in the late 19th century by a couple of scientists. Radium has been used extensively in the medical field since its discovery, but the metal also poses a serious threat to human health.
Today, radium is the most valuable metal because to get 2 grams of radium, many tons of ore must be dissolved, while a small piece of radium is worth tens of thousands of dollars because it is a very rare metal. Where this type of metal is present is in Canada and Bohemia.
The main benefit of radium is that it can cure skin cancer, tumors and many other skin types through its green light.
However, radium was later discovered to be harmful to human health when it was used in various chemical processes due to its high levels of radiation and chemical reactions. Currently, apart from its use in medicine and nuclear, radium is not used in any other field. Summary of important news events for January 07, 2021
