Mr. Chea Chanto said, "People's health is an important issue that needs to be addressed, especially during the period affected by Kovid 19 to improve people's health." The construction of a new building for Tang Krasang Health Center is now very important to improve the health of the people. This area.
He added that in order for this health center to be able to receive examination and treatment of patients as well.
On that occasion, Mr. Chea Chanto requested the doctors to pay more attention and be more responsible in treating patients. With this, we must continue to educate people on how to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 on a regular basis as instructed by the Ministry of Health.
Mr. Chea Chanto stated that today's achievement was built as Cambodians across the country celebrated the 42nd anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day, the day Cambodia was liberated and liberated from Democratic Kampuchea.
Mr. Chea Chanto considered that the new achievements that are happening in the territory of Santuk district now come from the unity force, especially the peace factor from the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
So far, Cambodia has had the fastest economic growth in the world, including in the areas of politics, security, social order, solidarity, prosperity and better political stability. Cambodia's reputation on the international stage has been continuously promoted and appreciated.
Cambodia-Vietnam friendship continues to develop. Recently, the leaders of the two countries agreed to continue to facilitate the implementation of the joint declaration and cooperation agreement between the two sides, including promoting widespread dissemination among the people of the two countries, especially the younger generation. About the friendly relations between Cambodia and Vietnam, and Cambodia considers January 7 as a national holiday as well.
The two leaders also praised the historical significance of the signing of two legal documents recognizing the achievements (84%) of the land border demarcation between the two countries and agreeing to speed up the implementation. Necessary procedures for the above two documents will enter into force soon and continue negotiations to resolve the remaining border areas that have not yet been demarcated to build a peaceful Cambodia-Vietnam border.
The two leaders also pledged to work closely and effectively on international and regional issues, especially within the framework of ASEAN cooperation and ASEAN-led mechanisms. , United Nations, World Trade Organization, ASEM, and the Mekong Subregion Cooperation Mechanism.
Within the economic framework, Vietnamese investment in Cambodia has yielded positive results. To date, Vietnam has 184 investment projects in Cambodia with a total capital of 2.76 billion US dollars, ranking third among 78 countries and territories in which Vietnam has invested (after Russia). And Laos). Vietnam has been investing in Cambodia since 2005.
Victory on January 7, 1979 saved the Cambodian people from genocide, regained the right to life, human rights, and entered the era of true independence and freedom, reviving the country and its people. Peaceful and beautiful life. This is also a joint victory of the people of the two countries, which shows the strength of the spirit of international unity, loyalty and complete love between the people of the two countries.
With this victory, the relations between the two countries, Cambodia and Vietnam, have entered a new era, which promotes solidarity, traditional friendship and comprehensive cooperation between the two countries on the principles of peace and respect for independence, sovereignty, territorial integrity and respect for common interests. Mutual law for the development and prosperity of both countries.
It can be said that the victory of the Cambodian people over the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime closed the darkest and most painful history of the Cambodian people by opening an era of independence, peace, freedom and development for this country. At the same time, January 7, 1979 became the National Day of the Cambodian people.
We can see that the meaning of the Vietnamese People's Army, which rescued the Cambodian people from the Khmer Rouge genocide of January 7, 1979, will remain in the hearts of the people forever. In this sense, this friendship will help promote the cause of building and defense of the two countries, as well as contribute to strengthening national cooperation, promoting regional and international integration of the two countries, Cambodia-Vietnam in the new era.
By Ouch Leang, Department of Asia-Africa and Middle East Studies, Institute of International Relations, Cambodia, Royal Academy of Cambodia
