Council for the Development of Cambodia Chairs a Consultative Meeting on the Draft Law on "New Investment of Cambodia"
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, chaired a consultation meeting on the draft law on "New Investment of Cambodia".
This consultation meeting was held on January 6, 2021 with the participation of the working group for the preparation of investment law of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, chaired by Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Both representatives of the Ministry and many other stakeholders.
This new draft law on investment was prepared in accordance with the indications of the Cambodia Industrial Development Policy Document 2015-2025 and the introductory speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum. Held on March 29, 2019 in order to make the Cambodian Investment Law more attractive and competitive for socio-economic development in Cambodia.
This draft law was discussed by the Working Group on Legislation, Taxation and Development (Group "D") of the Royal Government-Private Sector Forum by the Deputy Prime Minister, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Co-Chair of Group "D". With a private sector representative to get access eventually.
Please be informed that the Law on Investment of Cambodia was first adopted in 1994 and amended in 2003. BREAKING: Four killed in violence at US House of Representatives!
Secrets of the Sea of Milk sculptures in the galleries of Angkor Wat with night longer than day
After all, very few people have observed and known about these times. Archaeologists uncover the secrets of longer night and day events on the Sea of Milk sculptures in the Angkor Wat gallery.
Mr. M. Sokrithy, Archaeologist and Head of the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology of the APSARA Authority, presented some evidence of longer nights than days that the public should be interested in.
In the Hindu tradition, night means evil nature, which has more power than good nature. For example, during the night, which is longer than the day on December 21, the morning light shines on the statues as evil, making the shadows of the pillars in the temple gallery obscure the main sculptures that are the characters of nature. Good or gods.
As a follower and understand the benefits of the above event, Mr. M. Sokrithy further stated that this event takes place both in the East Gallery at sunrise and in the West Gallery at sunset, and this event will be the opposite. June 21 is an annual event where the day is longer than the night.
This great secret that the general public does not pay much attention to is another special feature of Angkor Wat, apart from the richness of the whole temple style.
In the opinion of Mr. M. Sokrithy, this event is not a coincidence, but it is the correct and precise calculation of the ancestors of that generation and was properly prepared before carving stories at each location.
