Svay Rieng Provincial Officials Continue to Find Soybean Bubbles with Chemicals and Some Defective Goods at Daun Sor Market, Svay Chrum District
(Svay Rieng): Svay Rieng Provincial Consumer Protection, Competition and Fraud Officer (CPC) led by Mr. Pheng Nil, Provincial Branch Manager, on the morning of January 6, 2021, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce and local authorities. Land inspected goods, food products and pre-packaged goods at the stalls in Daun Sor Market, Svay Chrum District, Svay Rieng Province.
He stated that as a result of the work, the professional officers found defective and expired goods such as 2 kg of soybean foam, 10 packets of borax, 10 packets of candy, 10 bags of duck eggs (15 kg). 8 cans of coconut jelly (16 kg), 11 bottles of soy sauce, 12 bottles of drinking water, 10 bottles of lemon juice, 15 kg of spray cake.
