Spokesman for the General Commission: On January 6, 2021, another 1,395 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson, within 6 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to January 6, 2021, the traffic police across the country inspected and A total of 4,865 vehicles were fined, including 3,617 motorcycles and 1,248 vehicles of all types.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun continued that for the past six days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
