"January 7 is a historical fact that happened at a time when Cambodia was facing death, so January 7 liberated the country from the genocide, and January 7 is the day we have a life of freedom, belief, tradition. "Religion is reborn." This was confirmed by Mr. Sok Isan in an interview with Fresh News on January 6, 2021.
January 7, 1979 was the day the Cambodian people, led by the Cambodian People's Party, with the participation of the Vietnamese Volunteer Army, successfully overthrew the Democratic Kampuchea regime led by the genocidal Pol Pot. January 7, 1979 Liberated the Cambodian people again, as an estimated 3 million people died during the genocidal regime.
Mr. Sok Isan recalled that January 7, 1979 led to the signing of the Paris Peace Agreement on October 23, 1991, and then the first general election in 1993. He added that despite the Paris Agreement, elections and the Constitution, Cambodia remained in conflict until the introduction of a win-win policy in 1996, which brought complete peace from December 29, 1998. Come on.
"Even though UNTAC spent $ 2 billion, it could not end the war in Cambodia in line with the main objectives of the Paris Agreement, so Samdech Techo Hun Sen established a win-win policy in 1996," he said. "And the collapse of the Khmer Rouge political organization brought to complete peace in December 1998, unprecedented in the hundreds of years of Cambodian history."
