(Stung Treng): Mr. Mom Saroeun stated that there are many forms of collective land rights and the well-known category is the rights of indigenous communities, indigenous identities in Cambodia, including ethnic people. Indigenous people living in the old Kbal Romeas commune will be legally entitled to occupy the land determined and given by the Royal Government.
He said this during the inspection on January 5, 2021, led the provincial working group to inspect and resolve the land registration of the Pnong indigenous community in Kbal Romeas Chas village, commune. Kbal Romeas, Sesan District and inspected the actual situation of Talat Health Center in Talat Commune, Sesan District, Stung Treng Province.
Mr. Mom Saroeun continued that the land registration of the Pnong indigenous community in Kbal Romeas Chas village, Kbal Romeas commune, Sesan district has benefited many indigenous people to enjoy this land without No corrupt person can invade the land of an indigenous association.
Seeing the difficulties of the people living in Kbal Romeas Chas village, the provincial governor urged the district authorities to cooperate with the relevant departments to study and repair the road step by step to facilitate travel.
On that occasion, Mr. Mom Saroeun continued to inspect the actual situation of the operation of Talat Health Center, which has been built 100% to serve the people to receive health care services in the entire Talat commune, as well as Some communes near this health center. The Ministry of Commerce and the Japanese company Yamato Green join hands to promote the cultivation and marketing of Cambodian products
"Yamato Green" is a large Japanese company that has invested in the agribusiness sector in Cambodia, with about 18 small and large companies as partners. The company has developed a value chain model for agro-commercial products to ensure both quantity and quality of agro-commercial products meet the needs of the domestic market and export sustainably through the franchise business of consistent product models. By scale and standard set only.
As an industrial and agribusiness development partner in Cambodia, Yamato Green will be a suitable partner for the development of sustainable agribusiness production and the provision of processing techniques, packaging and procedures to increase opportunities in Efficient supply of domestic market and export.
Mr. Pan Sosak stated that the signing of this Memorandum of Understanding is a joint venture between the public and private sectors in response to the Royal Government of Cambodia's policy to promote the agribusiness sector in line with the fourth rectangle. The first of the Rectangular Strategy, the fourth phase in the promotion of agriculture and rural development.
The Minister of Commerce added that the MoU will establish good cooperation to address challenges in the value chain and strengthen the productivity and quality of Cambodian products to meet market demand.
"To address the challenges of sustainable business model production in the digital age, Yamato Green's involvement in developing a state-of-the-art production model will drive current domestic production," said Pan Sosak. "
"Small and medium enterprises and farmers' groups will be able to establish an environmentally friendly supply chain and gain competitive advantage for market penetration and market diversification," he said.
On this occasion, Mr. Pan Sosak made some recommendations to stakeholders to increase the efficiency of cooperation and benefit growers and producers. The Minister recommended that stakeholders should have a specific information management system for sharing tasks according to functions and providing information to each other in a timely manner.
In addition, the team should develop medium- and long-term coordination systems and mechanisms to ensure that technical assistance and benefits provided to small and medium-sized enterprises and non-overlapping farmers.
The minister also suggested that Yamato Green should bring agro-commercial products from smallholder farmers to large markets, increase investment and provide development techniques at all stages of the agribusiness cycle, from cultivation to processing. Packaging until delivery. In addition, Yamato Green should provide technical assistance in enforcing e-commerce law enforcement.
Mr. Samrith Sakura, Acting Director General of the General Department of Domestic Trade and Director of the Smallholder Agricultural Market Promotion Project (AIMS), said that Yamato Green is a company with high experience in the agribusiness sector. He said that through this memorandum, the company will help share experiences and provide models in cultivation, processing, marketing and export for Cambodian products.
Mr. Samrith Sakura expressed confidence that "Yamato Green" and its partners will help improve the production chain and value of Cambodian agricultural products.
US Vice President Mike Pence will chair a session of the U.S. Congress on Wednesday in the counting of ballots cast for Biden and Trump on Dec. 14. It is also the time when the face of the new president of the United States will be finally announced.
The 538 voters, who directly ran for president of the United States, voted in favor of Joe Biden with 306 votes, beating Trump by 232 votes. With this turnout, Biden will become the 46th President of the United States, who will be officially sworn in on January 20.
