Galileo Galileo was born on February 15, 1564, in the city of Pisa in the Republic of Florence, now the city of Florence, Italy. He had studied medicine and philosophy in college, but Galileo always had the opposite view, as the professors at that time believed in the teachings of the ancient Greek scholars, especially Aristotle, and Catholic theology.
After learning this new theory, Galileo taught it to his students at the University of Venice, much to the displeasure of Galilean scientists, but they had no evidence to argue with Galileo. No, they slandered and accused Galileo of inventing anti-religious, anti-government, and anti-God theories.
It was not until much later, after many years of Galilee's death, that re-observations of objects in space resumed. Later generations of astronomers discovered the same sexuality as Galileo's theory, which began in the early 17th century, and the world changed its view of Galilean scholars. His is absolutely right.
