Senior Minister Ly Thuch: Donors Appreciate Samdech Techo's Leadership in Ending Landmine Threats
(Phnom Penh): Representatives of donor communities, including UNDP representatives in Cambodia, praised the leadership of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Action Authority, who set out a clear vision and goal of ending the mine threat. 2025.
The Australian Representative to Australia, David Bloch, expressed his support for the project implementation process and believed in the mine authority's ability to implement the project until 2025 and the coordination of UNDP partners. Agreed plan.
Elliott Kirton, First Secretary of the Embassy of New Zealand in Thailand, who attended the online meeting, expressed satisfaction with the funding for humanitarian demining in Cambodia through the Mine Action Project for the fourth phase. Embassy representatives hope to have the opportunity to visit and learn more about the need for demining operations in Cambodia one day.
The Senior Minister described UNDP as a strong and tireless partner with the Mine Authority, which has been actively involved in seeking support for demining projects for financial, material and technical consultations since its inception. 2006.
On behalf of the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Action Authority, the Senior Minister also thanked the Royal Government of Cambodia for its generous support provided by the people and governments of Australia, the Republic of Korea and New Zealand, among other countries, to participate in demining and remediation work. Explosives from the war in Cambodia through the demining project for the fourth phase.
He added that the joint support of donors and UNDP was highly appreciated by the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, especially the communities living in mine-affected areas, which was crucial while That we all continue to strengthen our joint efforts and goals towards achieving a landmine-free Cambodia by 2025.
The Senior Minister added that despite the Covid-19 pandemic, demining operations in Cambodia have continued successfully and safely. On that occasion, the Senior Minister thanked our deminers for their hard work and heroism, working both risk-free and fearless in their respective organizations.
As of November 2020, Cambodia has cleared 2,116 square kilometers, destroyed 1,094,616 anti-personnel mines, 25,473 anti-tank mines and explosive remnants of war, including two cluster munitions. , 880,314 goals, with 5,696,553 beneficiaries. Despite these efforts, Cambodia still faces huge challenges over an area of 2,150 square kilometers, of which 834 square kilometers are affected by landmines.
(Kampot): Four provincial governors, including Kampot Provincial Governor Chiao Tai, Takeo Provincial Governor Ouch Phea, Kampong Speu Provincial Governor Vy Samnang and Kep Som Piseth Provincial Governor, this morning, January 6, 2021, at the Provincial Hall. Kampot met to adjust the boundaries between the four provincial administrations with the participation of departments, professional institutions and relevant authorities of each provincial administration.
The four provincial administrations held this joint meeting because the demarcation of the administrative boundaries between the four provinces (Kampot, Takeo, Kampong Speu and Kep) was not yet clear to reach a clear definition. And agree on the management of the territory, the provincial administration speaks one by one and verifies some points of the provincial administrative boundaries that have not yet agreed on the management of the administrative territory.
During the meeting, Mr. Chiao Tai stressed that this meeting is really important in order to uphold the interests of the nation and society as a whole. In particular, it aims to accelerate to facilitate the provision of administrative services, public services, security and order to local people between the boundaries of each district of the five provinces that face challenges.
The Governor of Kampot Province also pointed out some challenges and suggestions that the Kampot Provincial Administration still has problems in determining the boundaries of the district administration in Kampot Province on the administration of the administration is not clear, especially for the council election. Commune / Sangkat of the upcoming 5th mandate.
In that meeting, after participating in the discussion, they also agreed on the direction of establishing an inter-provincial technical working group of the four provinces:
* To visit the demarcation of the actual geographical administration as a basis and to extract a clear data based on geographical and demographic factors in accordance with the general principles and procedures for reaching the adjustment of the provincial administrative boundary
* For specific basic documents to be submitted to the four inter-provincial meetings later
* To find common ground in the administration of the administration, in order to expedite the facilitation of the people in remote villages to receive administrative services, public services, as well as to provide benefits to the people and for the authorities to easily manage and maintain security and order. To the people and the communes to work close to each other so that the people can prosper
