According to Mr. Kim Sothin, Deputy Director General of APSARA Authority, the third ridge of the Bayon temple has deteriorated due to the ruptured stone structure due to weather, construction age, poor design quality. Construction structures that could endanger the entire temple structure, including some affected by tourist activities.
He stated that during the repair work, the APSARA Authority will carry out a number of works, such as moving the rock out and pushing it back in the third corner of the south, supporting 56 different areas where there is a risk of collapse. . There will also be a seal on the stone seam that it cracks so that it does not seep in water and adjust the uneven rough stone so as not to endanger visitors when visiting the temple.
This work is done by the experts of the APSARA Authority themselves and will take a year to complete the renovation of the Bayon temple in the third block if there are no obstacles, including the design, research and documentation. Inquiries from ADHOC experts of the Asia-Angkor International Committee.
