Angry mother-in-law forbids drinking, pulls a knife, kills 3, seriously injures mother and child in Kien Svay district, Kandal province
(Central): A woman and her two children were brutally attacked by her husband's friends, causing serious injuries as the victim forbade her to drink at her home, causing the suspect to become very angry while her husband The victim went out to buy meat, the suspect jumped up and pulled out a knife to cut the victim and the child.
This incident happened at 8:00 pm on January 5, 2021 in Ro Taeng village, Phum Thom commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province.
The three victims were rushed to the hospital overnight and the suspects escaped.
The victim, Sok Chandy, a 32-year-old girl, was seriously injured, her son Raksmey Sreyya, a 13-year-old girl, was seriously injured, and her other child, Raksmey Sochin, a 08-year-old girl, was seriously injured and is currently receiving emergency treatment. Also at Kantha Bopha Hospital.
The suspect is John Sovan Chantokol, male, 29 years old, ethnic Khmer, occupation Construction worker, born in Po Mieu village, Koki Thom commune, Kien Svay district, Kandal province. Currently living in the workplace (construction worker) in Sangkat Prek Eang, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
Authorities confirmed that the subject is already known because both the victim and the suspect are relatives working on construction together. Immediately after the incident, forces throughout Kien Svay district launched a hunting operation from the night of the incident to arrest the suspects and punish them according to the law.
