General knowledge: How many species of monkeys are there in Cambodia?
(Phnom Penh): Currently in Cambodia, 11 species have been found, most of which live in the highlands, at an altitude of more than 1,600 meters above sea level, and in the lowlands of the forest. Submerged and mangrove forests, while some monkeys also have the ability to swim professionally.
The following are the characteristics and living conditions of the tribes in Cambodia:
Apart from Cambodia, it also inhabits Thailand, Malaysia, the Philippines, Sumatra, Borneo, Java and Bali. Crab monkeys are suffering from being caught to sell to foreign traders.
Monkeys are present almost everywhere in the forest areas of Cambodia, except the flooded forest areas around the Tonle Sap Lake. It is also present in India, Bangladesh, Myanmar, Thailand, Laos, Vietnam and Yunnan Province, China. It is also a species of monkey that has been caught for commercial purposes.
It prefers high altitudes, dense and semi-dense forests in natural and regenerated forests up to 2,000 meters in height, and spends most of its time on the ground foraging. They eat seeds, plants, fruits, tubers and small insects. They also like to live in large groups of up to 50.
Many monkeys are present west of the Mekong River and east of the Mekong River in Cambodia. In addition, many are found in northeastern India, southern China and Malaysia, Thailand, Laos, Myanmar.
Monkeys are present in the Cardamom Mountains, the area around the Tonle Sap Lake, the northern region of the Tonle Sap Lake, and the Cambodian-Vietnamese border. It is also found in southern China, Burma, southern Indochina and southern Thailand.
Its diet consists of grains, buds, flowers and fruits. When there is a threat or interruption from other activities, it always beeps as a signal to tell each other to escape to hide on the tops of tall trees. The male monkey controls the herd in his herd.
White-tailed monkeys are found living east of the Mekong River in the northeastern highlands of Cambodia. Research has shown that there are two subspecies of this species, the white-tailed monkey and the red-tailed monkey. However, there is not enough data on the distribution of its existence in any country.
In addition to these six species of monkeys in Cambodia, there are also three species of vultures and two species of vultures, including the crowned vulture, the yellow-cheeked vulture, the gray vulture and the fire vulture, all of which are classified as the same species. Also. China to expand production capacity of Kovid-19 vaccine to ensure supply
