General Kim Bunthan expressed his appreciation to all officers and soldiers in the 385th Battalion for implementing the head of the Royal Government's measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease. He instructed all officers, deputies and soldiers to continue to follow the instructions of Samdech Techo of the Ministry of Health to protect themselves, their families and units from the 19 cases of Kovid.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Health, on January 5, 2021, delivered a message congratulating the people on the occasion of the Global Year 2021 and calling for continued protection from various diseases, especially Kovid. 19.
In an eight-minute message received by Fresh News, Ms. O Vandin urged people to live in a new way to protect themselves from Kovid 19, as the Royal Government has previously confirmed. In addition, she urged people to implement the principle of drinking clean, eating clean and living clean to get healthy.
Cambodia launches new STEM science course to boost economic growth
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Mey Kanyan, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, on January 5, 2021, said that Cambodia should become an industry with more local investors to promote economic growth.
This statement was made at a press conference on the course on Digital Production Line for Industry 4.0 Online at the Advanced Manufacturing Research and Training Center at the Royal University of Phnom Penh this morning, January 5, 2021.
Dr. Mey Kanyan added that Cambodia also needs to increase the value of services, industry and agriculture by simultaneously promoting human resource training because knowledge is a source of income.
According to the Chairman of the Board of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, the Cambodian economy is dependent on three major sectors, including services, industry and agriculture, in which the industrial sector is not yet strong.
However, the sector is also pushing the economy forward, such as: garment and footwear sub-sector, in which factories using electronic systems such as bicycle factories are also operating in the production chain. This is the additional confirmation of Dr. Mey Kanyan.
Regarding this course, Dr. Chet Chealy, Rector of the Royal University of Phnom Penh, said that the opening of this course is a new technology that Cambodia started with a partnership with DMG Mori (the world's number one company in the field. Manufacture of machinery) Germany and Japan.
He said that through this collaboration, not only will help the Royal University of Phnom Penh to be strong in STEM science, it will be able to help the big picture is to help the whole Cambodian economy, although it is now a small molecule, but it Will grow in the future for the economy and society.
The course will be conducted in two phases, the first phase, entitled "Digital Production Chain for Industry 4.0", will be launched online from February 2021.
All training will be provided directly by experts from DMG MORI Germany who have experience in such training around the world.
For the second session, the learning will be done with real machines so that students can gain both theoretical and practical knowledge to further enhance the quality by allowing the inclusion of practical industrial issues in the training.
The success of this project is very important for the whole Cambodian society as it will serve as a successful model of cooperation between the University of Industry and the government towards Industry 4.0.
Kandal Provincial Court Detains Star Soldier for Pulling Out Security Gun Over Ang Snoul
(Kandal): Mr. Thong Phalla Rangsey, Investigating Judge of Kandal Provincial Court, on January 05, 2021, issued a warrant for the detention of a one-star military officer after he pulled out a gun and hit the security guard on the head, causing him to bleed. The story of missing a pair of shoes.
* First: Illegal use of weapons * Second: Intentional violence has aggravating circumstances under the Penal Code.
Heng Kea Hong, a military officer wearing a star and the owner of Sok Meng Hospital and Maternity Hospital in Kandal province's Angsnoul district, who pulled out a gun and struck a security guard in the head, fainted. This incident happened on the afternoon of January 4, 2021 in front of Sok Meng Hospital and Maternity.
On January 3, 2021, at 8:00 AM, the suspect lost a pair of leather shoes that were left at the entrance of his clinic to work. Until 8 pm on January 3, 2021, no shoes were found, and security cameras were checked to see a man standing talking to the victim and handing the money to the victim, who was wearing the suspect's shoes. Get out.
After checking the security camera, the suspect contacted the security company to call the victim to talk about the story. Until the 4th of the same month, at 10:00 AM, the suspect made an appointment with the security company to bring the victim to talk in the clinic, but could not find him, so the suspect got angry and drove to the house around Chumpouvorn Market, Phnom Penh. Go back.
It was not until 12 pm that the security company arrived at the clinic and did not see the suspect, so they called the suspect back to talk. When the suspect returned to the clinic, he saw the victim standing in front of him and took a pistol from his waist and hit the victim on the left side of the head, causing him to fall and the suspect walked into the clinic. Gone.
The victim was taken by medical staff to wash the wounds and sew three stitches, and the victim called to report to the police, the police arrived at the scene and arrested the suspect, including the evidence. According to the suspect's confession. That he actually used a gun to hit the victim because he was angry and hired a guard, but got along with the thief. Exhibits seized by the police were a handgun, brand CF98, number 006009, one payload and one ammunition.
2020: More than 340,000 workers affected by Kovid 19 receive a total of more than 23 million dollars from the Royal Government
(Phnom Penh): Throughout 2020, a total of more than 340,000 workers in the labor and tourism sectors affected by Kovid-19 will receive cash support from the Royal Government. Heng Sour, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, confirmed to Fresh News on January 5, 2021 that the Royal Government has spent a total of 23 million dollars to support these workers.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Labor said that the opening of benefits to workers in the garment and tourism sectors began in May 2020, at a time when Cambodia is facing an epidemic of 19 measles. As of January 5, 2021, there have been 45 times.
Mr. Heng Sour continued that in 2020, the suspension of workers in the field of labor and tourism is not the same, but the period of suspension of workers in these two major sectors averaged four. Week.
As Cambodia suffers from the 19 epidemic of Kovid, which has caused severe damage in many areas, the Royal Government of Cambodia has put in place policies to assist factories, enterprises and workers. To date, 45 benefits have been paid to workers in the labor and tourism sectors affected by Kovid 19.
The Royal Government of Cambodia on December 23, 2020 also announced to support the textile, garment, footwear, travel products, bags and tourism sector for another three months until March 2021.
The Royal Government's intervention in the above areas includes:
* Continue to provide a monthly stipend of $ 40 to a worker working in the tourism sector such as hotels, guesthouses, restaurants and travel agencies for an additional three months from January to March 2021. Enterprises and businesses in the tourism sector must contribute on a voluntary and practical basis in addition to what the Royal Government has to offer.
* Continue to postpone the implementation of the social security pension system for another 6 months, until July 2021. The delay will be based on a continuous assessment of the actual socio-economic situation.
* Continue to waive the payment of social security contributions for occupational risk and health care of the National Social Security Fund during business suspension or suspension.
* Continue to waive the payment of patent tax and tax on stamp duty (tax on trademarks) to travel agencies and other tourism operators. These taxpayers are obliged to update the patents.
* Require taxpayers in the tourism sector, such as hotels, guesthouses, restaurants and travel agencies registered with the General Department of Taxation and have business activities in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, Kep, Kampot, Bavet and Poipet. Declare income tax for 2020 at the latest before the end of March 2021, but does not require the payment of any taxes.
