Agriculture Minister calls on authorities to curb illegal imports of fish from neighboring countries and calls on fish importers to return to collecting fish from local farmers
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on December 5, 2020, requested the competent authorities to help prevent the illegal import of fish from neighboring countries and called on fish importers to collect. The fish of the aquarium to meet local demand.
This request was made on the occasion that Minister Veng Sakhon was accompanied by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, the delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Fisheries Administration and professional officers inspected two fish farms in Prek Pnov district, Phnom Penh this morning. December 05, 2020.
After inspecting the above fish farms, Minister Veng Sakhon praised and appreciated the efforts of the fish farming industry to contribute to meet the needs of the local market and reduce imports.
Minister Veng Sakhon also encouraged hydrologists to continue to maintain this business, as this is a strong career and has effectively joined the Royal Government in ensuring food security for the people and the national economy.
Taking this opportunity, Minister Veng Sakhon also advised the Fisheries Administration and the Capital-Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and the Cambodian Aquatic Aquaculture Association to help find markets to sustain livestock production.
In addition, it is necessary to help plan production, compile breeders, and incorporate new technologies, including breeding, feeding, and rearing environments, to complete the production chain, including value-added chains for processing. Minister Veng Sakhon said that for consumers and consumers of processed fish products, please continue to support local products to help increase the growth of local aquaculture production in terms of quantity, quality and price.
He also called on local investors to increase investment in aquaculture in order to increase food production to meet domestic demand in the context of the global spread of Kovid-19.
