Minister of Environment: I want to see high-income people have a better life and participate more actively in the protection and conservation of natural resources.
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, emphasized that on behalf of the Minister of Environment as well as the Royal Government, he wants to see high-income people have a better life and participate more actively in the protection and conservation of natural resources in the local area.
"We want to see people with high incomes, prosperous lives, and when people have, they will be more active in protecting and conserving the natural resources we have," he said.
On that occasion, Mr. Say Sam Al instructed and explained to the people not to continue the land dispute, to participate in the protection and conservation of forests and wildlife in the area together.
The Minister also requested the people to change their occupation of hunting to participating in animal husbandry instead, because hunting is a crime and faces penalties before the law. The Minister has given people the option to raise meat animals such as cattle, and especially sheep and goats, which are easily raised in the community forest, with less time and more profit.
At the same time, the people who came to participate requested the Minister to exchange the land that they are currently enjoying on community land and some adjacent community land, with wildlife destroying their crops.
After the discussion, Minister Say Sam Al gave them good advice and will prepare land for exchange for them to be close to public services, hospitals, schools and pagodas so that they can live comfortably. .
Mr. Say Sam Al also urged to quickly demarcate the wildlife sanctuary, strengthen the education of the people, encourage the children of the people to learn together and propose to plant trees that soon bear fruit such as acacia. And so on.
