The Minister continued that this act is a violation of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and is defined as a criminal offense stipulated and punishable under the provisions of Article 437 duplicate of the Penal Code.
It should be noted that Sam Rainsy, the leader of the extremist opposition group, was already sentenced to four years in prison in June 2019 for insulting the King.
