"Touk Srey Pdey Prat" is the title of a song that tells the true story of the bitter love life of Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit who were separated during the Khmer Rouge era. The cause of Samdech had to leave Samdech Kittipritthbandit at that time because of the cause of the motherland, while Samdech Kittipritthbandit, who died the first child and was 5 months pregnant with the second child.
Samdech continued: "I died the first child and separated during the second child in the womb for 5 months until we meet again, the eldest son (Manet) called me uncle for 2 months. "These are stories not only for my wife and me, but also for Cambodians across the country who went through that period."
"The grief of a divorced woman" brought my wife and me millions of tears. But these tears have brought survival for people across the country, including my family. "From a poor young couple to now, we have a lot of children and grandchildren, but still remember the most difficult life of me and my dear wife." This is according to the further confirmation of Samdech Techo.
However, on the occasion of the 45th wedding anniversary, Samdech and his wife wish the compatriots all over the country happiness and good luck in the new global year 2021.
