The National Assembly decided to close the 5th session of the 6th legislature from January 5 onwards.
A press release from the General Secretariat of the National Assembly stated that: Announcing the closing of the 5th session of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature from January 5, 2021 onwards.
According to Samdech Heng Samrin, the 5th session of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature started from October 5, 2020 until January 5, 2021 for 3 months in accordance with the Constitution and the rules of procedure of the National Assembly.
Please note that throughout the year in 2020, Cambodia has made 36 new laws. This is according to the legal document approved by the National Assembly of the 6th legislature between 2019 and 2020.
