The gratitude and expression of gratitude was made on the occasion that Cambodia, represented by Mr. Ouch Borith, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, handed over the Royal Government of Cambodia's gift to the Government and people of Nepal. December 4, 2020.
Nepal's Minister of Health continued: "Nepal and Cambodia have enjoyed the best relations since the establishment of diplomatic relations. The two countries share a common role in regional and international affairs. We have always supported each other in many international forums, including the United Nations, on many issues of mutual interest.
"Our relationship is characterized by goodwill, mutual respect and closer cooperation," he said. "Our culture, civilization and heritage like Lumbini and Angkor Wat are providing a strong connection between our people."
Prime Minister of Nepal Sharma Oli visits the Kingdom of Cambodia in May 2019. Similarly, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, paid an official visit to Nepal in November 2018. The visit of these two historic leaders is important in strengthening our bilateral relations and cooperation to a new level.
