More than 73,000 people receive first dose in two days of Beijing vaccination campaign
BEIJING: A total of 73,537 people in 220 areas across Beijing have been vaccinated with COVID-19 in the two days since the city launched its vaccination campaign, authorities say. Among the high-risk groups on Friday this week. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Sunday night, January 3, 2021.
Gao Xiaojun, a spokesman for the Beijing Health Commission, told a news conference on Sunday that no serious side effects had been observed among the vaccine recipients.
The current vaccination campaign in Beijing covers nine groups of people between the ages of 18 and 59. These include front-line customs inspectors as well as staff working in the transport sector, both domestically and internationally. Those planning an urgent trip abroad can also apply for the vaccine at a community service center.
