(Prey Veng): Mr. Steng Sokhom, Chairman of the Government Working Group on Kamchay Mear District, on January 2, 2021, chaired a meeting to review the results of the implementation of the work in 2020 and to raise the direction of the Royal Government Working Group. Kamchay Mear district.
In an open-ended meeting with discussions on the report and debate for nearly four hours, the local government team visited Kamchay Mear district to think together to address the emerging challenges. In Kamchay Mear district.
Issues raised include land disputes, encroachments on state public land, which the chairman of the working group called on commune authorities to resolve quickly, based on the law, if negotiations between the parties to the dispute do not agree on a solution. Of the authorities.
At the same time, he also suggested that experts should ask the Provincial Department of Land Management to issue land titles to people in all villages and communes, stating that the speed of issuing land titles gives two positives:
First, make sure people own their property where they can do business or cultivate something. Second, it allows people to use this card to borrow money from banks to invest more in their business. And it is also a way to reduce land disputes.
Regarding the problem of water for cultivation, even though Kamchay Mear district has up to 5 irrigation systems, people still lack water to use and flood every year because the management of this irrigation system is the work of the Department of Water Resources. Agricultural skills, so the problem is still there.
Mr. Steng Sokhom also suggested that there should be good cooperation between the two skills so that the work of farmers can no longer be at risk.
Regarding environmental issues in the district, where there are no garbage collectors and landfills, people continue to dump garbage in the canals. Trash.
Regarding the problem of younger brother, older brother and drug problem, the chairman of the working group asked the district police to try to eliminate all the villages in the commune.
