Legal Awareness: Capital Gains Tax
However, in order for the public to better understand the provisions on capital gains tax, the General Department of Taxation, which is the staff of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, has issued a deferral notice for the implementation of capital gains tax for one period (one). Next year, the collection of tax on capital gains will be implemented by the end of 2021. Therefore, we will examine how the tax on capital gains has a legal regime?
Therefore, the legal awareness program of FRESH NEWS, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, would like to raise the topic of "Capital Gains Tax" to the following students:
Capital gains tax is a tax that taxpayers are obliged to pay to the General Department of Taxation at the time of transfer of ownership or disposal of ownership of their capital. For capital gains tax rate, the state has set a fixed tax rate of 20% (twenty percent) of profitable capital.
When should a taxpayer on capital gains be taxed? The taxpayer must file a tax return in the form prescribed by the tax administration within 3 (3) months upon the completion of the capital gain or after the sale or transfer or establishment of control over the property; Register for the transfer of ownership or possession of property with the competent authority, when deciding on the transfer of ownership or possession of property by a final judgment or judgment of the court.
In conclusion, the capital gains tax to be applied at the end of 2021 is an obligation that the resident or non-resident taxpayer must pay upon completion of the capital gains. By implementing the collection of tax on capital gains is an important driving force for the nation to continue to develop towards a bright future.
