On that occasion, she also handed out handkerchiefs to be distributed to the participants, each of whom received a sarong and a budget of 40,000 riels. Top 10 News on Cambodia-China Relations in 2020
(Phnom Penh): In 2020, despite the situation in the region and the world, which is severely affected by Kovid 19, Cambodia and China, which have a long-standing relationship, will continue to have close political and economic ties. And society.
Here are the top 10 news items on the relationship between Cambodia and China in 2020: 1: Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the first leader to visit Beijing
On February 5, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen, accompanied by his eldest son, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander-in-Chief of the Army, paid a visit to Beijing, China.
Samdech's visit became the first foreign leader to visit China after the 19 outbreak of Kovid. Arriving in Beijing under a snowstorm, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his eldest son were warmly welcomed by China's top leaders.
Samdech Techo's visit has amazed and respected the Chinese people. Through the Internet, the Chinese people described Samdech Techo as a "handsome man walking in the opposite direction" and understood that this visit took practical action to show the core meaning of the common destiny community between China and Cambodia, which together overcome all obstacles. 2. Cambodia-China conducts "Golden Dragon 2020" exercise
This is the only live-fire exercise attended by the Chinese army, which has led jointly with foreign troops amid the outbreak of the Kovid-19 virus, both in exercise and in the prevention of the virus. This shows the high level of military cooperation between the two countries.
3: China sends doctors to Cambodia to fight Kovid 19
On March 23, a group of medical experts sent by the Chinese side to Cambodia for the prevention of Kovid-19 virus. A group of medical experts arrived in Phnom Penh on a special flight. They have been working to prevent the spread of the virus in Cambodia for two weeks.
This is the first anti-virus expert that the Chinese government has sent to neighboring countries since the outbreak.
During their stay in Cambodia, the medical team inspected the main places located in Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville, etc., helped to build and improve the virus prevention system for the Ministry of Health of Cambodia also received high evaluation from the Royal Government and all circles in Cambodia.
On March 24, a group of Chinese military experts in the fight against the virus arrived in Cambodia. This is the first Chinese military expert group to prevent the spread of the virus to neighboring countries around the world. Each other.
4: Cambodia and China stand shoulder to shoulder to fight Kovid 19
Following the outbreak of the virus, the Chinese and Cambodian governments and peoples have helped each other overcome all obstacles and set an example for the international community in cooperating to prevent the disease.
Following the outbreak of the virus in China, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia in Freedom, Dignity and Happiness Both of them were willing to donate a lot of royal property and materials to the Chinese side.
Cambodians of Chinese descent and from all walks of life have provided a lot of aid to China, and the first anti-viral equipment sent to Wuhan, China, came from Cambodia.
The Cambodian students agreed that they would continue to stay in Wuhan and work together with Chinese teachers and students. After the outbreak of Kovid-19 virus in Cambodia, the Chinese side provided a lot of assistance to Cambodia.
To alleviate the shortage of raw materials in the textile and garment sector in Cambodia, the Chinese side has guaranteed supply to Cambodia while it is struggling.
5: Cambodia and China sign the first joint agreement to export fresh mangoes to China
On June 9, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Veng Sakhon and Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Vinthean signed a protocol on phytosanitary requirements for mango exports to China.
Through this agreement, the Chinese market is open to another level of Cambodian agricultural products. Mango will be the second Cambodian tropical fruit to be allowed to be exported to China after bananas. 6: China, Cambodia hold 5th Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee meeting
The two sides summed up the major achievements of all-round cooperation after the 4th meeting, fully prepared for the next stage of development for the two countries' relations, and signed a memorandum of understanding. The two sides discussed the current status of the China-Cambodia Intergovernmental Coordinating Committee.
