(Ratanakkiri): Two herds of wild elephants were found to be eating people's crops at night in O'Yang Dao district, Ratanakkiri province. The villagers asked the authorities to help move the elephants to the big forest so that they would not eat their crops.
Regarding this issue, the Pak Nhay commune administrative police chief, Brigadier General Dim Choeun, told Fresh News Agency in Ratanakkiri province on January 2, 2020 that for the past three days, two herds of wild elephants had eaten people's crops in At night, they are scared because the wild elephants are so ferocious that they do not dare to come close to take pictures.
Colonel Dim Choeun said that the first herd of six wild elephants was found invading and eating people's crops at night in Ta Kok Pnong village, Bor Kham commune, and the second herd of four wild elephants was found. Invading people's crops in Lum village, Pak Nhay commune, O'Yadao district.
According to the Pak Nhay commune administrative post chief, due to the ferocity of the wild elephants, the local police force led by Colonel Soy Samnang, O'Yadao district police inspector, in cooperation with the O'Yadao district national park environment environmental force, deployed 24 troops. 24 hours to intervene, lest the herd of wild elephants invade the village.
Separately, two villagers, Sol Tinh and Sol Hyun, who live in Lum village, Pak Nhay commune, O'Yadao district, said that wild elephants enter the village at night and eat their crops such as banana trees, cassava and rice.
The above citizens requested the competent authorities and relevant institutions to intervene to mobilize the herd of wild elephants to return to the forest to avoid destroying crops and causing fear to the people.
