(Banteay Meanchey): On New Year's Day 2021, a suspect who stole an Indonesian motorcycle as an employee of a Vietnamese market casino was caught by the military led by Colonel Nuon Ninaro, Commander of the Poipet City Gendarmerie. The search led to the arrest of a suspect named Mao Nath, a 36-year-old man who did not live in reality.
Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro confirmed that the theft was made according to the complaint of the victim, Beetonus, 32 years old, an Indonesian national, temporarily staying in Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat Poipet, Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province.
The victim said that he lost his motorcycle at the casino market in Vietnam at 5 am on December 31, 2020. Colonel Nuon Ninaro further stated that the military confiscated a black 2014 Honda Zoomer X motorcycle that Poipet Casino handed over to the victim to ride to work.
He confirmed that after the arrest, the suspect confessed that he had stolen the victim's motorcycle to take a New Year's Eve party at night and was arrested by the military.
The Provincial Office of Criminal Investigation has sent the case to the provincial court for legal action, while the motorcycle has been returned to its original owner by the municipal military.
