(Kampong Chhnang): Doctors in Singapore have opened a training course to share medical knowledge and health care to doctors at health centers in Kampong Chhnang province through the Zoom program, focusing on the prevention and control of Kovid infection. -19 and knowledge related to the diagnosis, treatment and treatment of Kovid-19 infection.
This training course started from December 28-30, 2020 with the participation of doctors from 4 local health centers. This training was conducted under the good cooperation between Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department and the University of Health Singapore through the Clean Water and Health Protection Foundation.
Ms. Keo Rany, Director of Water and Health Protection Foundation, said that this training is very important to transfer knowledge, skills and experience from a group of highly experienced doctors in Singapore to share with doctors in Health center in Kampong Chhnang province.
The training was also attended by the leaders of the Provincial Health Department, 8 doctors, trainers in Cambodia, doctors, trainees from health centers in Kampong Tralach, Kampong Chhnang, Boribo and Teuk Phos, a total of 13 people, along with teachers. Twelve more doctors at the University of Health Singapore.
In the context of Kovid 19, which is spreading around the world, the training is allowed to take place through the Zoom program, which is taught directly from Singapore by a team of doctors who train at the University of Health Singapore, with language and language coordination. Practice from trainers in Cambodia as well.
The study focused on 19 cases of Kovid, which included prevention, diagnosis, treatment, and direct or indirect exposure to 19 Kovid carriers, and how to remove them, she said. Sample suspects.
In this training, doctors and trainers in Singapore taught the trainees from health centers to understand the levels of ethanol and methanol in alcohol to check and practice to prevent people. Protect from alcohol poisoning because in the past in Kampong Chhnang province, there have been two incidents of alcohol poisoning and there have been casualties.
