General knowledge: Who first created the train and in what country and when?
(Europe): The train or train is a vehicle and a popular means of transportation for the world today, while few people know the history of the creation of this type of vehicle, and the name of the creator, place and year of its creation. That, too, is less well known.
At that time, engineers were trying to find ways to use steam to power machines (steam engines) to replace the traction of humans and horse-drawn carriages, but no one had thought of building a train. On the rail yet.
In 1770, a Frenchman tried to build a steam-powered cart, but it was too heavy to use, and once used, it often damaged the road and had to be discontinued. The best inventor is the four-wheeled chariot of Theravada, which appeared in the 1800s.
