Iran pays $ 150,000 in compensation to families of Ukrainian plane crash victims shot down in early 2020
Tehran: Iran's cabinet on Wednesday decided to pay $ 150,000 in compensation to the families of the 176 victims of each Ukrainian plane that was shot down, the official Iranian news agency reported. Dropped in Iranian airspace last January. This is according to the release by Arabic News on Thursday night, December 31, 2020.
Considering Iran's solution to the situation "unacceptable", the Ukrainian government has said the amount of compensation should be negotiated and those responsible must be brought to justice.
As relations between Iran and the United States reached a critical juncture in early 2020, Iranian Revolutionary Guards shot down a Ukrainian passenger plane carrying a total of 176 passengers and crew in its airspace. . However, they claim that it was caused by an infectious error.
