Samdech Techo Hun Sen's new strict order is intended to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease to communities in Cambodia again after the Ministry of Health found that nearly 10 people And contracted Kovid-19 from Thailand.
In an instant message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "The transport sector must suspend the transport of people from Thailand and strengthen the capacity to conduct military operations at the border checkpoints where we have located and take The samples were there for 14 days, ”he said.
The Prime Minister also stressed that the Ministry of Health needs to increase the budget for screening and sampling by adding a team of doctors if necessary. Therefore, what the prince wants to emphasize here is that the provinces along the border, as well as all border forces, pay close attention to managing our workers who travel from Thailand to Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also revealed that it is estimated that the number of Kovid-19 infected people from Thailand may increase gradually, while the Battambang Provincial Hospital will have to cover the treatment of all those infected.
