Two youths using drugs prevented the police from enforcing the court order in Stung Treng province
(Stung Treng): The Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie enforced a provincial court order in a case that led to the arrest of three people on the morning of December 31, 2020.
Authorities said that when the military police enforced a provincial court order on a woman in a case, two of her sons suddenly stopped the police from enforcing the warrant, leading to the arrest. 4 people.
Pursuant to the arrest warrant of Ms. Say Srey Leak, Investigating Judge of Stung Treng Provincial Court, the arrest warrant issued on April 23, 2020 against 47-year-old Krem Aysa, a Cambodian Muslim farmer Place of birth: Chheuteal Phlos village, Prek Saman commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province. Currently living in Or Russey Kandal village, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province.
He was placed under investigation for aggravated intentional damage and loss of faith in a court decision in Or Russey Kandal village, Or Russey Kandal commune, Siem Bok district, Stung Treng province on December 19. 2019.
The accused did not appear in accordance with the court order.
When the police implemented the order, suddenly two sons came to block the police and were arrested. First name: Heat Amin, male, 36 years old, holding a press conference of the Peacekeeping Unit, and second name: Heat Na In, male, 32 years old.
In front of the police, the two people checked their urine and found drugs. Separately, the mother of the accused told reporters that the case was related to a land dispute.
The Royal Gendarmerie confirmed that the two young men were arrested because the two young men came to prevent the authorities from enforcing the warrant.
The police further said that they brought the two young men to the Stung Treng Provincial Police Command and also tested them for drugs and found that they really contained drugs.
Currently, the Royal Gendarmerie is interrogating at the Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie Command to build a case to be sent to court for legal action.
