Farmers living in Rohat Teuk commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province, said that due to the water condition in some main canals, the rice was not accepted or fertilized, causing some rice to be gradually turning red and may face death later. Short face, if there is no timely rescue measures.
This has made them farmers very worried, as they depend on farming for their livelihood, but if the rice is damaged, they face a lot of losses by spending money to buy and sell. Rent all kinds of equipment. Therefore, they ask the authorities and relevant officials to help find a solution.
According to the deputy district governor, farmers' rice faces water shortage due to over-cultivation of farmers. When the time comes to pump water into the fields, they rush the same bag and exceed the plan, which in the district plan requires 10,000 hectares or a little more, but farmers make more than 20,000 hectares.
