Senior official of the Ministry of Tourism: Smoke-free environment in tourism is to prevent the impact of health and the environment to promote tourism
(Kratie): Mr. Hor Sarun, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, said that the smoke-free environment in tourism is a principle that the Ministry of Tourism has adhered to to promote the prevention of health and environmental impacts of tobacco products and To ensure that Cambodia is developing a smoke-free tourism industry worthy of green gold, which has contributed to building a green economy and a green community.
The Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism made the remarks at the opening ceremony of the seminar and award ceremony on smoke-free environment in tourism, Kovid-19 phase at Kratie Provincial Hall on December 30, 2020, with the participation of Ms. Kham Sopheap, Deputy Governor of Kratie Province.
The award-winning tourism business establishments were selected through a direct local evaluation by the Smoke-Free Environment Working Group of the Ministry of Tourism in collaboration with relevant departments and partners on 24 November. 2020.
As a result, the team selected 15 hotels out of 28 inspected and 15 restaurants out of 31 inspected for outstanding performance in implementing smoke-free environment in tourism. .
The selection of the best hotels, restaurants, and award-winning smoke-free environment in tourism is based on the score of the questionnaire, which is designed with the correct criteria indicators in accordance with the Law on Tobacco Products Inspection and Letters. Legal norms under the law include: sub-decree, proclamation, circular, instruction, etc.
The main points that the tourism service business base must adhere to are:
1: Must post or ban smoking at the entrance and appropriate places that can be clearly seen
2: Do not display or display cigarette butts
3: Must not smoke or smoke tobacco products in prohibited places
4: Do not advertise tobacco products on its premises in any form.
5: Can display only one package of ordinary tobacco products per brand
6: To display or sell only tobacco products that have a health warning message in the form of pictures and in Khmer size 55% printed on the top two main areas of the tobacco product package.
