Stung Treng Provincial Malaria Eradication Task Force Holds Fourth Quarterly Meeting in 2020
(Stung Treng): The Provincial Working Group on Malaria Eradication in Stung Treng Province on the morning of December 30, 2020, organized a meeting of the Provincial Working Group on Malaria Eradication for the fourth quarter of 2020 to monitor and manage cases. Malaria leads to the elimination of malaria cases in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's goal of eliminating the disease by 2025.
The meeting was held at the meeting hall of Stung Treng Provincial Health Department in the presence of Mr. Duong Pov, Deputy Provincial Governor and Chairman of the Provincial Task Force on Malaria Eradication, with the participation of the Deputy Governor, District Governors, Development Partners and stakeholders. Many.
Dr. Rin Ravuth, Director of the Office of Prevention and Control of Diseases of Stung Treng Provincial Health Department, said that the malaria situation in Stung Treng province in the last three months of 2020 has decreased significantly compared to the same period at the end of 2019. And this shows another level of success in participating in the eradication of malaria in line with the set direction.
During the last three months of 2019, there were 693 cases of malaria, of which 178 were malaria cases, especially in the last three months of 2020, he said. From October to December, there were only 166 cases of malaria and only 15 cases of malaria.
Mr. Duong Pov, Deputy Governor of Stung Treng Province and Chairman of the Provincial Task Force on Malaria Eradication, said that over the years, the fight against malaria in Cambodia has been remarkably successful in reducing the burden of the disease. Reduces morbidity and mortality due to malaria.
He added that the elimination requires clear and specific arrangements and the need for coordination between the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Bacteriology with development partners.
The Deputy Governor instructed the staff at all levels to be highly responsible for the work, challenges and solutions in understanding malaria, stakeholders, especially local authorities to provide comprehensive education for the people. All forms of all activities for people at risk of malaria at the local level who have difficulty managing data on people at risk of malaria.
In particular, local authorities help to organize and provide information on malaria and to update intervention activities such as mosquito nets, education on malaria prevention issues will ask stakeholders. 6 Departments of Public Function Capital-Province Send Congratulatory Message and Congratulate Samdech Techo Hun Sen on New Historical Achievements in Win-Win Politics Receive the First Drop of Oil
