US sends two B-52 bombers to the Middle East (Washington inside) (US) - The US military on Wednesday said it had sent two bombers to the Middle East to demonstrate its ability to detect and prevent any enemy attacks. US interests in the region. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua in the morning of Thursday, December 31, 2020.
In a statement, the US Central Command (CENTCOM) said: "The deployment of two B-52 bombers to the Middle East is also a sign of the US military's commitment to security. "In the region, as well as demonstrating the unique ability to respond quickly to threats."
The deployment of the B-52 bomber came after the US Embassy in Baghdad, Iraq, was hit by a series of rocket attacks on December 20, but no casualties were reported. Or injured.
The United States has accused Iran and Tehran-backed militants of being behind the attack, while US intelligence officials have warned that Iran or its allies could lead attacks on the United States or its allies. In the region, on the one-year anniversary of the death of Iran's Supreme Leader Qassem Soleimani, who was killed by a US drone on January 3, 2020.
National Bank of Cambodia: Cambodia's economy is expected to recover at around 4% in 2021
However, according to a report by the National Bank of Cambodia, the expected recovery of the Cambodian economy at around 4% depends on the extent to which effective vaccines can prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
The National Bank of Cambodia's forecast for Cambodia's economic recovery after the International Monetary Fund expects the global economy to recover in 2021, but remains uneven and faces high uncertainty.
"In a context where vaccines are effective in preventing the spread of Kovid 19 in the first half of 2021, the Cambodian economy is expected to recover at around 4% and inflation is expected to remain strong," the report said. "Below 3% is a manageable low with stable exchange rate and high maintenance of international reserves."
International financial institutions, meanwhile, have forecast that Cambodia's economic growth rate could reach 4% to 6.8%. However, these projections depend primarily on the effectiveness of the vaccine, the speed of recovery in the country's economic partners with Cambodia, and the strengthening of the local economic base.
The manufacturing sector is expected to grow steadily, especially in the garment and footwear sector, while the agricultural sector is expected to continue to grow as well as in 2020. Meanwhile, exports of agricultural products, especially rice and rubber, are expected to have high growth momentum, supported by the diversification of the Cambodian agricultural market and the growing demand for rubber in the context of the improving global economy.
The construction and real estate sectors are expected to recover slowly, in line with the growth of foreign direct investment, revenue recovery and expectations for future overall economic growth. On the other hand, the hotel and restaurant sector, as well as the transportation sector, will continue to grow, but at a slower pace due to the decline in international tourism, although domestic tourism is more active.
As of Thursday, December 31, 2020, China has already approved the use of five domestically-produced COVID-19 vaccines, including Sinopharm vaccine. According to the Chinese Ministry of Science and Technology, 14 other vaccines are being tested, of which five are in the third and final phase.
China is also considered to have been successfully controlling the COVID-19 outbreak in the country, but in recent times community outbreaks have become more frequent, especially in The capital, Beijing, is forcing Chinese authorities to be extra vigilant ahead of the New Year holidays.
(Phnom Penh): Mey Cheat has announced the winners of the "Let's! Do Good" video production competition held at Mey Cheat factory with the participation of the company's management, evaluation committee and youth group. Many competitors.
Helping each other in an emergency is an expression of the noble spirit that everyone must adhere to, which is the content of one of the three winning videos of the "Let's! Do Good" video production competition organized. By the National Noodle Company.
Recently, Mr. Hong Sovann, Marketing Manager of Mi Cheat Company, said that the "Let's! Do Good" competition was held under the theme "Participate in improving social ethics". A short video production competition program established in early October 2020 with the aim of promoting and contributing to the promotion of social ethics through the production and dissemination of short videos.
Mr. Hong Sovann added that all the videos that participated in the competition were quality videos and embedded good content as educational messages such as helping each other, understanding, tolerance, encouragement, respect, mutual respect and love. Each and so on.
Mr. Lao Van, Managing Director of Mi Cheat, also said that the implementation of social ethics is an important factor to contribute to a happy society. Participating in the promotion of social morality is the duty of each of us to fulfill every day, every good deed, whether small or large, is invaluable. Only by working together to create, implement and constantly improve the society can live a peaceful life together.
Mi Cheat, as a Cambodian private company, is always happy to create and support all activities that benefit the society and the Cambodian people. Mi Cheat hopes that good deeds, ethics and social morality will continue to spread throughout the society forever.
