Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum: Cambodia's first drop of oil marks the beginning of a new historical era in the development of the oil industry
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum considers the acquisition of Cambodia's first drop of oil as the opening of a new historical era in the development of the oil industry, a valuable resource contributing to the socio-economic development of Cambodia.
Letter from Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum stated that the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia has joined in celebrating the new historic achievement that the Kingdom of Cambodia received the first drop of oil on the occasion of the 22nd anniversary of its successful implementation. The win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which has brought national unity, peace, stability and development in all fields.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum stated: "The acquisition of the first drop of oil is the opening of a new historical era for the Kingdom of Cambodia in the development of the oil industry, which is a valuable resource to contribute to socio-economic development. "Cambodia, in particular, is promoting priority sectors, education and health, which are important for Cambodia's development."
The President of the Senate also highly appreciated Samdech Techo for his excellent and wise leadership, noble deeds and noble heroism in bringing a new great success for the whole nation of Cambodia.
Major and major oil production infrastructure built, installed and completed in Block A for the production process includes:
Construction of a production well on the Indonesian island of Batang began in December 2019 and was completed in August 2020. The platform arrived in Block A and was completed on September 7, 2020.
* The oil production vessel was installed, repaired and equipped in September 2020 in Singapore and arrived and completed in Block A on October 18, 2020. The tanker is ready and ready in Block A on November 9, 2020.
The first well was completed on December 23, 2020 and the first production will start on December 29, 2020. In addition, two other wells have already been drilled to the oil reservoir. The start of this oil production is a blessing for Cambodia.
Samdech stressed that the upcoming New Year 2021, although we are not as happy as in previous years because of Kovid-19, but we received a big gift for our nation, the oil produced for the first time in our territory. New year, new achievements for the Cambodian economy from the beginning of 2021 onwards. A total of 30 Cambodian workers from Thailand return through the Cham Yeam International Gate, Corridor and Waterway in Koh Kong Province
