(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 31, 2020, Lt. Gen. Thet, Deputy Commissioner General and Commissioner of Police of Phnom Penh Capital City, led the Deputy Commissioner, Chief of Office and many officials to attend the funeral service to honor the body and equip the corps of Colonel Colonel. Lieutenant Colonel Reth Sineth alias Nhok, who was shot dead in a traffic accident at midnight on December 30, 2020.
On that occasion, the Lt. Gen. expressed his condolences for the loss of an active officer, as he always did a good job for the unit, as well as cooperating in cracking down on many crimes and contributing to security. To the people in Phnom Penh in the past.
It should be noted that Lieutenant Colonel Reth Sineth, 41 years old, Deputy Director of the Bureau of Minor Offenses of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, has two children, a girl and a boy, a good officer who has sacrificed to serve the society and he also has a relationship. Well with all colleagues as well.
The commissioner also shared his sadness with the family of the late Colonel Reth Sineth. At the same time, the commissioner also brought some materials and money to give to the family of the corpse.
Lieutenant Colonel Reth Sineth died shortly after the unidentified gunman fired nine shots, one in the head and two in the body, due to a traffic accident.
