The Singapore Ministry of Health said in a statement that more than 30 health workers at the National Center for Infectious Diseases were the first group to receive the Kovid-19 vaccine on Wednesday.
Sarah Lim, a 46-year-old senior nurse at the National Institute of Infectious Diseases, is the first Singaporean to receive the vaccine, while she and other staff members will return for a second dose 21 days later.
Singapore's Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong has hailed the launch of the vaccination program as a new chapter in the fight against the Kovid-19 pandemic. "Today we launched the Kovid-19 vaccination campaign, with more than 30 health workers from the National Center for Infectious Diseases receiving it first," he said on his Facebook page.
