(Phnom Penh): Another milestone in the strong relationship between Cambodia and India as the Government of India has sent an Indian Navy ship, about 15 tons of aid, a total of 3,000 sets to the Government of Cambodia to use in Rescue people affected by the floods in the past.
The handover ceremony will be held on December 30, 2020 at Sihanoukville International Port in the presence of Mr. B. Subba Rao, Second Secretary of the Embassy of India, Representative of the Ambassador of India to Cambodia, Ms. Tevani. Cobragade and representing the Government of India and Mr. Hang Samoeun, Permanent Vice President of the National Committee for Disaster Management and Adviser to the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
He added that in addition to the flood relief supplies from the Indian government, the Indian Embassy in Phnom Penh also cooperated with the Indian community and the Indian business community in Cambodia to donate food and medicine to flood victims in the province. Kampong Chhnang and Battambang in November 2020.
Mr. B. Subba Rao continued that although these aid can not completely reduce the loss due to Cambodia's floods, it is a gesture and a message to the Cambodian people that the government and the people of India. Standing in the spirit of solidarity with the country is like a brotherhood with close cultural ties.
During the handover ceremony, Mr. Samoeun reminded of the strong ties between the two countries and thanked the Government of India for its generous gestures to help the flood victims in Cambodia.
