From today onwards, Cambodia has become one of the few oil producing countries in the world, which Khmer children of the Techo era should be proud of.
Around this great success, many Cambodian students expressed their congratulations and expressed support for the leadership of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who led the country to new historical achievements.
Ms. Chhom Povnika, a student at the Royal University of Law and Economics, said, "As a student and a Cambodian citizen, I am very pleased that Cambodia can produce oil on its own, because this is the dream of the Royal Government for a long time. "It 's been a long time coming, but it' s been a long time coming. It 's been a long time coming."
She added that this is a great achievement of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia to achieve in 2020, although this year Cambodia is affected by 19 cases of Kovid disease from abroad and in the community, this proves that the drop Oil in the context of Kovid 19 disease, which the world economy is threatening, but Cambodia can get this drop of oil is the patience and hard work of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
She added that, in fact, according to the words of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, the benefits of oil drops received in the form of funds and other resources will help in the field of education and health in line with the current situation.
Ms. Heng Ny Ty, a student at the University of Cambodia (UC), said: "I understand that Cambodia is a small and developing country, but has high ambitions to achieve its own oil production, especially during "In the context of Kovid 19, I am very proud of this great success."
She added that more importantly, the head of the Royal Government has taken advantage of the oil pump to help the education and health sectors in Cambodia, which shows the attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia. These two sectors need to be further developed.
Moeun Chamrong Rithisith, a student at Phnom Penh International University (PPIU), said: “The great success of Cambodia's first drop of oil is good news for the Cambodian people, and I congratulate the Royal Government of Cambodia for its decision. This new achievement.
He added that this is a good thing and this is a turning point in history and a step towards the extraction of oil, which is a natural resource, it is not a coincidence if there is no effort. Mobilize investors without the involvement of stakeholders.
Ms. Soeun Nitta, a student at the University of Cambodia (UC), said, “This is a gift for the new year that the Royal Government of Cambodia has worked hard for Cambodia. For me, this effort is great because the Royal Government of Cambodia has gone through many obstacles and took a long time, including tough negotiations to find investors to invest in the oil sector in Cambodia.
She added that oil production in Cambodia will be a driving force to help the national budget revenue as well as economic expansion in the oil industry. On the other hand, it could help the Cambodian economy in the context of the 19-year-old disease, and this oil production will help the Cambodian economy in the new year.
