Armed Forces Crack Down on a 502 Counterfeit Glue Warehouse in Sangkat Samrong Krom, Khan Por Sen Chey
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of December 29, 2020, Mr. Soeun Moniroth, Deputy Governor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, led the Royal Cambodian Gendarmerie to inspect the warehouse No. KC888, which has 502 counterfeit glue traders. A moss is located in Cheng Meng village, Sangkat Rong Krom, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
After receiving the company's complaint, Mr. Soeun Moniroth led the National Gendarmerie to inspect the warehouse No. KC 888 and found 170 cases of counterfeit 2016 glue similar to 502 glue, which affected the brand 502. And the market of companies that are legally licensed and properly taxed.
Based on the answer of Chhuon Loy, a 33-year-old man who was detained by the police for questioning, he replied that 2016 glue is currently circulating in the market to distribute 2016 glue. After arriving at the warehouse, they met Aun Menghak, 41, alias Sok Meng and Hor Sokchea, and Isu Jing, 35, all of whom represented Suong Kuntha, female. The ownership of the 2016 glue exhibit in that warehouse is real.
Representatives of the Prosecutor's Office and the National Gendarmerie are preparing to send the case to court to proceed with the legal process.
