Economists: Oil revenues will be a major source of revenue growth
(Phnom Penh): Economic experts express their views on the historic event of Cambodia's first drop of oil, recently announced by the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the occasion 22 years of win-win politics.
The two economists are: Dr. Ky Sereyvath, President of the Institute of Chinese Studies of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, and Dr. Chheng Kimlong, Director of the Center for Innovation, Governance and Democracy at the Asian Vision Institute, which they are all proud of. And congratulations on the achievement that Cambodia received this first drop of oil.
However, Dr. Chheng Kimlong also stated that Cambodia has not been able to reap the benefits of large-scale oil production on its own, as this is the first step that will take more time and that Cambodia will not There is no challenge on the oil bag.
At the same time, Dr. Chheng Kimlong expressed confidence that when Cambodia becomes an oil producer, the price of gasoline and gas in Cambodia will fall if any part of this oil is refined in Cambodia and cut. Reduce the import of oil and gas from abroad.
In particular, Dr. Ky Sereyvath stated that the income from the sale of oil is a resource income that we see that most countries in the Arab region are high income from oil pumping.
He added that the fact that Cambodia has become an oil-producing country on its own is a new history born from the hard work of the Royal Government, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia under a win-win policy.
At the same time, the senior official of the Royal Academy of Cambodia also asked his compatriots to join in congratulating the efforts of the Royal Government under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
"This new history is about the hard work of the Royal Government, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has worked hard under a win-win policy," he said. I would like to ask my compatriots to join in congratulating the efforts of the Royal Government.
On December 29, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced the good news and pride for the Cambodian people from the beginning of receiving the first drop of oil after waiting for many years.
140 Officers Completed 2nd Artillery Command Commander Training and Artillery Squadron Commander Training
(Kampong Chhnang): The 2nd Artillery Command Commander Training Course and the Artillery Squadron Commander Training Course ran for 91 days with a total of 140 trainees, 14 military instructors. From the subordinate units of the Army and the Armed Forces, the Artillery Command Unit successfully completed on December 30, 2020, with 88 outstanding scores and 30 moderately good scores.
The Closing Ceremony took place at the Light Artillery Command of the Army in Teuk Phos District, Kampong Chhnang Province, in the presence of Lt. Gen. Khem Chea Sakhoeun, Deputy Commander and Chief of Army Staff, accompanied by Lt. Gen. Uon Saroeun. Deputy Commander of the Army, Lt. Gen. Prohm Pheng, Deputy Commander of the Army, Commander of the 1st Intervention Brigade, and several senior officers under the Army Command.
On behalf of the Artillery Command, Lt. Gen. Pov Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Land Forces and Commander of the Artillery Command, outlined the organizational structure, leadership, and responsibilities in the area of responsibility, including the Artillery Command. The mainland has achieved basic training, both in terms of training human resources in the command and in training visits to the units defending the territorial integrity along the border.
The lieutenant general also mentioned the work of building a unit to raise livestock, continue the work of political education, psychology for the army on a regular basis and the task of rescuing the people.
Lt. Gen. Khem Chea Sakhoeun emphasized that the Artillery Command is a specialized unit that plays an important role, especially the command and control staff, the artillery, technical equipment, artillery and is also an important core force of the Army. Support forces intervene and resist enemy attacks on the village roll.
Lt. Gen. Khem Chea Sakhoeun instructed all trainees to return to their units to use the knowledge gained from the study and use it effectively and effectively, to be absolutely loyal to the nation, religion, and the King, based on a patriotic conscience. Strictly all the roles and responsibilities of the army and the orders of the Royal Government, the Ministry of National Defense, the Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Army Command have been laid down.
