Ministry of Tourism issued a circular on strengthening the management of tourist destinations on the occasion of the Global New Year 2020 to 2021
(Phnom Penh): To prepare to welcome tourists on the occasion of the Global New Year 2020 to 2021 and at the end of the community event on November 28, the Ministry of Tourism on December 29, 2020 issued a circular on strengthening management Tourism destinations during the Global New Year, pointing to the 25 capital-provincial tourism departments, must be strictly followed.
The circular on strengthening the management of tourist destinations during the Global New Year has the following instructions:
1: Continue to promote the strict and strict implementation of the measures issued by the Ministry of Health and the Tourism Safety Rules of the Ministry of Tourism to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease, especially the control of heat, wearing masks, hand washing and spraying. Alcohol kills germs regularly at all tourist destinations.
3: Continue to cooperate with the capital-provincial administration to improve the quality of tourism services, maintain environmental hygiene and keep product prices reasonable.
4: Continue to visit the main tourist destinations to spread public awareness to tourists and people about the risks and measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
The Ministry of Tourism has further instructed all departments of tourism upon receipt of this circular and must cooperate with the capital-provincial administration, relevant departments and the private sector to implement the above content to achieve better results in a spirit of high responsibility.
Despite the Kovid-19 crisis, domestic tourism activities have shown positive signs of rapid recovery (except during the November 3 and 28 November community events), which have partially supported Cambodia's tourism sector. In particular, it has helped some tourism businesses reopen in accordance with tourism safety rules and generated direct income for local people.
