(Pursat): Due to the encroachment on forest land to be owned and sold to migrants in O'Som area, O'Som commune, Veal Veng district, the governor of Pursat province, Mr. Mao Thunin, called on the people in this area to stop and Withdraw from this illegal activity immediately, otherwise the provincial authorities will take legal action.
The above appeal of the Governor of Pursat Province was made on December 29, 2020 during the visit and distribution of gifts to people from 6 villages in O'Som commune, a total of 897 people. (4 different locations).
He added that the desire must be limited, but if the desire is against the law, the person concerned will be punished according to his crime. He asked the district, commune and village authorities to check the actual people who are hired as workers, they have land to build houses, but no land to enjoy, they may be the first to be able to provide.
What the provincial governor wants to emphasize is that the call for the people in this area must stop and withdraw from this illegal activity immediately, otherwise the provincial authorities will take legal action.
Apart from mentioning the above land case, Mr. Mao Thunin also told the people that as the leader of the provincial administration and on behalf of the same family to mourn together, O'Som commune is the first commune. He has been of great interest since he came to lead the mechanism in Pursat more than six years ago.
Please be informed that the donations to be distributed to a total of 897 people, each of them received 20 kg of rice, 1 blanket, 2 bottles of fish sauce and 2 bottles of soy sauce. Army Command Receives Donation from Chairman of Samdech Techo Foundation Association for the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): In the morning of December 29, 2020, at the Land Forces Command, a handover ceremony was held and received a gift from Duke Te Tang Po, Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Samdech Techo Foundation for the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia to the Command. Army of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
On behalf of the Army, Lt. Gen. Hun Manet, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the Army, thanked the Samdech Techo Foundation Association for the Development of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia.
The general added that this precious gift is a generous spirit and an important contribution to support the army in addressing the various needs of the unit.
The donations include 6,000 bottles of fish sauce, 6,000 bottles of soy sauce, 1,000 bottles of disinfectant and 20,000 US dollars. The people are very satisfied and happy that Cambodia has become an oil-producing country under the leadership of Samdech Techo and want Samdech to continue to lead the country.
(Phnom Penh): The cancerous news of the Cambodian people was announced by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, on December 29, 2020, that Cambodia has now started to receive its first drop of oil after waiting. A long time ago.
More importantly, the start of the first oil pump on the 22nd anniversary of the end of the war brought national unity and territorial unity through the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia's most outstanding leader. .
After receiving the good news of receiving this first drop of oil, the Cambodian people were very happy and excited.
Mr. Masamorn, who was born in Svay Rieng province and is currently working in the informal economy in Phnom Penh, expressed his support and is very happy that Cambodia can produce oil and will make Cambodia even more prosperous.
Mr. Masamon said that Cambodia's success now due to the right leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, and he considered Samdech Techo like a father who makes his children happy.
Mr. Polin said that as a Cambodian citizen, he was very happy that Cambodia, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, could produce oil on its own.
Mr. Polin said, "I just want to talk about the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen because he has worked very hard to lead the country for many years and he also promoted Cambodia to grow. All sectors.
With love and satisfaction, he said, "I am satisfied with the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and the future wants the prince to lead Cambodia in the future to lead a more prosperous Cambodia and a prosperous life for all."
Mr. Phat Lavi, Construction Supervisor in Phnom Penh, also said that when Cambodia can produce oil on its own, he sees that it can help the Cambodian economy and produce its own products, which makes the economy grow. Another level.
He said that in addition, it can help those in the transportation business can help reduce the cost of transportation and can be transformed into a factory that can attract more investors to invest in Cambodia. Well.
Meanwhile, Ms. Vanna, a noodle seller along Street 598 and Mr. Chiep Mak, a car mechanic, also expressed their satisfaction and happiness after receiving the news that Cambodia has started to receive the first drop of oil, they understand It will help the whole national economy and they appreciate the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen so that Cambodia can become an oil-producing country like this.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced the success of Cambodia's first oil pump on December 29, 2020. Samdech considers this to be an important first step for Cambodia towards building national capacity and the oil, gas and energy industries in Cambodia. The main benefits that Cambodia receives include: National budget revenue, economic benefits from the creation of industrial diversification in the oil sector and national capacity building.
The discovery and exploitation of Cambodia's mineral resources under the leadership of the Royal Government is a blessing for the people and the nation, not a curse, as some unscrupulous people claim. An angry man stabbed his fiancé in Takhmao City, Kandal Province, the perpetrator was arrested by specialized forces
(Central): A woman was stabbed by her ex-fiancé with a knife, causing serious injuries after asking for a break because the perpetrator was a drug user and used violence against her. The incident happened in Stung Chrov village, Doeum Mean commune, Takhmao city, Kandal province.
Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Chhoeun Socheat told Fresh News that the assailant, a former fiancé, was arrested by police this afternoon, December 29, 2020, around Koh Pich in Tonle Bassac commune, Chamkar Mean district. Phnom Penh after taking action on November 8, 2020.
The assailant who was arrested by the specialized force was named Rabori, alias Tuy, 23 years old, living in Phum Sangkat, where he was selling cocktails. Separately, the victim named Keo Muy Kim, 19 years old, resided in the village where the incident took place, working at home.
According to the report of Kandal Provincial Police, the suspect and the victim were ex-fiancés before the incident, but because the suspect was a drug user and had often beaten the victim. The victim also filed a complaint and kept it at the Deum Mean police station and then resigned, but the suspect still came to harass the victim.
