Despite the Kovid Crisis, some Pailin residents are able to make a living by raising ducks and chickens.
(Pailin): Although the disease of Kovid-19 disrupts the business and occupation of some people, but a family of smart farmers in Pailin province, Ms. Kim Sokunthea and Mr. Hoeung Sokea set up a farm to raise ducks and chickens of a reasonable size. Income to solve daily family life.
The farming family living in O'Khteung village, Otavao commune, Pailin city, said on December 29, 2020 that they have raised more than 1,000 ducks and more than 1,000 chickens. Black chickens (meat is black, bones are black) on his brothers' farm.
As for raising ducks and chickens, so far the number of ducks has increased by more than 1,000 and the number of farm chickens has increased by nearly 1,000.
The farmer described with a smile on his face that he also raised many black-boned hens, breeding from Banteay Meanchey province, and one black hen weighing more than 1 kg can be sold for 50,000 Riel and a black rooster sold for 100,000 Riel, and a small black chicken sold for 8,000 Riel because this black bone chicken is delicious and needs more medicine. More.
Ms. Kim Sokunthea will expand this farm in the future, not only to raise ducks, farm chickens and blackbirds, she will also raise more geese because they are big and expensive, that is, one can be sold from 7 to 100,000 riels.
In a telephone conversation with Russian President Vladimir Putin on Monday evening, Xi said relations between China and Russia "have a strong value for independence", showing a degree of cohesion despite his new administration. Jobiden, who is about to take office, has set out a policy.
A statement from the Chinese Ministry of Foreign Affairs quoted Xi as saying that China-Russia relations will not be affected by changes in the international situation or interference by other factors. Strengthening strategic cooperation between China and Russia can effectively counteract oppressive attempts and separatist intentions.
China is committed to developing a comprehensive strategic partnership with Russia in the new era. Xi's remarks come as China is pushing for closer ties with other countries ahead of Zhou Biden's inauguration on Jan. 20. 2021.
Meanwhile, several other senior Chinese officials have been in talks and even visited countries in Southeast Asia as well as Europe in recent weeks after Washington announced the announcement. Sanctions and vows to take further action against both Beijing and Moscow.
In fact, on Monday, Biden called for stronger alliances with US policymakers and allies to confront China over trade and economic issues.
The Chinese president stressed that any crisis would push Sino-Russian relations to greater prominence, adding that the two countries were working together to curb the spread of the COVID-19 pandemic. The two sides continue to assist each other in overcoming difficulties and continue to support each other on issues related to core interests that reflect the high level of trust and friendship between the two sides.
The Russian presidential office also announced that the two leaders praised the bilateral relations, stating that they had reached the highest level in history and that it was beneficial for both sides. The two presidents also reaffirmed their joint willingness to enhance joint cooperation in the international arena.
