Spokesman for the General Commission: On December 29, another 919 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson, within 243 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to December 29, 2020, the traffic police nationwide inspected and parked A total of 247,470 vehicles were fined, including 182,160 motorcycles and 65,310 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet offense, sign offense, no license plate and drunkenness. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, speeding, drunken driving, overtaking, driving without a seat belt and using a mobile phone.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 243 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
It should be noted that for December 29, 2020, there were 11 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 8 people were killed and 10 people were injured (06 people were seriously injured).
