During a message to his compatriots this morning, December 29, 2020, from his home in Takhmao City, Kandal Province, Samdech Techo Hun Sen claimed that the November 28 community event was closed after no Kovid was found. 19 for 14 consecutive days.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I would like to take this opportunity to announce the closing of the 28 November Community Event, which today marks the 22nd anniversary of the end of the war, bringing peace, national unity and On the 15th of May, too. ”
Samdech Techo Prime Minister claimed that the three main reasons that led the Royal Government to decide to close the event to enter the community. The situation was under control for the Nov. 28 community event, with no Kovid-19 cases diagnosed in 14 days, and so far 37 of the 41 cases have been cured. .
Apart from that, there are only 8 people left to be sampled as of December 27, 2020, so there are no more cases left with suspicious cases. Samdech continued that after taking control and left for a period from November 15 until now, seek to explore all the gates, there is no further suspicion.
