(Phnom Penh): A man who specializes in creating fake Facebook accounts uses pictures of beautiful women and chats with men to get videos and nude photos and then threatens to post them publicly if the victim does not give him the required amount of money. The Criminal Police Department arrested him on the afternoon of December 28, 2020 in Tuol Roka 1 village, Chak Angre Krom commune, Meanchey district.
The operation was carried out under the direct command of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, Lt. Gen. In Bora, Deputy National Police Commissioner, and with the guidance of Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, Director of the Criminal Police Department.
The arrests were made directly by Lt. Gen. Cheav Vibol, deputy director of the Criminal Police Department, and Lt. Col. Hem Bona, director of the Serious Crimes Police Office.
The suspect, Mak Hak Chetra, 23, was born in Phsar Thmei village, 13 Makara commune, Battambang city, Battambang province. The arrest came as the suspect was on his way to withdraw money from a male victim living in Tuol Kork district.
After the arrest, the specialized force found that in the suspect's phone, there were many naked pictures and videos of men, all of whom cheated the perpetrator by consoling and sending pictures as well as videos of beautiful women to the people. The victim is soft-hearted and does what the suspect tells him to do. The suspects are now building a case to proceed with the proceedings.
