Congratulations! Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Father of Politics, Wins the Founder of Peace and Development in Cambodia! All Cambodians, I would like to express my gratitude to Samdech Techo and the victorious political operators who dissolved the Khmer Rouge political and military organization, bringing peace, stability and development so far within the framework of "Peace for All". "Together for peace."
He said that the long-held dream has come true due to the long-term peace that Samdech Techo has built and maintained with life as capital. In addition, the bright leadership has provided confidence for investors. National and international investment in substantial and continuous for national economic development.
He added that although the oil sector, which requires high investment and is facing the same high risks, the actors in today's success are still overcome with confidence in the leadership and leadership of Samdech Techo. Cambodia's first drop of oil in the context of the difficult global economy threatened by the Kovid-19 pandemic is a testament to the hard work and perseverance of the Royal Government and its most remarkable investors.
Samdech stressed that the upcoming New Year 2021, although we are not as happy as in previous years because of Kovid-19, but we received a big gift for our nation, the oil produced for the first time in our territory. New year, new achievements for the Cambodian economy from the beginning of 2021 onwards. Today marks the 22nd anniversary of the end of the war in Cambodia! 11 Elements of Win-Win Politics Towards the End of the War
(Phnom Penh): As of December 29, 2020, it has been 22 years since Cambodia has achieved complete peace and complete national unity in history after being divided since the post-Angkorian Empire. The end of the war, the tears and the division of the nation came through the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
It can be said that win-win politics in Cambodia has a wide meaning, that is, it covers all sectors of society as a whole. Thus, win-win politics are strategies that will bring about social security, national unity, peace, territorial integrity, sovereignty and sustainable socio-political development.
The definition of win-win politics as a strategy for ending the civil war and seeking peace in Cambodia has the following 11 main points:
1. Win-win political policy: is to set out three key principles for ensuring security:
A) Ensuring the personal safety of individuals and families who volunteer to end wars and battles and return to the core of society.
B) Ensuring occupational safety by providing them with sufficient opportunities to continue their careers and livelihoods.
C) Ensuring the security of the property they have owned and occupied in the past without foreclosure or dismantling.
2. Win-win politics: is the morality and art of concession of the philosophy of peace, which is in the strategy to end the civil war, the strategy against guerrilla warfare or insurgency, and such a strategy has continued to be implemented until now, highly effective in taking measures to prevent and Suppress terrorism later.
6-Win-win politics: is to open the door to develop the former areas that used to divide the management and remote areas to develop in all areas by connecting Phnom Penh as the heart of the Kingdom of Cambodia through important measures and policies. To connect the distance from the countryside to the city and receive cultural and economic equity with equity.
10-Win-win politics: to create conditions and opportunities for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to be able to prepare itself as a more professional unit in the work of defending and building the motherland of Cambodia, especially in the field of soft power, such as participation in building Infrastructure, roads, irrigation, disaster relief and contribution to Cambodia's foreign policy through UN humanitarian peacekeeping missions.
11. Win-win politics: Provides Cambodia with the opportunity to reconsider, resolve legally and internationally on border issues with neighboring countries clearly at each stage, avoiding conflicts and conflicts and create conditions for Further development in the border area.
