(Prey Veng): Mr. Ouk Samnang, Director of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on December 28, 2020, led a professional officer from the Provincial Production and Livestock Office to visit duck farmers in Krous village, Prey Pnov commune. Pearang district, Prey Veng province, and brought some disinfectants to duck farmers to use in disinfection in duck cages to protect the health of the baby.
Mr. Ouk Samnang said that today, officials met with duck farmers and introduced measures to protect animal health, especially in the event of climate change, temperature, some cold, including instructions on how to use spray. Kills germs effectively.
At the same time, he also asked and discussed about the concerns of farmers and accepted the request of farmers raising ducks. And let all farmers have the patience to face the challenge a little bit in this situation where the price of duck eggs is low.
He added that in general, every year during the end of November and December, there are always some discounts, and only last year, the price is lower, but there are still traders to collect all, not long, especially this year. The price went down and the traders did not collect all the goods, with some remaining for almost a week, then the traders came to buy all of them, and at a low price, it dropped to 275 riel for a small egg, and a good big egg can cost 290 riel per egg.
