Prey Veng Migration Team Meets to Respond to the Return of Cambodian Workers After 19 Kovid Outbreak in Community in Thailand
(Phnom Penh): Following the instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister, at the Ministry of Public Function this morning, December 28, 2020, the Prey Veng Provincial Migration Working Group held its working meeting to review past activities. Come and set the direction for further action, especially the action plan, as an urgent measure necessary to respond to the return of migrant workers when there is an outbreak of Kovid 19 in the community in Thailand.
From the beginning of April 2020 until now, the Secretariat of the Migration Working Group has been the core of the 13 provincial working groups and administrations of Prey Veng province in cooperation in preparing the conditions for the migration of migrant workers. About 12,000 returned from Thailand.
The recent 19 outbreaks of Kovid in a community in Thailand's Samut Sakhon province have led to the daily return of some migrant workers. So far, 141 migrant workers (29 females) have returned to their hometowns in Prey Veng province.
Of those, 45 were facilitated by authorities and military forces at the border and transported to the province. After passing the test, all of them were sent by the team to be sent to stay at the district level. In addition, samples are prepared, tested and calibrated according to the possibilities of each base.
Based on the above situation, the meeting mentioned some necessary measures to continue to implement by striving to implement thoroughly and consistently all medical rules to cooperate more effectively in the process of preparing for the return of migrant workers. From Thailand back.
Overall, in addition to their work activities to work together to ensure the safety and well-being of migrant workers returning from abroad and to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 into the community, the Prey Veng Migration Working Group remains committed to continuing to educate the public. At the grassroots level to contribute to strengthening the cause of maintaining peace and national development forever.
