Mr. Rath Sandab continued that at the same time, in terms of the Khmer belief system, both Hinduism and Buddhism, elephants are the beasts of happiness, bringing good fortune to the kingdom. Elephants are also the vehicle of Indra, a deity representing clouds, rain, wind, thunder, lightning, irrigating the earth to life.
That is why elephants are sacred and very popular animals in Cambodian society, especially linking the power of kings, armies and religion, playing an important role in building our glorious Angkorian empire. In addition to war vehicles or ordinary vehicles can also keep the Khmer kingdom is a sacrifice of alliance between countries.
The expert on Khmer civilization also noted that today, due to advances in science, elephants seem to be facing the loss of values in Khmer civilization, which is worrying because if you look at the neighboring countries, they are taking Take care of elephants and be a tourism product to attract tourists.
