Please confirm that Mr. Dum Saing is a former soldier of Kork Banteay commune. During his tenure as a sergeant in 1985, he was assigned to guard the railway in Teuk Phos district, during which time he fought with Pol Pot soldiers at O'Plou in Kraing Skar commune and suffered three cuts to his left arm. Right eye blindness and severe left leg injury.
After the end of the war and his recovery due to poverty, he started a business selling palm sugar. Later, because it was difficult to find firewood for sugar, he switched to making palm juice for sale for 10 years. Each day, 10 tubes of palm juice for sale, which can earn from 10,000 to 15,000 riels for daily living.
Unfortunately, on the morning of December 21, 2020, when he climbed a palm tree, which was about 11 meters high, he fell dizzy and fell on the top of the palm tree, seriously injuring himself. Until now, he could not get up, there was pain in the chest, shortness of breath, back and lumbar pain because he fell from the end of the palm to touch the tree in the middle of the tree and then fell to the ground.
Mr. Chin Malin clarified 3 points about the legal aspect of the issuance of the Order of the Minister of Justice in the case of Sam Rainsy insulting the King (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Chin Malin, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Justice on 27 December This 2020 clarifies three points about the legal aspect of the issuance of the order of the Minister of Justice in the case of Mr. Sam Rainsy, the illegal rebel leader insulting the King.
1. Insulting the King is not an exercise of the right to freedom of expression, but a criminal offense under the provisions of Article 437 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia and a violation. Also seriously on the spirit of Article 7 of the Cambodian Constitution.
2. The issuance of an order by the Minister of Justice is not in accordance with the orders of any institution or dignitary, but is the performance of its duties, duties and responsibilities as the Minister of Justice and in accordance with the provisions of Article 29 of the Code. Criminal procedure of the Kingdom of Cambodia for the purpose of protecting the dignity and prestige of the King, the highest veneration of the Khmer nation.
3. The issuance of an order by the Minister of Justice to the Prosecutor's Office is not a violation of the power of the court, as the Minister of Justice is the head of the hierarchy of the prosecutor's office, which represents the executive branch in the implementation of the criminal policy of the Royal Government for the purpose of protection. And maintain social security, public order and national interests.
It should be noted that Mr. Keut Rith, Minister of Justice, on December 25, 2020, sent a letter to Mr. Chreung Khmao, Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, to take immediate and strict legal action against Sam Rainsy, who was seriously insulted. To the King of Cambodia. This is according to the letter from the Minister of Justice, which was received by Fresh News.
In connection with this case, Mr. Koy Sao, Deputy Chief and Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on September 16, 2019, issued an order instructing the authorities at all levels to investigate and bring Sam Rainsy to justice. For the case of insulting the King.
