(Phnom Penh): A fire broke out in a rented room north of Bak Touk High School along Street 199, Village 4, Sangkat Veal Vong, Khan 7 Makara at 10:10 pm on December 22, 2020, leaving sadness for two victims. The siblings stayed in the ward after their brother died while being treated at Calmette Hospital.
In this fire incident, 29-year-old Lahn Chhunly tried to protect his sister from the rubble and flames that burned her whole body.
The fire was reported by the media, which received confirmation from the neighbors that it was caused by an explosion of a gas canister. Pauline, who was staying in the room, told Fresh News that the incident was not caused by an explosion of a canister, but by a short circuit and spread to the canister.
The victim described that on the day of the incident, his room was without electricity and the owner of the rented room came back on. That night, the electric current at the station ignited and spread to the exploding gas canister.
Pauline also denied reports that she was cooking at the time. Polin confirmed more than 10 o'clock at night, what else to cook?
Pauline said the death of her beloved brother was tragic, but even more tragic was the misrepresentation that led to the fire.
Therefore, for Polin, clarifying the real cause of the fire is to do justice to his brother's body and to calm his brother's soul. Ms. Polin also claimed that coming to blame for the real cause of this incident also did not want to demand compensation from the owner of the room, just to let the public know and give justice to the body.
With tears in her eyes, Polin stated, "I came out to confirm that I do not want to demand any compensation from the landlord. "I just want to clarify the facts of the incident to give justice to my brother, let him die blindfolded."
On this occasion, Ms. Polin would like to thank all the benefactors and friends, including the Khan Red Cross, who attended the funeral and shared their condolences.
Currently, the body of the young Lahn Chhunly, who took the fire to save his sister's life, held a ceremony at his hometown in Sangvor village, Kampong Leng commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province.
In this tragic fire incident, Lahn Chhunly, although he was extinguished and left far away, left the most courageous hero in saving his sister's life from the fire, regardless of the danger to his life.
The heroism of the young Lanh Chhunly led to an explosion of amazement and sympathy from the masses.
