Please watch the full video prepared by the Ministry of Tourism: Samdech Techo Hun Sen and efforts to build a voter registration system (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The voter list is an important element in determining the accuracy of the national election process. Both MPs and Commune / Sangkat Councils. From the first-term elections in 1993 to the fifth-term elections in 2013, elections in Cambodia were often contested on election results.
Voter lists are always a problem. As in the case of the same name, the names overlap on the voter list. Some voters have names there and elsewhere. Some say that as the election draws near, people are being transported from here to there to vote.
In order to eliminate the problem of conflict of opinion on the results of the national election one by one. In the aftermath of the devastating crisis over the 2013 fifth parliamentary election, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen has initiated electoral reform initiatives, including improvements to the voter list.
Cambodia has decided to abolish the old voter list and require people of all ages over the age of 18 to re-register to vote, switching from manual registration to technology.
How has the new voter registration system integrated with this technology helped the accuracy of the election process?
The new voter registration system is critical to controlling voter attendance and eliminating the suggestion that one can go to the polls in multiple places and duplicate names. The new system has established an accuracy in voter data, which does not allow duplicate names, meaning that only one person can have one name in the system. If the identity is the same, the system will not allow it.
The new system makes it easier for voters to track their names in the system. Those who have problems with their list can complain to the NEC every year when the NEC prepares to register voters or check the voter list.
The new system also helps the National Committee to closely monitor the movement of the deceased and to remove names from the list. Overall, the new voter registration system, coupled with this technology, has made the voter data more accurate and precise, which helps to provide confidence when voting, without mentioning that one person casts multiple or multiple ballots.
Building a clear voter list is a strong effort of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and also a major reform in the Cambodian electoral process to bring confidence in the Cambodian electoral system and avoid There are differences of opinion and views that occur every time there is an election in Cambodia.
Initiating the construction of this new voter registration system through technology in 2019, Comfrel estimates that the voter list in Cambodia is up to 99.7 percent better.
From building a good voter list, it has built confidence in the 2017 Commune / Sangkat Council election process and the 2018 6th Mandate National Assembly Election. It can be said that after building a clear and accurate voter list, it will no longer lead to phenomena or post-election protests for 2017 and 2018.
Since 2016, the NEC has been updating the voter list every year by registering people of all ages, deleting your name and correcting some of your data.
In 2020, the National Election Committee (NEC) organized the registration and review of the voter list from October 1 to 19.
The 19-day voter registration and verification process saw 268,553 new registered voters, or 89.40 percent, compared to the planned 300,390 registered voters.
