Pailin Governor Inspects International Border Gate and Tells Officials to Take Extreme Care to Prevent Kovid-19 Transmission
(Pailin): Mrs. Ban Srey Mom, Governor of Pailin Province, on December 26, 2020, took her subordinates to inspect the situation at the international border gate in Phsar Prom village, Stung Karch commune, Sala Krao district, Pailin province. Bordering Chan Borei Province, Thailand to strengthen work efficiency, especially to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
On that occasion, Ms. Ban Srey Mom said that by following the instructions of the Royal Government, the provinces bordering the neighboring countries should pay close attention to the spread of Kovid-19, especially the Cambodian border. Thailand is at high risk and there are Cambodian migrant workers there as well.
The provincial governor emphasized that in order to prevent the spread of the disease into the community, officials at the international border checkpoints must monitor and monitor the situation of workers crossing the border and must constantly monitor the Thai authorities. Send Cambodian workers back to their hometowns, and if so, health officials must check for 14 days.
On that occasion, Ms. Ban Srey Mom reminded professional officers and local authorities at all levels to pay attention and high responsibility, as well as cooperate to educate, disseminate and guide people to follow the instructions of the Royal Government and Ministry of Health to prevent and control the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
According to Mr. Sles You, Director of the Pailin Provincial Health Department, in accordance with the recommendations of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health, the Department has set up checkpoints and officers at the international border checkpoint, equipped with thermal scanning cameras. The provincial administration has prepared 50 hotel rooms to accommodate migrant workers returning from Thailand.
