Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth chairs a meeting of the Economic and Financial Policy Committee to review and discuss amendments to the Labor Law
The "Labor Law" is an important legal framework for the promotion of labor rights and harmony in industrial relations, which has been promulgated since 1997. To date, the law has been amended twice, with the first amendment in 2007 relating to wage rates and night work, while the second amendment in 2018 involves seniority pay.
In line with the sharp reform measures packaged by the Prime Minister at the 18th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum 2019 in response to the rapid socio-economic development, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training Prepare "Draft Law on the Amendment of the Labor Law and the Law on the Amendment of the Labor Law".
The draft law of the third amendment is the result of discussions and input from stakeholders, including unions, workers 'representatives, employers' associations and representatives of the International Labor Organization (ILO). Overall, this draft aims to align Cambodia's labor law with regional countries to improve the investment climate by focusing on:
1: Revise regulations related to shifts to increase the attractiveness of modern industries such as factories, electrical equipment, electronics and food processing, etc. and increase employment for people.
2. Expand the scope of services of the Arbitration Council in resolving individual labor disputes in order to strengthen the effectiveness of labor dispute resolution mechanisms to further ensure harmony in industrial relations.
3. Considering various aspects in response to the socio-economic development of Cambodia, aiming to increase labor productivity and strengthen the economic competitiveness of Cambodia, both regionally and globally.
