Spokesman for the General Commission: On December 25, another 957 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson, within 239 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to December 25, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and paid A total of 243,827 vehicles were fined, including 179,406 motorcycles and 64,421 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet offense, sign offense, no license plate, cell phone use and drunkenness. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, overtaking, driving without a seat belt and using a mobile phone.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 239 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine the offending vehicles has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for December 25, 2020, traffic accidents throughout the country also occurred 8 times, in which 10 people died, 10 people were injured (08 seriously injured).
