(Kampot): Mr. Som Chen, Member of Parliament for Kampot Constituency and Chairman of the Working Group of the Cambodian People's Party to Assist Kampot City, Kampot Province, stated that during the Techo Hun Sen era, the development of the country was focused on investing in human resources as an important priority among the sectors. Priorities.
He said this during a meeting with teachers and representatives of 347 12th grade students from Cambodia-Japan Friendship High School in Kampot and Preah Reach Sampea High School, Kampot Province. The ceremony was held at the Cambodia-Japan Friendship High School in Kampong Kandal Sangkat, Kampot City on December 25, 2020, with the participation of many relevant leaders.
Mr. Som Chen also said that from the beginning, the Royal Government under the leadership of the People's Party led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen has implemented the main policy is to invest in human resources. Among the priority areas for the socio-economic development of Cambodia until the development and improvement of the lives of the people in harmony.
In fact, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has built thousands of schools across the country. Separately, in Kampot province, Samdech Techo also built hundreds of schools for the children of the people from primary to secondary school in all communes and dozens of high schools in all districts and cities and universities in the province.
Mr. Som Chen said that compared to the past, people often run to school, but in the era of Techo Hun Sen, now schools run to the children of the people to rural areas. At the same time, starting from the attention of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia is now rich in intellectuals, especially the children of people with knowledge and skills to contribute to the development of a more prosperous and prosperous nation.
At the same time, Member of Parliament Som Chen also instructed his grandchildren to be students after being automatically bankrupt under the context of the global fight against Kovid 19 under the correct action of the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. As the Prime Minister, I would like to ask my grandchildren to pay more attention to study at the college level in order to gain knowledge and skills to contribute to the development of the society.
On that occasion, through donations from the Chinese Chamber of Commerce "Chaosan" in Cambodia, Som Chen also donated money to the two schools with a total of 39 teachers, 50,000 each. Riel and a total of 308 students, each with a budget of 20,000 Riel and a small bottle of alcohol for hand washing.
