Keo Remy Leads a Delegation of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee to Distribute Donations to Orphans at Cambodian Child Development Organization
(Kandal): Mr. Keo Remy, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, on December 25, 2020, led the civil servants and human rights lawyers of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee and some other philanthropists. Visit and bring food, study materials to give to children at "Cambodian Child Development" organization in Prek Treng village, Sitbo commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
Mr. Keo Remy said that due to the peace factor, all Cambodians have rights, Buddhists and other religions continue to live together peacefully until today. The reason is that the Cambodian people know how to maintain good morals in respecting each other in religious beliefs as stated in the Constitution.
In fact, on December 25, this is Christmas Day, when the Christian people come together for a family dinner, and that's why all the leaders of the Cambodian Human Rights Commission remember the children who live there. In the organization "Child Development of Cambodia", which orphans parents also prepare pizza to distribute to children to eat along with some food.
Speaking on the occasion, the President of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee said that this is the seventh time that the Cambodian Human Rights Committee and philanthropists and friends have brought gifts to orphans living in the development. Cambodian children. In addition, the leadership as well as philanthropists will continue to support the organization to contribute to alleviating the hardships of young children living in the organization.
Mr. Keo Remy also reminded the children living in the organization "Development of Cambodian Children" to try hard to learn and listen to the advice of teachers who respect each other like brothers and sisters, especially do not commit any mischief. And to be considerate of its future first.
Mr. Keo Remy also commended Ms. Chhouk Seiha, Executive Director of "Cambodian Child Development" for creating this cozy place to help children in all walks of life by providing shelter, food and shelter. And education. These are excellent examples of helping the Royal Government as well as the Cambodian Human Rights Committee to promote human rights, especially children's rights.
It should be informed that the Cambodian Human Rights Committee under the leadership of Mr. Keo Remy always raises funds or other study materials from national and international philanthropists to distribute to orphans and poor children in centers or orphanage support organizations. In supporting them.
