Samdech Vibol Sena Phekdey Say Chhum Asks South Korea to Encourage Investors and Tourists to Invest and Enjoy More in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia, requested South Korea to mobilize and encourage more investors and tourists to invest and entertain in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The President of the Senate expressed his warm congratulations to Mr. Park Heng-kyung on his appointment as Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of the Republic of Korea to the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The President of the Senate is confident that through his diplomatic mission, the Ambassador will continue to strive to improve relations and cooperation in all fields between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Republic of Korea for the greater benefit of the people. Cambodia and the Korean people, both now and in the future.
The President of the Senate expressed his satisfaction and appreciation for the good relations and cooperation between the people and the two countries, which are constantly growing. This good relationship is reflected in the exchange of visits between leaders and officials at all levels of our two countries and mutual support in the framework of regional and international cooperation, especially at the United Nations. Nation.
In this phase of the global spread of Kovid-19, the President of the Senate thanked the Government of the Republic of Korea for its assistance to Cambodia in the fight against Kovid-19 through the framework of bilateral cooperation. And the ASEAN-Mekong Cooperation Framework. Samdech agreed with the Ambassador's remarks regarding the relationship and trade volume between the two countries, which has steadily increased.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum thanked the Government of the Republic of Korea for taking care of the Cambodian workers who are currently working in Korea. Workers in Korea have made significant contributions to improving the lives of their families and the Cambodian economy. Through the diplomatic mission of the Ambassador, the President of the Senate requested the Republic of Korea to increase the quota for Cambodian workers.
The President of the Senate informed the Ambassador that within the framework of cooperation between the legislatures of the two countries, the Cambodian Senate has a friendly group with the National Assembly of the Republic of Korea. In addition, the General Secretariat of both houses of parliament signed a memorandum of understanding and the National Assembly of the Republic of Korea provided 120 computers to the Cambodian Senate.
The Senate President urged the two parliaments to increase closer cooperation through exchanges of visits after the Kovid-19 crisis and requested the National Assembly of the Republic of Korea to help train and strengthen the capacity of Senate General Secretariat staff in information technology. ICT) in the Republic of Korea.
On behalf of the Senate and on behalf of Samdech personally, the President of the Senate is always ready to cooperate closely with the Ambassador as well as the Embassy of the Republic of Korea in the Kingdom of Cambodia. Through the Ambassador, the President of the Senate sent a courtesy call to the President of the National Assembly of the Republic of Korea with the deepest respect and friendship.
On that occasion, Mr. Park Heng Kyung expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum for allowing him to pay a courtesy call on this occasion. He expressed his pleasure to see that the relations and cooperation between the two countries have been steadily developing, especially in the fields of politics, economy and people-to-people exchanges between the two countries.
The ambassador praised the state visits between the leaders of the two countries, exchanging with each other in 2019 and 2020.
He hoped that on the occasion of the Republic of Korea to mark the 40th anniversary of the ASEAN-Korea Summit and the Kingdom of Cambodia to host the 13th Asia-Europe Summit in early June 2021, the top leaders of both countries The two will also have the opportunity to exchange ideas with each other.
The Ambassador noted that the relationship and trade volume between the two countries reached 1 billion dollars in 2019, of which the volume of Korean public investment in Cambodia ranked second with 5 million. , $ 7 billion. In exchange between the people of the two countries, more than 400,000 Korean tourists visit Cambodia every year.
