Prince Sar Kheng's Donation Distributed to 165 Poor Families in Preah Sdach District
(Prey Veng): The precious gift of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, and Lok Chumteav was distributed by Prey Veng Provincial Governor Chea Somethy to 165 poor families in Preah Sdach district on the morning of December 25. This year 2020.
The ceremony was attended by the Deputy Governor, the director of the department-unit around the province, the three forces, the district governor, government officials, district halls and some people in Preah Sdach district.
Mr. Chea Somethy sent a message of greetings from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and Lok Chumteav to the people in Preah Sdach district, where Samdech and Lok Chumteav always think about the well-being and living conditions of the people in Prey Veng province. No one dies of starvation.
The provincial governor confirmed that due to the problem affecting livelihoods due to the spread of Kovid-19 disease in Cambodia, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and Lok Chumteav handed over some food to the provincial administration to be distributed to the most needy people to solve their livelihood. Everyday at the grassroots level, though small, is essential to help the poor now.
Mr. Chea Somethy called on all people to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid 19 more vigorously, starting from regular hygiene by washing hands with soap and alcohol, wearing masks and gaps. In particular, follow the instructions of the Ministry of Health, as well as local authorities.
The donations distributed so far were 165 families from 3 communes: Boeung Dol commune, Angkor Reach commune and Sena Reach Udom, Preah Sdach district, and each family received 25 kg of rice and some money.
