Phnom Penh Forestry Administration Planted Trees in New Lot Community in Prek Pnov District to Contribute to Climate Change Prevention
(Phnom Penh): About 200 saplings were planted by the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration at a location in the new plot community, Samrong Tbong Village, Sangkat Samrong, Khan Prek Pnov, to serve as a wind barrier and a green cover to prevent climate change on the planet.
At the same time, the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration also called on the community to plant trees together, and if there is a shortage of seedlings, please make a request to the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration.
This was stated by Mr. Koam Seiha, Director of Phnom Penh Forestry Administration and during the tree planting ceremony in Dey Thmey Community, Samrong Tbong Village, Sangkat Samrong, Khan Prek Pnov, Phnom Penh this morning, December 25, 2020.
Koam Seiha, director of the Phnom Penh Forestry Administration, said that trees are important in helping to preserve the environment in this community as a wind barrier, especially to be more green and beautiful, help reduce climate change on the planet. Get rid of toxins in the air.
He added that the trees also provide shade and help get rid of carbon dioxide in the air and increase oxygen. At the same time, he also asked the people to plant trees, if there is a shortage of seedlings can ask the Forestry Administration to distribute.
(Phnom Penh): Following the instructions of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, 3 roads in Chamkar Mon district will be repaired after being damaged by rain to facilitate traffic for people to work. Journey.
In fact, this morning, December 25, 2020, Mr. Theng Sothol, Governor of Chamkar Mon District, with the participation of the Deputy Governor, the Director of Khan Administration, relevant offices, Sangkat Boeung Trabek Administration, Boeung Trabek Police Station and relevant officials inspected the site. Repairing AC rubber on Street 99 from Street 432 to Street 484 in Sangkat Boeung Trabek, Khan Chamkar Morn, which is a project of Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
Mr. Theng Sothol said that for the project to repair the road after being damaged by heavy rains in Chamkar Mon district, there are 3 lines, including Street 99, Street 294 and Street 432 next to Boeung Trabek, Toul Tum Poung I, Toul Tum Poung. Second and Tonle Bassac Sangkat.
For December 25, according to the instructions of Mr. Khuong Sreng, the team has been repairing with 5 cm thick AC rubber on Street 99, 940 meters long, 9 meters wide, from Street 432 to Street 484. In Sangkat Boeung Trabek, Khan Chamkar Morn, which is a project of Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
He said that in the past, as long as the construction site to repair or build roads in Chamkar Mon district, as the district governor, he always disseminated to the people with the opening of public forums for the people to cooperate and Mention the issues they want.
The district governor also requested the people living on both sides of the road who are in the process of repairing to cooperate with anything that has an impact on the road and sidewalks. Goes smoothly and is ready as planned.
On behalf of the people of Chamkar Mon district, Mr. Theng Sothol expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Mr. Khuong Sreng for instructing to repair and rehabilitate all the infrastructure damaged by the floods. Khan in Phnom Penh. Court Sentences 3 Murderers to Motorbike in Sak Sampov Commune
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ouk Sovannrith, Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, this morning, December 25, 2020, held a hearing to announce the verdict in the case of the murder and robbery of 29-year-old Mek Phin on October 16, 2019. At 06:30 on a rice field road in Khva village, Sak Sampov commune, Dangkor district, each person was sentenced to 18 years in prison.
Please be reminded that the police arrested 3 suspects in this operation under the guidance and direction of Lieutenant General, Director of the Criminal Police Department, the Office of Serious Crimes led in cooperation with the Office of Serious Affairs, Police Inspectorate, Po Sen Chey District Police Inspectorate, Dangkor District Police Inspectorate. Of Phnom Penh Municipal Police.
Please be reminded that a man was found dead in the middle of the road in Kvit village, Sak Sampov commune, Dangkor district, Phnom Penh, on suspicion of murder and robbery of a motorcycle. 30 am, October 16, 2019.
According to the police, the body of the man named Mek Phin, 29 years old, who works as a glassblower and runs a motodup, lives in a rented house around Jinchuri Plaza Market, Po Sen Chey District, and was born in Samkly Village, Prek Khla Commune, Koh Andat District, Takeo Province.
According to the relatives of the man, the victim rode a 2015 Dream Serey motorcycle from home and disappeared at 8 pm on October 15, 2019, but could not be reached until the morning of the 16th. The victim was beaten to death and his motorcycle was stolen.
