150 Poor, Elderly, Disabled and Orphans in Koh Nhek District Receive Donations from Mondulkiri Provincial Governor
(Mondulkiri): To help solve the needs of the people who are experiencing shortages while Cambodia is plagued by Kovid-19 this afternoon, December 24, 2020, Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Mondulkiri Province. Conversation and bring gifts in the form of food and some supplies to the poor, the elderly, the disabled, orphans, 150 families in 5 communes in Koh Nhek district.
Speaking on that occasion, Mr. Svay Sam Eang brought greetings and greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who always cares and cares for the general public, especially the people. Poor people, the elderly, widows, orphans, the disabled, and other distressed families, regardless of political affiliation.
The provincial governor added that bringing donations to the affected people now is to contribute to solving the needs of the people to a certain extent, especially for them to be able to grow crops and engage in other businesses. .
According to the Director of the Department of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Fitness, Mondulkiri Province, Mr. Khem Sophon, said that 150 families, equivalent to 5 communes in Koh Nhek district, each family received donations, including: rice. 15 kg, 1 mat, 1 blanket, 1 fishing rod, 4 bottles of fish sauce.
Separately, Mrs. Yean Dina, wife of the provincial governor and president of the Provincial Scout Association of Cambodia, donated 20,000 Riels per family and the Provincial Peace Youth Coalition also donated 150 winter coats.
