Ministry of Public Works and Administration of Preah Vihear Province Calls on Relevant Departments to Actively Participate in Road Traffic Accident Reduction Plan
He made the call during a meeting to review the implementation of the 11-month road safety action plan for Preah Vihear province for 11 months, which was held at the Preah Vihear Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport in the afternoon. December 24, 2020, with the participation of representatives of the National Police, representatives of relevant departments around the province.
On that occasion, Mr. Samleang Try, representative of Mr. Prak Sovann, stated that under the leadership of Mr. Prak Sovann, road infrastructure, especially roads in the provincial town, is being developed to serve the interests of the people, especially in order to participate. Reduce traffic accidents in the province.
Mr. Samleang Try also said that the issue of road traffic safety requires that all of us who are road users must respect each other, not to be separated from the problem of speed limit signs from road problems. No matter the traffic signal, it is important to be mindful when traveling on the road.
Mr. Samleang Try also mentioned that in response to the 8-point action plan of the National Road Safety Committee, the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, as well as the provincial authority, the Provincial Road Safety Secretariat has educated and disseminated the new road traffic law to Civil servants, the armed forces, teachers, students and people throughout Preah Vihear province.
