(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance on December 24, 2020, launched a series of remote training courses (Zoom Video System) on 'Public Procurement, Budget Implementation Procedures, Programs for Budget Units and Internal Audit'. Target participants who are civil servants in charge of relevant work of ministries and institutions.
The purpose of this training is to strengthen the capacity and increase the awareness of the officers in charge of procurement, budgeting, accounting and internal audit to contribute to the promotion of transparency, accountability, efficiency and effectiveness of the work. According to the technical principles and in accordance with the legal documents in force and within the framework of the public financial management reform program - the third phase of the Royal Government.
The opening ceremony was held under the leadership of Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Capacity Building Working Group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and was attended by leaders of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, trainers and a total of 90 participants. People.
