Two Tampuan Indigenous Communities in Vern Sai District, Ratanakkiri Province Receive 15 Collective Land Titles
(Rattanakiri): Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Rattanakiri Province and Chairman of the Provincial State Land Management Committee, on December 24, 2020, handed over the Certificate of Collective Land Ownership to the Tampuan Indigenous Communities in two villages: Rok and La Lai villages are located in Kok Lak commune, Vern Sai district.
Mr. Ly Usaphea, Director of the Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs of Ratanakkiri Province, said that the distribution of certificates of collective ownership of indigenous communities in Tampuon to Rok and Lalai villages, Kok Lak commune, Vern Sai district now has a certificate. A total of 15 plots of land on an area of 12,259,196 hectares.
Mr. Thong Savun considered this collective land title that the community received as a very important document as a document representing the entire community property, a document representing the exclusive right of the owner of his land to actually use and enjoy it. Respectively.
He said that the land that the parents and siblings have collectively registered in the land register and received the title deed meets the solid foundation conditions guaranteed by the state and protected by law and is also an important condition for the use of the title deed.
Collective registration, therefore, is to strengthen the security of sustainable land and natural resource tenure in the community, which will promote the potential use of land, and this has certainly ended land disputes and disputes between villages, in particular. Poverty reduction, which is the Royal Government's policy to promote land registration for indigenous peoples in Cambodia.
At the same time, the provincial governor also mentioned the policy of indigenous development of the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, which has improved the living standards of indigenous people. By harmonizing in Cambodia as well.
At the same time, he also commended the land registration team and all stakeholders who worked hard to achieve this task responsibly and transparently, and instructed the people of the indigenous communities in both villages to take care of it. Preserve this collective title and be united in the community, preserve all land that is registered and used sustainably for future generations.
