APSARA Authority completes the renovation of the Elephant Temple on the ridge of Kulen Mountain
(Siem Reap): The Department of Preservation of Temples Outside Angkor Park of the APSARA Authority has completed the restoration of the Damrei Krab Temple on Phnom Kulen, which is in a state of disrepair. The walls were cracked, and the front door frame collapsed, and parts of the roof were damaged.
These damages are caused by human factors, nature and age, which are the main causes, such as criminals digging the foundations of the temple, the roots of the trees tore the walls and roof of the temple, and some trees fell on the temple.
During the restoration work, the team strengthened the decaying branches at the four corners, prepared the western part that collapsed, sprayed the seedlings and cleaned the tree roots that grew on the walls and roof of the temple to stop the growth of trees.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on the afternoon of December 24, 2020, chaired a meeting to disseminate and discuss the work of collecting agricultural statistics and summarizing the work of cultivating the rainy season 2020. Organized by the General Department of Agriculture.
The meeting was also attended by the directors of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries across 25 capitals and provinces and officials.
The Minister said that agricultural statistics play an important role in the development of the agricultural sector as well as the overall economic development because it is an indicator that can analyze and reflect the changes and take measures to prevent any inactivity. Affects short-term and long-term agricultural development projects or programs, including measures to prevent "supply-demand imbalances".
The minister said that every year, the ministry prepares and disseminates statistical documents on annual agricultural crops, all of which are extracted and summarized based on the survey report of the department. Agricultural crop statistics were collected based on the combination of rainy season (April to October) and dry season (November to March).
Mr. Ngin Chhay, Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Agriculture, said that the results of the 2020 census of agricultural crops achieved the following results:
Taking this opportunity, the Minister gave additional instructions to the leaders of the General Department of Agriculture, Departments and all professional officials with relevant content:
First, the General Department of Agriculture shall facilitate the compilation of agricultural crop production data from 2020, starting from January 1 and ending on December 31 of each year, ie adding the dry season data with the rainy season data. .
Fourth, the Department shall report on the cultivation of rice, short-term horticulture and short-term industrial crops (seasonal crops) daily, weekly, quarterly, semi-annually and annually in an effective and transparent manner.
Fifth, the Department shall report on the cultivation of long-term horticultural crops and long-term industrial crops quarterly, semi-annually and annually.
Sixth, the General Department and the Department shall coordinate and collect data on agricultural crops at the household level, investment and economic land concession companies in all aspects.
Seventh, the Department shall coordinate to record the unofficial export of agricultural products in each province on the main crops and report to the General Department of Agriculture on a daily basis, as well as to cooperate in controlling the import of agricultural products through various border crossings.
Eighth, the General Department of Agriculture and the Department of Statistical Planning must set up a clear data collection system in all aspects to make statistics more accurate.
Ninth: The department must report all kinds of data in the prescribed format to the relevant institutions in a timely and consistent manner.
