However, in this case, Major General Sok Samnang, Takeo Provincial Police Commissioner, admitted that this case really happened when he went to crack down on drugs, as the suspect had been following for a long time. "This is a case of drug crackdown, but our officers did not go down to seize drugs, but to kidnap people for money," he said.
According to the Takeo provincial commissioner, he is setting up a working group to investigate the matter, and if he finds any wrongdoing, he will discipline the forces, such as reducing his strength, and if he finds serious wrongdoing, he will ask for higher principles so that his superiors can You decide.
The victim said that after sending him to the provincial commissioner, the police officers asked his family to give him another $ 2,000 in exchange for his release. Also threatened him not to share this information further.
