(Phnom Penh): On December 23, 2020, the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud "KPR" The Ministry of Commerce has brought two mobile food test vehicles to operate at two different locations, Orussey Market and Chbar Ampov Market, to check the compliance of food products.
In this operation, the specialized officers of the General Department of the DPRK Instantly inspected and analyzed samples in 50 mobile food laboratory vehicles at Orussey Market and 52 samples at Chbar Ampov Market, including bubble bean, dried fish, swollen fish, sausage, prahok, fish, squid, fish, shrimp, meatball Beef and many other vegetables.
As a result, officials found 8.5 kilograms of soybean foam containing the banned chemical boracic acid, while other samples did not detect the presence of banned chemicals. In that, the professional officer also confiscated and searched for the source of the production location to continue the legal procedure.
