Takeo and Kampot Provincial Departments of Agriculture Confirm Causes of Duck Egg Prices and Confirm No Imports from Neighboring Countries
(Phnom Penh): The Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Takeo and Kampot Provinces issued a press release on December 23, 2020, confirming some of the main reasons for the drop in local prices and claiming that The drop in the price of duck eggs is not imported from neighboring countries, especially Vietnam.
Confirmation of the reason for the drop in the price of duck eggs came after the people recently reacted to the fall in the price of duck eggs, which cost 300 riel per egg and below 300 riel per egg.
According to a press release from the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampot and Takeo Provinces, obtained by Fresh News on the evening of December 23, 2020, the factors that led to the fall in duck egg prices were due to:
1: This season is rich in natural fish.
2: The production of duck eggs and salted duck eggs decreased with the demand of customers decreased.
3: Demand to Phnom Penh and other provinces decreased.
4: Demand for restaurant supply decreased due to the lack of customers.
5. According to the weather conditions in Cambodia in the autumn and rich in food in the fields and dry areas, which makes ducks produce more eggs than in other seasons.
6. The General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, as well as the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, have never allowed the import of eggs from neighboring countries, especially Vietnam, to the Cambodian market.
7: In case the traders who raise animals, especially raising chickens and ducks and eggs, know the information about the smuggling of duck eggs and chickens from neighboring countries, please contact the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampot Province by phone number 017 803 007, 017 842 403 and 012 603 303 for the Department to intervene to suppress the crime of animal movement and animal products in accordance with the law on animal health and animal production.
Meanwhile, the current situation of raising ducks in Takeo province is about 1,128,544, of which about 80% of the eggs are raised and produce about 700,000 eggs per day and supply hatcheries in 76 provinces. Location and use in the province, in addition to supply to Phnom Penh and the provinces.
Separately, for the price of duck eggs, there are two types, in which male eggs cost 250 riel-300 riel per egg and male eggs cost 250 riel -280 riel per egg, which is similar to the price of duck eggs in Vietnam.
