This is according to the press release of the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the results of the meeting to monitor and balance the implementation of the cash support program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19, which was held on the morning of the 23rd. This December 2020.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and Chairman of the Working Group on Policy, Budget, Finance and Social Assistance to manage the fight against Kovid-19.
The meeting reviewed and discussed the results of monitoring and balancing the implementation of the cash subsidy program for poor and vulnerable families during the fight against Kovid-19, which the Royal Government has announced to be implemented since the 24th of this month. June 2020 ago.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth also instructed the team to prepare this report to study and analyze more thoroughly, focusing on some key issues to find solutions and improve any gaps, such as issues related to identification. Benefit, etc., which may deviate from the principles of the Royal Government.
He added that the results of this study also need to find out about the options and recommendations in terms of policies and mechanisms to implement the program. In particular, the impact of the program on the economy and society, as well as the livelihoods and lifestyles of the people who are the beneficiaries.
It should be noted that the results of this study show that 99.1% of poor households who receive government subsidies are very satisfied because this cash subsidy program is implemented at a time when living conditions are difficult and the families receive The results also show satisfaction with the verification and withdrawal procedures.
Regarding the implementation of the program, the results show that most of the officers and village-commune chiefs have been informed and instructed on the implementation process of the program, such as: statute of identification of poor families, use of computers, Solve urgent problems and understanding of the statute: beneficiaries, although the understanding of commune officials is different, especially in remote rural areas.
