In a report released on Tuesday, CPJ said that by 2020, a total of 30 journalists had been killed while on duty while leading an investigation into the deaths of 15 other journalists. Whether they died because of a job as a journalist or not.
The Committee to Protect Journalists (CPJ) also expressed shock at the case of journalist Ruhollah Zam, who was executed by Iranian authorities on December 12 for covering anti-government protests in 2017. Iran accuses it of inciting opposition and attempts to overthrow the Tehran government.
According to the CPJ, the number of journalists killed in the war in 2020 is the lowest since 2000. The decline is due to restrictions on travel around the world to prevent the spread of COVID-19. Only three journalists were killed in the war, all three in Syria. Mexico remains the most dangerous country for journalists.
Major General Men Ly announces donation of 5,000,000 Riels to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to purchase Kovid-19 vaccine
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the evening of December 7, 2020 announced the provision of funds for the purchase of vaccines to be given to the people for free as the first step of 1,000,000 doses to inject people. About 500,000 people.
Local media have criticized the government for being too lax in ensuring the safety of vaccines and relying heavily on locally developing vaccines that will take longer than foreign vaccine options.
In response, the South Korean president's office on Tuesday issued a statement saying the vaccination program would begin soon. The government has already confirmed that vaccination will begin in early February 2021.
On Wednesday, South Korea recorded an additional 1,092 new cases, bringing the total to 52,550, according to the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (KDCA). 739 people died. In the face of such a sharp increase, Seoul and surrounding areas have announced a ban on gatherings of more than five people, which will take effect from December 23 to January 3, 2021.
In addition, restaurant and shop owners could face fines of up to 3 million won (about $ 2,700) if found violating the regulations. South Korean authorities have also ordered the closure of all ski resorts and winter destinations in an effort to stop the outbreak during the upcoming Christmas and New Year holidays.
(Phnom Penh): In recent days, many people have been going to make prahok along the Tonle Sap River, a fishing pole in Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province, while the fish are coming down from the Tonle Sap Lake.
