Experts continue to find chemicals in 7 kilos of soybean foam and 9 kilos of noodles at Kralokor market, Svay Rieng province
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Pheng Nil, Branch Manager of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud in Svay Rieng Province, this morning, December 23, 2020, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce, local authorities inspected goods at Kralokor District Market. Svay Chrum, Svay Rieng Province.
According to Mr. Pheng Nil, the inspection team inspected the food at the stalls in some markets and used the first test kits on 36 samples of food to find banned chemicals that are harmful to health. Citizens.
At the same time, the Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud Officer also advertised and distributed stickers to traders to understand the products with the correct labeling.
He said that as a result, after the work, the professional officers found goods containing chemicals such as: 7 kg of soybeans containing Borax and 9 kg of noodles containing chemicals, as well as milk for AD babies. After the expiration date, the professional officer made a record of confiscating the goods and storing them for later incineration.
Mr. Pheng Nil called on traders who are vendors to cooperate with professional officials to test for banned chemicals in food and expired goods in order to improve the well-being of the people.
Farmers growing vegetables, hair and cabbage in Sangkat Kampong Svay, Serey Sophorn City complain about the harvest and sell it cheap
(Banteay Meanchey): Ta Sak and Cabbage are a kind of vegetable that has a good market and is not difficult to grow and take care of. In particular, this year, due to the crisis of 19 communicable diseases, buyers were silenced, and the market was flooded, making it difficult for farmers to harvest and sell at low prices.
Tum Thoeuy, 48, a resident of Pong Ro village, Kampong Svay commune, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province, said that this year the sale of vegetables in the market was cheaper as she and her family worked hard to grow crops.
Sik Siek, a 30-year-old cabbage farmer, also complained that he did not lose much to cucumber growers, stating that usually only during the cold season, good weather, combined with the Kovid 19 crisis, especially in other villages. Planted at the same time, this is why it is so expensive. At present, a good type of kale costs 800 riel, if normally 500 riel.
In addition, they complained about the loss of cultivation by spending a lot of energy, materials, budget to rent and buy a lot of fertilizer, spraying, until the harvest and when there is no market and sell. At a lower price.
(Phnom Penh): A storm of criticism has been circulating on Facebook in recent days due to falling egg prices. The storm of criticism hit the Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon.
During a visit to the Tonle Sap Collection of prahok fish on December 22, 2020, Mr. Veng Sakhon did not hesitate to criticize him for some of his words.
The minister explained that the flooding of duck eggs and up to the drop in prices was due to a number of factors, such as the implementation of measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, leading to various ceremonies being suspended, and the demand for restaurants, restaurants and some hotels being reduced. At the same time, freshwater fish are abundant, leading people to reduce their consumption of duck eggs.
With the fall in egg prices, this has led to some speculation that the fall in prices is due to the import of duck eggs from neighboring countries. Especially from Vietnam.
Responding to this, Mr. Veng Sakhon confirmed and confirmed that after the complaints of the people, he immediately sent professional officers to study the price of duck eggs in Cambodia and in Vietnam. According to the study, the price of duck eggs in Cambodia and Vietnam is similar and Vietnam is slightly more expensive than Cambodia.
The reason given by the Minister is to emphasize that no trader imports duck eggs from Vietnam to Cambodia at a similar price.
"What we have seen is that there is no import phenomenon, and at the same time we have confirmed that the fishing season is right, people are reducing their consumption, and at the same time, the General Department has announced that in case any people check that "Any illegal imports must be reported immediately to the General Department of Animal Production, animal health immediately." This is the confirmation of the Minister of Agriculture.
The minister called on egg farmers to report to the Ministry of Agriculture to arrest traders who smuggled in duck eggs because the ministry did not allow traders to import duck eggs.
