National Bank of Cambodia and Laos vow to further strengthen traditional bilateral cooperation and relations
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia and the Central Bank of Laos are committed to further strengthening and expanding traditional cooperation and bilateral relations for the benefit of the two countries located in villages along the fence.
Bilateral meetings between the two central banks are held annually with the aim of strengthening bilateral cooperation and relations, aiming to contribute to the development of the financial and economic sectors and friendly relations between the two countries.
During the meeting, the two sides exchanged views on the economic situation, the conduct of monetary policy, banking supervision, especially policies and measures taken by the two countries during the negative impact of the Kovid-19 epidemic.
The Central Bank of Laos and the National Bank of Cambodia have played an important role in mitigating the impact on the economy by maintaining price stability and implementing a monetary policy to support the banking sector's liquidity in economic activity.
At the same time, the two central banks have also contributed to alleviating the burden of the poor and companies suffering from declining revenues by easing a number of regulations that enable banks and financial institutions to restructure credit. .
The two central banks also praised the progress of bilateral cooperation, which has contributed to the strengthening of professional capacity through the exchange of knowledge and skills and strengthen the development of the banking and economic sectors of the two countries.
Please note that currently two Cambodian commercial banks are present in Laos and have grown significantly. The Central Bank of Laos highly appreciates measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and the effectiveness of the National Bank of Cambodia's policy to support economic activity.
The Central Bank of Laos thanked the National Bank of Cambodia for providing technical assistance to the Central Bank of Laos in the past and requested to expand the scope of cooperation in addition to sharing experiences on payment systems, especially Bakong and technology. Finance.
