Amazing! Two boys and a girl asked their mother to visit them and drowned in Banteay Meanchey province
The family went to find the body at 12 noon on December 22, 2020 at Klong Chik O Thom in Reaksmey Samaki village, Sangkat Nimit, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
Local police said the bodies of the victims were identified as Mao Dao, a 5-year-old boy, and Vong Vida, a 6-year-old girl. The two children are cousins and live in Reaksmey Samaki village, Sangkat Nimit, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province.
Police said that according to the description of the mother of the victim, Chum Srey Tha, 36 years old, told the authorities that before the incident, her son, Vong Vida, asked her to kiss him and take a shower. Compassionate siblings who previously did not kiss their mother.
Overwhelmed, he agreed to take a shower for a while, then saw the two children come back up and take a shower in the house, remembering that the two children heard their mouths in the pool. His house is not interested, continue to cut grass growing near the house.
After a while, his mouth disappeared and he went to the pool and asked his grandmother to go to the bakery. She could not find the clothes at the mouth of the stream. Then find another nephew.
Local police confirmed that after finding the two children and the parents took the children to the district health center, doctors said that both children were dead.
Undeterred, the parents continued to take the two children to the Poipet City Referral Hospital. Doctors said that the two children had lost their lives and were exhausted to take their children to prepare for the traditional festival with great sadness.
