Colonel Prohm Yorn confirmed that the six fires occurred:
* Second time: Occurred along Street 217, Sangkat Steung Meanchey III, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh, by burning and destroying the location of Ouk Thuk Sen seat, but the owner was able to extinguish it without spreading.
* Third time: Occurred along National Road 5, Sangkat Chrang Chamres I, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh. As for the cause of the electric shock, 4 vehicles were used, 3 vehicles were used by the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and 1 vehicle was not used by Russey Keo District Hall.
* 4th time: Occurred along Street 528, corner of Street 339, Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, by burning and destroying power lines and light poles. The cause of the explosion was a fire truck.
* 5th time: Occurred on the corner of Street 528 and Street 337, Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, by burning and destroying power lines and light poles. The cause of the explosion was a fire truck.
* The 6th time: It happened behind Bak Touk High School, Sangkat Veal Vong, Khan 7 Makara, Phnom Penh. In this case, 5 people were seriously injured in 2 men and 2 women were seriously injured and were taken to rescue Emergency at the hospital while three other women suffered minor injuries.
As for the cause of the explosion of the gas tank, in which 8 vehicles were used, including 7 vehicles of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and 1 vehicle of Olympic Market.
At the same time, Colonel Prohm Yorn, Director of the Fire Prevention Office, also urged all residents to be extremely careful, especially during this windy season to pay close attention to incense, candles and electricity. Properly before leaving home.
