(Kampot): Mr. Chiao Tay, Governor of Kampot Province, chaired a meeting to mediate a long-running land dispute in Mak Prang commune, Teuk Chhou district, using a win-win strategy, leaving both parties without winners and losers. On December 22, 2020 at the meeting hall of Kampot Provincial Hall, with the participation of the working group of professional institutions and relevant authorities, as well as the people who are land disputes.
After years of filing a lawsuit in court, the disputing parties, who are relatives of the family, seized more than two hectares of land in Bot Kbal Damrey village, Mak Prang commune, Teuk Chhou district, province. Kampot turned to the provincial administration for intervention in early December 2020.
After inspecting and meeting with the relevant authorities of the conflicting parties, Mr. Chiao Tai, Provincial Governor, held a meeting to mediate the dispute between Sok Ngyim, Okim and Chuy Sang, living in the above commune village again on 22 December. This year 2020.
As a result, after listening to the explanations of the relevant parties, the provincial governor used a win-win strategy to resolve disputes outside the court for both parties and agreed to divide the disputed land into two parts, including Ms. Chuy Sang agreed to accept 60% and Ms. Sok Ngyim agreed to accept 40% and the actual land survey will be done in the future.
At the same time, the provincial governor also said that on behalf of the provincial administration, he did not want to see any citizens arguing or suing each other in court, and as a provincial leader, he asked all citizens to be tolerant. High and resolve disputes outside the court system so as not to waste their time and money.
In case of any unresolved land dispute, the provincial governor encourages the people to submit a request for intervention to the provincial authorities first or can contact him directly to take action in a timely manner.
