An old dolphin weighing 200 kg in Kampi dolphin canyon dies
(Kratie): An old female dolphin weighing 201 kg at Kampi Dolphin Canyon in Kratie province died and was found by people on December 22, 2020.
Mr. Mok Ponlok, Director of Kratie Fisheries Administration District, said that he received information from the river guard team at Kampi Chroy Banteay Post, provided by Mr. Sao Sinoeun, a member of the Sambok fishing community, that a dolphin was found dead at Prek Khsor Phum. Sambok, Sabok commune, Chit Borey district.
Immediately after receiving this information, he assigned Mr. Tan Someth Bunwat, Deputy Director of Fisheries Administration in cooperation with WWF Kratie Province to inspect the above points. According to the actual situation, this large dolphin died about 1 day ago because the dolphin was still in good condition.
Mr. Mok Ponlok confirmed that the dolphin lives in the canyon ID-95, which weighs about 201 kg and is 230 cm long. Causes of death According to the physical examination, this dolphin is old because its teeth are worn on both the top and bottom, and there are no bruises or scratches on the dolphin's body and tail. After examination and measurement, the team decided to perform surgery to keep the sample at WWF.
