Mr. Keo Rattanak stated that "the top power substation is a fruitful achievement from the good cooperation between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the People's Republic of China in the development of the electricity sector contributes to the growth of the Cambodian economy." Cambodian, Vietnamese diplomats chair 18th Cambodia-Vietnam joint commission meeting
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 22, 2020, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, co-chaired a meeting with Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam Pham Binh Minh. The 18th Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Commission via video.
The 18th Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Commission Meeting focused on economic, cultural, scientific and technological cooperation. The meeting reviewed the progress made in accordance with the minutes of the 17th Cambodia-Vietnam Joint Commission Meeting in 2019 in Phnom Penh, and explored ways and means to further strengthen and expand the scope of Bilateral cooperation between the two countries in all fields.
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan, through its Embassy in Cambodia, has agreed to provide a total of US $ 288,473 to three Cambodian entities for the Japan Grants for Small-Scale Human Security Project (Kusanoni).
The signing ceremony was held on December 21, 2020 by Mr. Mikami Masahiro, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary of Japan to Cambodia and representatives of the three recipients.
The Japanese government-sponsored projects include:
* First: Medical Equipment Project at Angkor Borey Referral Hospital, Takeo Province (US $ 87,900) Recipient Unit: Prey Kabbas OD Office.
In this project, one X-ray machine, one ultrasound camera and one generator will be equipped at Angkor Borey Referral Hospital, Takeo Province. Hospitals are currently unable to adequately diagnose their patients due to a lack of equipment. Through this plan, about 1,500 patients will receive improved medical services every year.
* Second: Project to equip stamps in special schools in Phnom Penh and 3 provinces (budget $ 96,726) Recipient: Krousar Thmey.
Under this project, four printers and four recording devices will be installed at special schools in Phnom Penh, Kampong Cham, Siem Reap and Battambang. The project is expected to help more than 210 students and teachers by improving the learning environment.
* Third: Project to install diagnostic equipment, hearing and communication services for children in Phnom Penh and 6 provinces (budget 103,847 USD) Recipient Unit: Ear Health Organization in Cambodia.
