(Phnom Penh): A cement truck was driving smoothly when the steering wheel fell off the road into the rice field upside down without knowing the reason, but fortunately did not cause any injuries to the driver or anyone else.
This incident happened at 11:30 noon on December 22, 2020 on the concrete road, Taphem village, Sangkat Kampol, Khan Kampol, Phnom Penh.
According to sources at the scene, the overturned cement truck, a red and white Hyundai with license plate number 5A-2971, was driven by a man. Prior to the accident, the vehicle was traveling on the concrete road from the south to the north. When it reached the scene, it oversteered and crashed into a field, regardless of whether Driving has no obstacles.
Fortunately, the driver or no one else was injured. After the incident, the police went to the scene immediately and the company pulled the car out of the scene by itself.
