(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries issued a press release on December 21, 2020 to explain the reasons for the drop in the price of duck eggs to below 300 Riels. 1 tablet.
According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on December 21, the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, as well as the Ministry of Agriculture, recently observed that the public, especially poultry farmers, participated. Comment with the Facebook account of Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries regarding the lower price of eggs in the market in recent days.
The case of eggs falling below 300 riel per egg in some areas is said to be due to the import of eggs from neighboring countries such as Vietnam, which makes the egg products produced locally. Cheap, unsold and very difficult to find a market.
In connection with this, the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production would like to inform the public that:
1. The General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, as well as the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, has never in principle allowed the import of eggs from neighboring countries, especially Vietnam, into the Cambodian market.
2: The price of duck eggs for hatching compared to Cambodia with Vietnam, that is, the price is similar. In Cambodia, normal non-fertilized duck eggs cost 280 riel per egg, while in Vietnam it costs 300 riel per egg.
3. Kovid 19 is threatening public health and rallies have been suspended, maximizing egg demand as egg-laying is on the rise across the country. During the fishing season, some people turn to eating fish instead of bird eggs.
4: In case the traders who raise animals, especially raising chickens and ducks and eggs, know about the smuggling of chicken and duck eggs from neighboring countries, please contact the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production at 012 828 209 to intervene. Suppress crimes of animal movement and animal products in accordance with the law on animal health and animal production.
