The trial was held at the White Building of the Chamkar Mon State Palace, presided over by Dr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council and President of the Trial Chamber. Mr. Im Chhun Lim examined and decided on 28 cases, from Case No. 363/005/2020 to No. 390/032/2020 of members and agents of the Coalition for Democracy Party who appealed against the decision of the National Election Committee. Involved in the initial voter list.
According to a statement from the Constitutional Council, the hearing was attended by 12 plaintiffs representing the Coalition for Democracy, as well as four representatives of the National Election Committee and the general public. In these 28 cases, the Trial Chamber of the Constitutional Council ruled as follows:
* Received all 28 complaints in the legal form, but rejected them in violation of the law.
* Reserve the decision of the National Election Committee as a whole.
* This decision is a final decision, closes the way for protests and has the power to apply to all the powers stated in the Constitution and must be published in the Government.
(Phnom Penh): General Kiet Chantharith, Director General of the General Department of Immigration of the Ministry of Interior, on December 21, 2020, issued a directive on measures to prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 to all border police officers. Especially the gates along the Cambodian-Thai border.
* First, must continue to work closely with officials of the Ministry of Health to check, especially the entry of foreign visitors and Cambodians who come from Thailand thoroughly, requiring them to do the right thing.
* Second: Take care to control and patrol the left wing and right wing in the jurisdiction of the gate clearly and must stop passengers, especially Cambodians who come from Thailand to be handed over to health agency officials to control Do a thorough health check-up and do a sedative.
* Third, take care to instruct and remind the immigration police officers who are stationed at the gates to take care to keep the distance between individuals, keep clean, wash their hands with soap and alcohol or be careful of the transmission of passengers who come to God Kingdom of Cambodia. Banteay Srei District Administration to Hold Model House Contest as Preah Dak Village Becomes Model Village on Environmental Aesthetics
(Siem Reap): The Banteay Srei District Administration of Siem Reap Province will hold a competition for clean houses in the future as Preah Dak villagers' houses are becoming a model village for other villages in Banteay Srei district due to the cleanliness of this village. And well organized, especially on the streets.
If we travel to Preah Dak village, we will immediately notice the problem of garbage, noting that there is almost no garbage, because each house has a trash can in front of each house, what is special is the planting of flowers. More in front of the house. At night, the village is bright.
Regarding this model village, Mr. Khim Finang, Governor of Banteay Srei District, said: "Our district is a tourist district, so cleanliness and hygiene must go hand in hand for tourists to visit here."
According to the young district governor, there are 36 villages in Banteay Srei district that he controls, and what makes Banteay Srei district clean and free of garbage is due to the participation of the people and the activities of the village-commune authorities as well as the youth force. Volunteer to educate local people about the importance of environmental sanitation.
At the same time, he also said that "the organization of the village has made the connection between cleanliness and economic value to the villagers until now for almost a year. In the future, there will be a clean house competition until the clean house race in Banteay Srei district.
However, the district governor also confirmed that everything is possible from the Ministry of Environment, and as a tourist district, the district administration is committed to continuing to clean up everywhere.
According to the young district governor, the district administration is also having a special garbage collection mechanism, which is to fine people who do not follow the district administration's instructions.
"We can not walk around collecting garbage for free," he said. In Preah Dak village, the district administration is considering a self-governing community project by having workers walk around collecting garbage, with villagers giving it to garbage collectors. ”
He said that so far there is no charge for garbage collection, but in the future there will be a special focus on traders in the market and in people's homes is to think later. At the same time, the district governor also added that it is not yet known how much garbage was collected per day, but incineration is about 10 to 15 tons per day.
According to Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, the Ministry of Environment has supported environmental clean-up activities in Banteay Srei district, Siem Reap province, in line with the government's policy to the sub-national level.
"We appreciate the Banteay Srei district administration, as well as the people who have participated in the implementation of good solid waste management, including the decoration to make it more attractive," he said.
The senior official of the Ministry of Environment also said that the Ministry of Environment has helped the district administration with materials and techniques, including providing incinerators and cars in the community for convenience. This is part of strengthening the responsibility of citizens and local leaders in the management of solid waste and garbage.
