(Phnom Penh): General Dr. Neth Savoeun, General Commissioner of the National Police, has ordered the traffic police in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap to resume traffic law enforcement after a 15-day suspension after the incident. Community 28 November ", which is the first case of Kovid-19 infection in the community.
On the morning of December 21, 2020, General Him Yan, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, told Fresh News that after a 15-day suspension from December 1 to 15, 2020, due to In the case of Kovid-19, General Neth Savoeun instructed the traffic police to continue to enforce traffic restrictions as usual.
General Him Yan stated, "This period of suspension is 15 days from December 1-15, and from December 16, His Excellency General Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner General, ordered Police in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap have resumed enforcement of traffic laws, while other provinces have not been suspended, so far.
The reaffirmation of General Him Yan after the suspicion and question that in the past there were instructions to suspend the implementation of traffic laws in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap until a new notification, but no notification. Suddenly, the police began to tighten traffic laws and impose fines again.
