Thailand spends nearly 2 million USD to build a trade link between Tha Sen village in Trat province and Thmor Da in Veal Veng district, Pursat province
(Pursat): The Thai side is currently constructing a 14-meter-wide, 1.9-kilometer-long AC commercial asphalt road with four lanes between the border checkpoints in Tha Sen village, Lem Kat commune, Moeung district, Trat province. Thailand to National Road 55 (Thmor Da) in Sangkum Thmey Village, Thmor Da Commune, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province, Cambodia, using the provincial development budget for 2020 totaling 51,737,000 baht, approximately 2 million USD.
The decision to build the trade route came after the Thai Parliament approved it and after Mr. Chhat Prachai Phornmonlard, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior of the Kingdom of Thailand, signed the request of the Governor of Trat Province on November 27, 2019. With the acceleration of the opening of this international border crossing.
