Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has assigned the Ministry of Environment to review and study, test and implement the payment of ecosystem services with stakeholders and prepare a policy of payment for ecosystem services for the Royal Government to review and decide.
According to the senior official, the Ministry of Environment and stakeholders, especially at the sub-national level, as provincial PES implementers, have decided on the mechanism of implementation and fundraising by choosing the appropriate option to implement PES in the mountains. Kulen: First, the voluntary contribution of large water users (businesses), and second: the payment of taxes on commercial water use, including producers and distributors.
He added that "the funds raised from this implementation will go to the Environmental and Social Fund, which is managed by the Ministry of Environment to be able to use to protect the ecosystem in Phnom Kulen." "Phnom Kulen National Park in Siem Reap and Kbal Chhay Multi-use Areas in Sihanoukville are two locations that the Royal Government has decided to pilot on an ecosystem payment plan."
It is believed that the water from Phnom Kulen is Amret water and some scientific studies have also shown that the water from Phnom Kulen is good quality water for human consumption.
Secretary of State Neth Pheaktra stressed that in order to sustainably provide ecosystem services in Phnom Kulen National Park, especially water from Phnom Kulen, it is necessary to protect and preserve Phnom Kulen ecosystems, such as prevention of deforestation, reforestation and systems. Natural water lost and damaged function to prevent pollution of rivers and groundwater.
Ms. Chan Somaly, Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Environment, in charge of Biodiversity, said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has assigned the Ministry of Environment to review and study the implementation of ecosystem fees with stakeholders and to develop a policy for system fees. This ecosystem for the Royal Government to review and decide.
