Mr. Sakhoeun Sakda added that while on the ridge of Kulen Mountain, there are ancient pools and dams with an area of more than 100 hectares. Geographically, Phnom Kulen is located in the heart of Siem Reap province. What is more special is that water flows from the mountain into the Angkor area, which has a western baray that stores about 111 million cubic meters of water for farmers to use for irrigation. Other crops will flow to the Tonle Sap Lake as well.
