WASHINGTON, Dec. 19 (Xinhua) - US President Donald Trump on Saturday claimed that the recent large-scale cyber-attacks on the US government did not appear to have caused any serious problems, as things were under control. Yes, he also contradicted his own administration's assessment that Russia was behind the move. This is according to a quote from the AFP news agency on Sunday, December 20, 2020.
Donald Trump's claim is in stark contrast to Secretary of State May Pompeo's remarks about the source and severity of the recent cyber-attacks on the United States. Pompeo said that according to experts, the attack could have deep repercussions and take months to fully resolve, while those behind it were clearly Russia's actions.
