Teuk Sap Market, Chhnuk Trou Commune, Kampong Chhnang Province, Completed, Traders Cannot Negotiate
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Saing Kim Sorn, Chief of Chhnuk Trou Commune, announced that all the old traders in Chhnuk Trou Market should sell dollars in this market because the company has already done it. He said that those who can not afford to rent a stall can come to negotiate directly with the company to have the opportunity to have a stall in the market.
The commune chief confirmed that this year, the commune authorities received 15 hectares of sub-land from the state for development in the commune. Of that, 6 hectares of land was built as a fresh sea market in Chhnuk Trou commune, while the other 9 hectares were used as a port location, in which the port is divided into 3 types: tourist port, agricultural port and fish port.
Regarding the lease of stalls in Samuth Teuk Sap Market, Chhnuk Trou Commune, Mr. Lim Song, a representative of the investment company, stated that this Samuth Teuk Sap Market has 220 stalls for rent. Stall fees are set at $ 1,500 per stall for a period of three years. The monthly rent for the stall is $ 35 per month. As of today, 80% of the vendors have registered to rent the stalls.
The company representative stated that the deposit of $ 1,500 per stall was not a stall purchase price or stall rent, but a three-year sales guarantee. In the next three years, if any trader does not want to continue selling and wants to leave, the company will reimburse $ 1,500. However, this deposit is also deducted when any trader refuses to pay the company's monthly stall fee.
He added that traders who can not afford to pay the stall can come and register to negotiate directly with the company. When the research company finds that it is not possible, the company will help to provide stalls for sale in good faith.
