(Phnom Penh): Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Information Technology Project Management Team for Public Financial Management (FMIS), received a representative of the International Monetary Fund on December 18, 2020. (IMF) to discuss some of the work related to public financial management.
The IMF representative stressed the importance of the FMIS project, which countries around the world have been successfully implementing to build a foundation for improving the quality of public services through better budgeting and financial management. High efficiency.
Along with the revision of the Financial System Law, the IMF representative strongly recommended the Ministry of Economy and Finance to incorporate the content of the FMIS into the law as well as other developed countries in order to achieve a clear legal framework. For the use of this system in budget implementation and public financial management in Cambodia.
At the same time, the IMF representatives commended the hard work of the relevant departments, the General Secretariat of the Public Financial Management Reform Committee, and especially the Secretariat of the FMIS Project Management Team, which in addition to successfully implemented the action plan. The project has also worked to facilitate the smooth running of the IMF mission.
During the meeting, he asked the IMF to continue to support the implementation of the FMIS project in the next steps, especially the management of change and the sharing of experiences as a priority of the public financial management reform process.
