The United Kingdom is also an important trading partner for Cambodia in Europe. Cambodia's exports to Britain include clothing, footwear, bicycles, rice and other agricultural products.
Data recorded by the Ministry of Commerce confirms that in 2019, the trade volume between Cambodia and the United Kingdom reached 1,057 million US dollars, of which Cambodia exported more than 977 million US dollars to the United Kingdom and the United Kingdom imported nearly 80 million US dollars to Cambodia. .
In 2020, the trade volume decreased slightly. In the first 11 months of 2020, the trade volume between Cambodia and the United Kingdom was 813 million US dollars, of which Cambodia exported to the United Kingdom 766 million US dollars and the United Kingdom brought more than 46 million US dollars to Cambodia.
