"Van" lone elephant adapts well to new environment and regularly communicates with 3 female elephants after arriving in Cambodia
(Oddar Meanchey): The elephant named "Kavan", the loneliest elephant in the world, is finally no longer lonely and after being sent from Pakistan to live in the wildlife sanctuary of Cambodia since the 30th month November 2020 under the care of the Ministry of Environment and the Cambodian Wildlife Conservation Organization (CWS).
The spokesman for the Ministry of Environment pointed out that Cambodia has given new shelter, new life and new hope to this lonely elephant. Cavan, a 35-year-old male elephant, was rescued from a Pakistani zoo by a wildlife conservation group through legal action, and Pakistan's Supreme Court has finally decided to release him and release him. Natural forests of Cambodia's wildlife sanctuaries.
He said that the new home of the Elephant Cave in Cambodia has protected areas and all 68 biodiversity corridors of Cambodia. Cambodia is globally recognized for its rich biodiversity, including the most endangered and endangered species.
Meanwhile, the spokesman for the Ministry of Environment confirmed that the Kavan elephant is an endangered Asian elephant and that Cambodia has between 400 and 600 Asian elephants living in the protected forest. Of Cambodia in Ratanakkiri and Mondulkiri provinces and in the Cardamom Mountains. Cambodia also has more than 70 domestic elephants.
With the strict enforcement of law enforcement by the authorities and the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia to protect and conserve in the last 10 years, the level of crime of hunting wild elephants for ivory and tails to use the traditional beliefs. In Cambodia, there has been a sharp decline, almost none.
According to Oknha Sok Hong, President of the Cambodian Wildlife Sanctuary, through the rapid adaptation of the Cavan Elephants in the new Cambodian territory in the Kulen Prom Tep Wildlife Sanctuary, the Cavan will be in place for about three more months. May be released outside the cage like the other three female elephants to breed.
