Minister Lim Kean Hor orders officials to ban and take action against encroachment on state public canals in Svay Chrum commune, Khsach Kandal district
(Kandal): Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, ordered professional officers to cooperate with Kandal provincial authorities and relevant institutions to ban and take action against land grabbing, encroachment on state public canals and construction. Construction on the newly poured land in Svay Chrum commune, Khsach Kandal district.
A senior official of the Ministry of Water Resources told Fresh News on the afternoon of December 18, 2020 that after receiving a report on this case, Minister Lim Kean Hor ordered a professional officer to investigate and do this work immediately. To stop illegal activities.
The official added that in the face of action, the Minister has ordered the suspension of land grabbing, encroachment on canal land and summoned all relevant parties to come for questioning and resolve this issue.
It should be informed that the villagers of Svay Chrum, Svay Chrum commune, Khsach Kandal district reported on December 16, 2020 that they saw traders engaged in the sale of land and continued to pour soil in violation of the state's public canals. Owned and built on the newly poured land, although the local and district authorities to ban and prevent several times is not effective.
As for the encroachment on the state's canal land, the villagers reported that the local authorities had arbitrarily sold the land to the traders, and the traders used this reason to gradually violate the land until it was full and built. Solid construction.
Residents reported that they had dumped several meters of the canal and continued to build solid construction by December 16, 2020, if not stopped, the public canal would become private. No. According to previous reports, the authorities also went to ban, but the traders acted secretly at night.
According to the villagers, these traders have been clearing the land, taking some time during the day and some at night until it is completely cleared, and have started to build on the land to resell or rent. These traders bought without proper documents, only the signature of the commune chief, while the state canal food could not be owned by anyone.
Previously, Mr. Bun Pheng, the governor of Khsach Kandal district, asked the authorities to ban the landfilling of this canal and called the party to settle it until a contract was signed, but this person refused to sign the acknowledgment. The district governor only allowed officers to go down and stop, but could not prevent these abusive activities.
Regarding this issue, the people who enjoy the canal land have asked the provincial governor to help save it so that they can share it.
It should be informed that since the development in Svay Chrum, Khsach Kandal district, they often see corrupt traders vying for the ownership of public lake land, especially when they hear that they will cut this area into Phnom Penh. The encroachment on state land also occurred without any wires, while the people only asked the top level to help check this issue.
Ministry of Economy launches remote training course on strengthening governance of finance, climate change for gender equality
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of December 18, 2020, on the Zoom video system, the Ministry of Economy and Finance opened a training course on "Strengthening Governance of Finance, Climate Change for Gender Equality" for target trainees Technical of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, the Ministry of Rural Development and the General Department of Budget of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Dr. Hean Sahip, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Capacity Building Working Group of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Mr. Samuel Hurtig, Head of Cooperation Section, Swedish Embassy in Cambodia Chea Chanthou, Deputy Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the National Council for Sustainable Development.
He added that this training workshop will meet the specific needs of capacity building and development for the leaders and technical officials of the relevant ministries and institutions:
* The Science of Climate Change * Gender and Financial Relations Climate Change * National and International Policy for Response to Climate Change * Investment Project Evaluation Methods in the Context of Climate Change * Climate Change Finance for Cambodia And the universe.
These are all important foundations that Cambodian civil servants need to understand more in order to improve the implementation of better and more effective in order to contribute to the implementation of national political programs, especially the development of infrastructure and logical systems of the Royal Government.
In particular, Hartis stated that Sweden will continue to support this effort through the Cambodian Climate Change Alliance. Banteay Meanchey Sub-Operational Area Closes Real Shooting Training at Phnom Khla Kon
(Banteay Meanchey): The Banteay Meanchey Military Operations Area held a closing ceremony of a live-fire training course to strengthen the military capacity of Phnom Khla Kon in Khla Kon Thmey village, Kampong Svay commune, Serey Sophorn city after three days of training.
The ceremony on December 18, 2020 was presided over by Major General Seng Thearin, Deputy Commander, Chief of Staff of the 5th Military Zone, and was attended by Major General Chhun Mao, 1st Division Commander, Banteay Meanchey, Brigadier General Chim Bun An. Banteay Meanchey Military Operation Area Commander and many other trainees.
Brigadier General Chim Bun An said that the three-day live-fire training includes lessons such as security and order training, how to line up, how to use weapons, wash weapons and live ammunition. Distance and shooting distance sleep.
He further stated that all the trainees need to strengthen their capacity in this real shooting training, strictly follow the orders of the military instructors for good results, which the trainees work hard and pay attention to in this real shooting training. .
Brigadier General Chim Bun An further stated that the practical and theoretical practice in the training course has been conducted to increase security, public order and safety along the Cambodian-Thai border. Moreover, this training course is committed and ready to take action against the rebels who are trying to overthrow the legitimate government and try to destroy the peace in the country.
On that occasion, Major General Seng Thearin instructed all trainees after training to apply this knowledge to the target, such as equipment, weapons and ammunition for operations and to help people in disaster. Eventually.
Lt. Gen. Seng Thearin instructed all the military to patrol and protect the main targets and the town, assign special skills to search for the perpetrators, to carry out prevention and suppression of various crimes, and the military forces have the duty to follow the orders of the Chief of Police. The government and its superiors to protect the people, the nation, the religion, the king and the legitimate government.
He stressed that the forces must make efforts to increase security and security monitoring at international border crossings, regional border crossings and the Cambodia-Thailand corridor in Banteay Meanchey province.
