The Senate presents the results of the meeting of the Standing Committee of the Senate (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Standing Committee of the Senate on Friday morning, December 18, 2020, held a meeting chaired by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate.
A press release from the General Secretariat of the Senate, obtained by Fresh News, states that after review and discussion, the Standing Committee of the Senate has set the morning of December 21 and 22, 2020 to resume the sixth session of the Senate. Fourth, with seven agendas.
The seven agendas include:
1. Review and comment on the draft law on finance for management in 2021.
2. Review and comment on the draft law on the payment of the general state budget for management in 2019.
3. Review and comment on the draft law on state securities.
4. Examine and comment on the draft law on the organization and functioning of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority.
5. Review and comment on the draft law on the ratification of the ASEAN Agreement on Mutual Recognition on Pilot Licensing.
6. Review and comment on the draft law on the approval of: * The third protocol on the right to cooperate on domestic flights within the territory of any ASEAN member country. * The fourth protocol on the right to co-operate between Airports within the territory of ASEAN member countries.
7. Review and comment on the draft law on the approval of the protocol approving the 9th and 10th contract packages of air transport services under the ASEAN Framework Agreement on Services. The Ministry of Public Works announces the suspension of service centers at Aeon 1, Aeon 2 and Chip Monoromol Mall for 3 days due to relocation
(Phnom Penh): Due to the relocation of the technology infrastructure of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, which caused the impact on the use of the Internet and automation systems, the Ministry decided to suspend the service center at Aeon 1, Aeon 2 and Market. Modern Monorom Chip for 3 days.
In the announcement of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, which was received by Fresh News on the morning of December 18, 2020, it was stated that the service center of Aeon 1, Aeon 2 and Chip Mong No Rom Mall was temporarily suspended. Three days from December 18 to 20, 2020.
