(Siem Reap): The Ministry of Environment led a group of about 30 national and international journalists from 20 institutions to understand the payment of ecosystem services at Jayavarman-Norodom Phnom Kulen National Park in Siem Reap.
The visit is led by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, for three days, from December 18 to 20, 2020.
The senior official said that the Royal Government of Cambodia has entrusted the Ministry of Environment with the task of reviewing and studying and implementing the payment of this ecosystem service fee with stakeholders and preparing a policy of paying this ecosystem service fee for the Royal Government to review and decide. .
Neth Pheak explained that ecosystems refer to the interactions between living things and the environment or habitat in which they live, and that the flow of these interactions creates many benefits for people, which we call "ecosystem services" and necessary. Most need to be protected and conserved, such as protecting groundwater sources for long-term use. Water is an integral part of the planet's ecosystem. Without water, humans, animals, and plants would die.
