Angry wife could not resist taking pesticides to kill herself in Mongkul Borey district, Banteay Meanchey province
(Banteay Meanchey): A man got angry with his wife and took pesticides to kill himself. This incident happened at 10:40 pm on December 16, 2020 at Anha Chet rice field in Chak village, Rohat Teuk commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province.
According to the local police, the man who drank the pesticide was Prem Rath, a 40-year-old man from Chak Keut village, Rohat Teuk commune, Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Local police said that before the incident, the victim, along with two or three others, were drinking. When drunk, the victim returned to his hut and asked his wife to find medicine for him to swallow.
At that time, the wife replied that there was no medicine. The husband then says he will get some pesticides to drink. Immediately, the husband took pesticides and drank them, causing poisoning. At the same time, his wife was taken to the hospital and died halfway through.
Police confirmed that the victim had previously taken herbicide, but was rescued in time. The second time, he drank snail medicine and his wife tried to save him, but could not, so he lost his life. As for the corpse, the family arranged for a traditional ceremony.
