Police clarify that the perpetrators of violence against thieves in Sangkat Stung Meanchey, Khan Meanchey are not private security agents, but citizens who witnessed the incident
(Phnom Penh): Recently, a video was shared on Facebook about the arrest of a suspect who committed a crime in Sangkat Stung Meanchey III, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh. The video also shows the use of violence against the suspects by the people who witnessed the incident.
From the video, it was initially speculated that the perpetrator of the violence was a private security agent who apprehended the suspect, but later discovered that the perpetrator was not a private security agent. People living at the scene above, who hate the perpetrators of theft, have not been able to control the violence.
The acts of violence against the suspects were carried out by the two men, not the agents or employees of the MPC Security Company, they are the people living at the scene who hate the perpetrators. Theft has not been controlled to the point of violence. After the arrest, the suspect was sent by private security agents to the Stung Meanchey III Administrative Police Station for further action.
The Department of Private Security Management does not support private security in the use of violence against suspects, and thanks to the public for their cooperation in all aspects of the law in case an agent or employee of a private security company violates the responsibilities set forth in the internal regulations. Or the company's articles of association.
However, through this experience, the authorities have also shown no support for the use of violence against the perpetrators, because in the past, some cases even caused the suspects to lose their lives. Offenders are held accountable before the law, but the use of violence against individuals is also illegal.
