Experts found chemicals in 14 kg of soybean foam and 32 kg of expired cakes at Svay Rieng Veal Yun Market
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Pheng Nil, Branch Manager of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud in Svay Rieng Province, this morning, December 17, 2020, in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce, the local authority inspected goods at Veal Yun Market, Svay Rieng City. Svay Rieng province to find chemicals and goods that have expired.
Mr. Pheng Nil said that the inspection team inspected the food at the stalls in some markets and used the first test kits on 17 samples of food and 27 samples of vegetables and desserts. Come and test in a small laboratory to find banned chemicals that affect people's health.
He said that as a result of the inspection, the officers found 14 kilograms of borax in the bubble and 32 kilograms of expired cakes, and the officers confiscated the goods. Save it for later incineration.
