General knowledge: Which city has the longest official name in the world?
(International): Every country in the world has a major administrative city, which is the capital or the capital of their respective countries, while the name of each city is always short and long according to the definition and the call of the people of the country. But do you know which city has the longest name in the world?
If it is called in Khmer language, it reads "Krong Tep Mohanakor Bovor Rattanakosin Mahindra Yutthaya Mahatilok Phop Nopparat, Borey Rom, Udom Reachnivis, Mahasathan, Amarpiman, Avata Sathit, Sakkattiya, Vishnukam Prasidh."
Today, the city is popularly known as Bangkok, Thep or Rattanakosin, and the Thai capital is now 238 years old.
There is a lot of applause for allowing 12th graders to pass this year without passing the exam because of Kovid 19, but some students also want to show their ability
(Phnom Penh): The advice of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, allows 12th grade students in the 2019-2020 academic year to pass the high school diploma without having to take an exam due to the Kovid 19 crisis, leading to different views and perceptions. But there seems to be a lot of support as some students still want to show off their abilities.
For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the leader of the destiny of the whole nation, Samdech said that Samdech can not think only about the exam and bring health risks for the candidates and the society as a whole.
Despite Samdech Techo Hun Sen's suggestion, as of December 16, 2020, no official decision has been made by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports.
Although no official decision has been made yet. However, there are many opinions between teachers, parents and students who are candidates for the exam, some support, but some candidates want to have the opportunity to show their abilities.
Heng Vanda, Rector of Vanda Institute of Accounting and President of the Association of Higher Education Institutions, applauded Samdech Techo Hun Sen's decision. Mr. Heng Vanda called Samdech Techo's decision a good thing to avoid the risk of spreading Kovid 19 disease.
For Heng Vanda, this decision also facilitates the planning for higher education. According to Heng Vanda, higher education institutions are waiting for the 12th grade students 'exams to plan for the new school year, but if the students' exams are delayed, it will affect the higher education plan. .
"If the exam does not happen again and again, it will be a problem for higher education," Vanda said. "Higher education is just waiting for the national bankruptcy. If the national bankruptcy does not have results, higher education institutions have no strategy, because the strategic plan comes from that point."
Mr. Suy Sopharis, a math teacher at Prek Luong High School in Khsach Kandal District, Kandal Province, also applauded the decision of Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. For Mr. Sopharis, the decision of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on such a social context is the right thing to do to ensure the social stability and health of students as well as the people as a whole.
"The two-day exam is just a time to measure students' abilities," Sopharis said. But the current student, he tried hard to learn that the ability is not bad.
However, the math teacher only wants to exempt the exam this year. If the next year exams are held, students may drop out of their study efforts.
Lay Po, a teacher in Sihanoukville, said that given the circumstances, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's decision was correct and he believed that before making such a decision, he had carefully considered it. Therefore, this is a good decision as the head of the country.
"Under these circumstances, the prince's decision was right," he said. I believe that our country's leaders think very carefully before deciding anything. We, the children, have to follow him better. ”
Despite the enthusiastic comments, some expressed concern that the admission of the exam would affect the quality of education, as some students would give up their studies.
