(Phnom Penh): While the situation of Kovid 19 in Cambodia has not yet improved, Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, has ordered the leadership and officials under the Ministry of Tourism and the 25 Departments of Tourism to continue to pay attention. Regularly strengthen and monitor the implementation of tourism safety measures.
The strict regulation was made at a monthly review meeting to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 at the Ministry of Tourism on December 16, 2020.
In the above meeting, Mr. Thong Khon recommended to the leaders of the 25 Ministries-Departments of Tourism, including:
1: Continue to strengthen the implementation of tourism safety measures in tourism destinations and business bases throughout the 25 capitals and provinces in order to participate in preventing the spread of Kovid 19 in the tourism industry.
2: Introduce the professional sector to increase and strengthen tourism products, especially ecotourism, community tourism, agro-tourism, rural tourism, which may become a popular new tourism product during the Kovid 19 crisis, but must strictly implement the guidelines of the Royal Government and Ministry of Health.
3: Gradually study to attract international tourists again after the world officially recognized the vaccine against Kovid 19, while the Ministry of Health is optimistic that the vaccine will be officially recognized by mid-2021.
4: To actively promote vocational training in online tourism.
6: Strengthen the implementation of administrative work to manage civil servants by incorporating the new practice procedures, that is, all civil servants must consistently wear masks every hour to maintain safety gaps, to measure heat and to constantly spray alcohol. Wash your hands often with alcohol and monitor your symptoms. If you have the flu, stay away from others or have signs of suspected Kovid 19 need to see a doctor immediately.
As of November 2020, the results of the assessment and certification of tourism safety measures across the country have been totaled in only 1,416 locations, which the Minister urged to double the effort and must be summarized every month. . The National Assembly of the Cambodian National Trade Union Confederation disseminated and sprayed 19 Kovid vaccines at the Department of Training and Training (Video inside)
