Authorities are searching for the perpetrators of marijuana planting in Prey Phnom, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province, while more than 1,000 marijuana trees were burned
(Pursat): Authorities in Veal Veng district, Pursat province, are searching for suspects involved in a case of planting marijuana trees in the mountainous area for legal action, while 1,426 fresh marijuana trees that the perpetrators stole were planted by the police. Coalition cracked down, cut and burned on the spot on December 15, 2020 at a fertilizer depot located in Krapeu 2 commune, Veal Veng district.
The operation to crack down on the marijuana plantation was led by Mr. Ung Kimleang, Deputy Governor of Pursat Province, Lt. Col. Theang Leng, Veal Veng District Police Inspector, Provincial Police Force, Provincial Police Force and District Environmental Force, Director of Social Affairs, Joint District Governor. And the People's Protection Commune Authority with a total of 49 people.
According to Colonel Theang Leng, before reaching the crackdown, his forces searched for a long time to find the location and also planned to crack down on the mountainous area and the difficult situation. On the way through the forest, mountains, streams, which made the perpetrators escape.
During the operation, the police removed and burned 1,426 marijuana plants on the spot and confiscated some exhibits. Currently, the authorities are searching for the suspects involved in the case of planting marijuana trees for legal action.
