Ministry of Women's Affairs Holds Annual Meeting and Related Meetings of the ASEAN Commission for Women via Video
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Women's Affairs on December 15-16, 2020, organized the Annual Meeting and related meetings of the ASEAN Commission for Women through video, while Cambodia took over the chairmanship of the ASEAN Commission. On women from the end of December 2020 to October 2021, after Brunei Darussalam expires in 2020.
The Annual Meeting and related meetings on "Promoting Women's Leadership and Women's Participation in Politics" were chaired by Ms. Kheng Samvada, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Women's Affairs and Chair Of the ASEAN Commission for Women.
The Annual Meeting discussed in depth the draft of the new ASEAN Commission on Women Action Plan 2021-2025 to be submitted to the ASEAN Women Ministers for review and decision in the first quarter of 2021.
The Meeting agreed to set out a number of key documents to implement and ensure that gender is fully considered in the activities of the ASEAN Commission for Women, the ASEAN Commission on the Promotion and Protection of the Rights of Women and Children, and the ASEAN Inter-sectoral Institutions. Such as the involvement of some civil society working with women and girls.
Meanwhile, at the ASEAN Commission for Women meeting, the presence of ASEAN Plus Three, China, Japan and Korea also attended the 12th meeting of the ASEAN Commission for Women Plus Three via video.
Two workshops were organized, including:
1: Workshop on Promoting Women's Leadership and Political Participation in ASEAN in order to gain input on the successes and challenges of women in leadership and political participation in countries ASEAN member.
2: Discussion forum on the definition of unpaid work and domestic work in order to promote awareness and discuss the importance of tackling unpaid work and domestic work as contributing to strengthening economic empowerment. To women in ASEAN.
The Annual Meeting and related meetings of the ASEAN Commission for Women are an important forum for the ASEAN Dialogue to review the progress of work and determine the direction that can be taken to meet its five-year action plan. As well as achieving gender equality and protection of women's rights in the entire ASEAN region.
After failing in a legal battle to contest the election results, which showed that he lost to Joe Biden and after a majority of voters voted for Biden to be the 46th President of the United States, Trump will return. Return to private life when Mr. Biden is officially sworn in on January 20, 2021.
However, Donald Trump still has some opportunities at hand. Those opportunities include announcing his candidacy for the 2024 presidential election, appearing on television or returning to running his business.
What is clear, however, is that even after his term as president, Trump is believed to still have political influence, having set up a political action committee that will allow him to raise money and maintain influence. In the Republican Party after he left the White House.
Donald Trump, who has maintained that there is no evidence that the November 3 election was rigged, has told his allies that he will run again in the US presidential election next year. 2024. However, he has not officially announced the decision and has not confirmed whether he will attend the swearing-in ceremony of Joe Biden on January 20, 2021.
