General Department of Customs of Cambodia Participates in the 137th Meeting of the International Customs Cooperation Council via Video
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Se Sokhorn, Deputy Director General, Representative of Dr. Kun Nhim, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, led a delegation from the General Department of Customs and Excise of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to attend the group meeting. The 137th International Customs Cooperation Council, organized by the World Customs Organization via video.
In his opening remarks, the Acting Chairman of the Council said that the Global Customs Administration has played a key role in the global epidemic of Kovid 19 and needs to maintain momentum and prepare for the recovery phase in particular. Ensure the rapid delivery of key commodities, including the 199 vaccine, and increase support for economic operators.
In addition, he said, "the WCO Customs Administration and the Secretariat have shown resilience to adapting and responding to crises, and continue to develop guidelines, guidelines and standards for the benefit of all members."
As a result, the meeting approved some important work such as:
* First: Establishment of the Coordinating and Inspection Team for Passengers
* Second: Resolution on the role of the Customs Administration in facilitating cross-border traffic of drugs and vaccines
* Third: Declaration on Gender Equality and Diversity in Customs Institutions and Duties on Duty Free Zones, Small Island Economy, Conservation of Hazardous Goods, Data Analysis and Transit.
