Spokesman for the General Commission: On December 15, 579 more vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 229 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to December 15, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 234,110 vehicles were fined, including 172,142 motorcycles and 61,968 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet overcrowding, no license plate and cell phone use. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, drunk driving licenses, no seat belts and cell phone use.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 229 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
