Mr. Chea Somethy: So far, Prey Veng province has not had a single case of Kovid-19.
(Prey Veng): Mr. Chea Somethy, Governor of Prey Veng Province and Chairman of the 19-Kovid Disease Control Committee, said that in order to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, the Prey Veng Provincial Administration has continued to implement health promotion activities. So far in Prey Veng province, there has not been a single case of Kovid-19 infection.
Mr. Chea Somethy said this on the morning of December 15, 2020, during the meeting to disseminate the principles and measures to prevent and prevent the spread of COVID-19 at Hall A of Prey Veng Provincial Hall. From the President of the Provincial Court, Mr. and Mrs. Deputy Governors of the three forces, heads of departments and units around the province, district governors, provincial hall officials, members of the Chamber of Commerce and other relevant officials.
Mr. Chea Somethy also urged all stakeholders to take more drastic protection measures to educate people in all localities throughout the province on prevention measures, sanitation and measures recommended by the Ministry of Health. Increase and strengthen the implementation of these measures in all public and private units and factories in the province to be highly effective.
He added that the provincial administration has also set up a place to consult and provide screening services to people suspected of being infected and volunteers to be tested for Kovid-19, which is suspected to be related from the area. But the 19th Kovid was born at the end of the tower and in many other places.
He also urged all relevant departments, especially the Department of Health, which is responsible for the Ministry of Health to set guidelines to continue to actively implement the guidelines of the Royal Government to prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 virus is emerging globally.
The provincial governor also called on departments and units around the province to provide additional support to the Commission for the Prevention of the spread of Kovid 19 virus to ease the burden on the provincial administration as well as the people of Prey Veng province as a whole.
It should be noted that as of December 14, 2020, a total of 3,795 suspected Prey Veng people sent samples to the Institut Pasteur for testing with negative results. Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications announces measures to prevent Telegram attacks in the form of falsifying the names of leaders or other individuals
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications on December 15, 2020, issued a notification on measures to prevent telegram attacks in the form of falsifying the names of government leaders or other individuals.
The ministry's announcement comes after a significant telegram attack took place, with hackers carrying out attacks in the guise of impersonating royal leaders. Government or other individuals to transmit the virus via text message in a telegram program to deceive the targeted user (victim).
