Mr. Sok Kim Eang, Vice President of Peaceful Youth Coalition, Andong Meas District Branch, said that the statue of Mr. Ngoy Krong Paly is now born from the pure generosity of teachers and members of the Peaceful Youth Coalition in Ratanakkiri Branch. Donated their own funds to build the above achievements as a legacy for future generations.
Mr. Sok Kim Eang said that in addition to the statue of Ta Kram Ngoy, the Ratanakkiri branch of the Youth for Peace, led by Mr. Say Saman, built a statue of Jayavarman VII and a statue of Chuon Nath in Hun High School. Sen, Andong Meas district as well.
Mr. Mam Bassac, Principal of Hun Sen High School, Andong Meas District, said that this high school has a total of 582 students (282 girls) from 7th to 12th grade. The high school has a two-story building, built in 2012 as a precious gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia through Try Pheap.
With a video message on Facebook on December 15, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that: We can prevent it or not, it is within 15 days, now in 15 days So far we have taken control of the situation, but we have not finished the November 28 event.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that the situation of the November 28 community event was not the same as the November 3 event, which was passed on by the Hungarian Foreign Minister for a number of reasons. November 28 is a serious event.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the November 28 community event was under control but was not over for five reasons:
1: It is not yet known if there are any other places that the patient arrived to find, the patient did not tell or forgot the place arrived 14 days before the discovery.
2: Are there any direct or indirect affected people who do not show up for fear of testing, which is a risk of infecting the community.
3: Some sufferers do not have a second or third test date yet, because they have just been exposed to a positive Kovid 19 and only tested once or twice.
4: You have to do the catheterization from November 29 to the last positive result on December 14. Do not know if you have had catalysis 14 days or three tests?
5: In some provinces where the patient arrived before the disease was found, have all the stakeholders been found?
Cambodia first contracted 19 communicable diseases in the community on November 28, 2020, after the Ministry of Health found a positive 19 cases of measles in the wife of Chhem Savuth, the director general of the prison, at which time the source was unknown. No copy of this.
This community event has spread so far that the Ministry of Health of Cambodia has so far identified a total of 41 community outbreaks out of 18,828 directly and indirectly tested by the Ministry. Health continues to call on all stakeholders to participate in the Kovid 19 test and to be isolated.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who had been involved in battle since he was a young man and had gone through many difficult problems, considered that the fight against Kovid 19 was not an ordinary event. He revealed that every day he held his phone, shaking his hand to watch the news about the 19 cases of Kovid in Cambodia.
However, Samdech Techo asked the public not to attack Chhem Savuth because Chhem Savuth was also a victim.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also commended the working group of the Ministry of Health and the front-line doctors, sub-national authorities, relevant institutions, especially the people who participated in the event that is dangerous to our nation and people.
Recommendations and regulations issued by Samdech Techo Hun Sen include:
* First: Follow the rest of you who have not been tested in full or do not have enough time every day. Sub-national authorities need to check, do not rely on doctors, doctors are very tired.
At this point, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also instructed the Capital-Provincial Governors to pay attention to those who have to do charitable work, especially for poor families, and if those who come to do charitable work are the head of the family, they must pay the allowance before the period. 15 days, 20,000 Riel per day, do not wait to open once a day.
* 4: In shops, restaurants, cafes, supermarkets and banks, have people assigned to check the temperature if there is no mask and alcohol or hand gel, and arrange to keep more than 1 person safety gap. Half a meter up is necessary. Avoid crowded seats and be hygienic when customers leave the table.
At this point, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded all capital-provincial governors to monitor shops, restaurants, restaurants, banks, supermarkets, etc. If they do not follow the standards and guidelines of the Ministry, the capital-provincial governors have the right to temporarily close their businesses without No need to ask the Prime Minister for advice.
The Prime Minister stressed that the four measures to be taken are the key topics in the fight against Kovid-19 by treating ourselves as fear because we are afraid, then we will win Kovid and if we are strong Definitely a loser.
In this regard, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia has warned critics of the CPP-led government that there should be no confusion and, in particular, do not underestimate the morale of the Cambodian people. At the same time, Samdech expressed an unexpected feeling that the Cambodian people and people from all walks of life have donated money directly to the Royal Government during the crisis of the Kovid-19 epidemic.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen "Considers the donations from the people of Cambodia and philanthropists as a large-scale national movement, which I call" the pillar to protect the health of the people "and that I compare it to the national movement "People's defense in 2008, 2011 and to this day is the people's defense."
