The Prime Minister reminded the Royal Government's program to provide cash to poor families affected by the Kovid-19 crisis, in which the Royal Government has set out a three-stage or three-stage implementation mechanism, including:
Round 3: Implemented in October and will end on December 31, 2020. In October, the working group found that the number of poor families continued to increase to 674,146 families, with a budget of about 120 billion riels. In November, the number of poor households reached 73,592, with 126 billion riels to be provided, but the November budget is still pending.
Samdech Techo said, "Since the beginning of the budget for the first poor families until now, the Royal Government has spent about 674 billion riels, or about 160 million US dollars."
The Prime Minister continued that the program to provide cash to poor families in the third round will end on December 31, 2020, but seeing the situation has not improved, Samdech Techo decided to announce by providing cash assistance. To the poor in the fourth round for the next three months, from January to March 2021. By March 2021, the situation of Kovid-19 disease has not improved, the Royal Government will continue this work.
Please be informed that the Royal Government has allocated about 200 million US dollars to provide for poor families affected by the Kovid-19 crisis. Samdech Techo stated that if this amount is not enough, the Royal Government also has additional budget to solve.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia added that although the situation of Kovid-19 has calmed down by March 2021, the Royal Government will not give up, it is necessary to take some transitional measures such as reducing the budget. Offer them little by little at an appropriate time.
Samdech said that the budget used to solve the above problem is from the revenue collected from local taxes (taxes), non-tax revenue, customs duties, etc., which total budget is about 4,500 million US dollars.
Samdech continued that the Royal Government of Cambodia still has many other programs to support the people, such as the cash program for rural employment, which increases the budget up to 150 million US dollars. Notice! National Veterans Fund will pay the Social Security for December for the first 2 weeks from 2 pm on December 16
