Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen breaks through the education of his children
(Phnom Penh): The five children of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen are seen as the descendants of Kol Thida who have been liberated by good morals, ethics and behavior in society.
Educating children well is a necessary task for parents. In his book "Bun Rany, the Strong Wife of Cambodia" by Mr. Chhay Sophal highlighted the methods of educating children of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
In this book, Samdech Kittipritthbandit highlights that Samdech and Samdech Techo are lucky that their children are free from the path of Dharma.
But Samdech Kittipritthbandit also showed strictness and firmness in educating children.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit stated in Mr. Chhay Sophal's book, "I would like to inform you that my husband is a person who hates the children of the powerful and abuses the weak." He said this after marriage before we had children, which is why he and I focused on educating children on morality, ethics, behavior and virtue.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit added, “My husband holds a book on the relationship between school and family. He checked and commented to the teacher, asking for help educating about morality and character.
According to Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, Samdech's children were not lucky enough to drive to school. They had to walk from the Independence Monument to Chaktomuk School, except for Manet, who rode his bicycle and occasionally rode his motorbike to Sisowath High School.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit reminded that when Mr. Manet entered the high school, the school required his young students to guard the school. Manet also had to guard the school like other young people.
"The main goal of my family and I is to have equality among students without discrimination between the children of the people and the children of the powerful." This is the additional confirmation of Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit said that Samdech's family strictly disciplines children at home and teaches them to pick rice from rice before cooking. If any child makes a mistake, the children are all punished by having them sit together, read a book, or remain silent.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit also said that when his son went to study in France and the United States, Samdech Techo went to discipline his children by writing on the bathroom and on the wall. Like coming out of the bathroom, turning off the lights, not talking loudly outside the house, spending money, asking for permission from whom? Walking a few meters away from home, who to ask for permission?
"This is a strict rule, but the children do not make it difficult for us," he said. They know how to build and manage themselves well.
Mr. Hun Manit and Mr. Hun Many, although not completed their PhD (as of 2019), also completed two master's degrees in the United States and Australia.
