The Ministry of Rural Development issued a press release on the results of the International Forum on Poverty Alleviation hosted by the State Council.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, on December 14, 2020, attended an international forum on sharing experiences on poverty reduction organized by the Office of the State Council of China and the Ministry of Rural Development. China's State Council Information Office on "Promoting Global Poverty Reduction and Building a Unified Future Community"
According to a press release from the Ministry of Rural Development, obtained by Fresh News on the night of December 14, 2020, the forum was attended by leaders and ministers from various countries, UN agencies. National development partners, civil society organizations, media and research institutions as well.
The main purpose of this forum is to mobilize all stakeholders together to strengthen mutual trust in reducing global poverty, which is an important contribution to achieving the goal of sustainable development this year. 2030.
The purpose of the forum is to respond to the urgency and needs of the international community by adhering to the principles of multilateralism, peace and stability in the eradication of the Kovid-19 epidemic, as well as accelerating the global poverty reduction process. .
Lu Youngfu, Minister of the State Council of the People's Republic of China, welcomed the participants and all stakeholders to share their experiences and views on global poverty reduction.
The forum also discussed issues related to poverty reduction with the participation of countries, key development partners, the United Nations, as well as research institutes on policies and practices to respond to poverty reduction. Global poverty.
During the forum, he stressed the importance of the forum to share experiences and challenges, as well as to find solutions through building partnerships and cooperation to reduce global poverty, especially in Context of the Kovid-19 epidemic.
He also pointed out that the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Cambodia has become one of the leading countries in reducing poverty in the last 25 years.
He also stressed the importance of the participation of the People's Republic of China in supporting the development of rural infrastructure, especially in the areas of rural roads, water supply, sanitation and rural sanitation, as well as capacity building.
The forum identified the challenges of the past and raised appropriate response policies to contribute to global poverty reduction in the context of the Kovid-19 epidemic by working together on multilateral building principles. Peace and stability.
All stakeholders expressed their commitment and continued to work together to accelerate the global poverty reduction process.
