Pailin Provincial Prosecutor Orders Authorities to Seize Four Land Trucks Involved in Mountain Excavation
(Pailin): On suspicion that a trader used a machine to dig a mountain without proper rules, the Pailin Provincial Prosecutor ordered the Pailin Provincial Gendarmerie to lead a force to seize a number of trucks. Four units were stored at the Provincial Gendarmerie Command, while excavators were stored near the excavation site.
The incident of cracking down on suspected illegal machines took place at 12:30 on December 13, 2020 at the foot of the mountain near the top of the mountain, the land of Mr. Seav Sophal in Phsar Prom village, Stung Karch commune. Sala Krao District, Pailin Province.
According to the source, the owner of the machine, Ta Mab, a 52-year-old man living in Ochheukrom village, Stung Karch commune, Sala Krao district, was arrested by the Pailin Provincial Military Police under the order of Mr. Kong Chan Khemrith, Prosecutor Initially, the province confiscated 4 land trucks, including 2 right-hand drive vehicles, while the machinery was kept near the same place while being intercepted and released.
As of the afternoon of December 14, 2020, the four vehicles were still stored at the Provincial Gendarmerie Command, while the owners of the vehicles claimed that they had the law, even before the excavation. Also asked for the law to all institutions.
He added that although the owner of the machine claimed that there were correct rules, but did not bring him to check the law. Therefore, he will submit this matter to the Forestry Administration to prepare the case, if there is any mediation or intervention from any party in the province, he will prepare the case to be sent to the Ministry.
According to Mr. Om Virak, Director of Pailin Forestry Administration, on the afternoon of December 14, 2020, so far, the provincial and prosecutors have reached an agreement and the owners of the vehicles and vehicles. Go home too.
He stated that the upper mountain land is not yet a forest sanctuary, and has not yet been handed over for business, unless the above decision can be cleared to build a house or prepare for other things. However, most of the mountainous land in Phsar Prom village, Stung Karch commune, Sala Krao district has a solid title deed or almost everyone owns it.
