Police confiscated 3895 liters of wine and 532 cans, 75 liters of wine, a package of yeast and half a liter of wine. Authorities also destroyed 21 cans of glutinous rice and 21 petrol cans.
According to the Deputy Commissioner, after the operation to confiscate the above wine, the competent experts found that in the white wine, the drug has a high methanol content of 14.15%, which is usually allowed only. Only 05.10 percent. As a result, 131 local drinkers were poisoned, eight of whom died.
As a follow-up measure, the authorities as well as the competent authorities no longer allow anarchic wine production. The winemaker must have a valid license and must also produce wine according to the techniques set by experts. Separately, for wine, drug and methamphetamine, which the authorities confiscated, the provincial authorities and the authorities asked the court to burn in the coming days.
