According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 228 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to December 14, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 233,531 vehicles were fined, including 171,744 motorcycles and 61,587 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet overcrowding, no license plate and cell phone use. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, drunk driving licenses, no belts and cell phone use.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun said that for the past 228 days, the implementation of the new sub-decree to fine vehicles for offenses has been going well. He thanked and commended all the road users for their good obedience to the traffic law so far, especially the traffic police for their dedication and hard work. Tighten traffic with the highest sense of responsibility.
Please note that for December 14, 2020, traffic accidents across Cambodia also occurred 10 times, in which 6 people died and 15 people were injured (6 people were seriously injured).
