(Phnom Penh): On December 14, 2020, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, chaired an emergency meeting to discuss the role of the Cambodian Aquaculture Association in increasing aquaculture production. Cambodia to grow in both quantity and quality.
In addition, to meet market demand, reduce imports as Kovid-19 is spreading globally, especially the implementation of the Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen's statement that "agriculture is the pulse of the Cambodian people."
The meeting was also attended by Ms. Vuthy, Secretary General of the Ministry, Mr. Eng Chea San, Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Fisheries Administration, Mr. Sok Raden, President of the Cambodian Aquaculture Association and many other members. The meeting was held at the Ministry of Agriculture.
After discussing in detail and grasping the actual situation of the Cambodian Aquaculture Association, Minister Veng Sakhon introduced the following key points to the Fisheries Administration:
* First, to cooperate with the association to clearly assess the production capacity of local supply and additional demand by using the mechanism of collecting statistics on farms, breeding grounds and other business clusters and determine a clear supply quantity and demand.
* Second: To further strengthen and expand the work of disseminating technical, administrative procedures and existing legal documents to the members of the association.
* Third: Strengthen the work to prevent the crime of importing aquaculture products by cooperating with stakeholders and associations.
* Fourth: Help organize business clusters or breeding networks to easily manage production volume and demand.
* Fifth: Efforts to study more about breeding techniques to increase breeding productivity in the same pond area to ensure the health, prosperity and sustainability of Cambodia's aquaculture sector in the near future.
Regarding the Cambodian Fishermen's Association, Minister Veng Sakhon made the following recommendations:
* First, to cooperate within the association to increase the productivity of all kinds of fish farming, shrimp, turtles and frogs, both in quantity and quality, to increase the supply to the local market and reduce imports.
* Second: Organize a comprehensive set of fish farming business networks or networks, apply the correct techniques for both breeding programs, breeding programs and marketing programs.
* Third: Working together to implement technical procedures, administration and law enforcement more effectively to meet production standards, which is a good opportunity for competition.
* Fourth: Reduce inactivity, increase activities to encourage, support and disseminate market demand, quantity and price within the association widely.
* Fifth, to better cooperate with the Fisheries Administration to promote the Cambodian aquaculture sector and to participate in preventing the crime of importing illegal aquaculture in all forms.
Minister Veng Sakhon encouraged all members of the Aquaculture Association to pay more attention to the implementation of breeding techniques and expand the breeding business to seize and use the opportunities of this epidemic more effectively, both economically and socially. .
In the United States, the people do not directly elect the president, but the electorate represents the American people to determine who the president is. A total of 538 voters will gather this Monday (US time corresponds to Monday night, Phnom Penh time) in the capitals of their respective states to formally elect the 46th President of the United States. .
To be elected President of the United States, Trump or Biden must gather 270 votes. However, with 306 votes cast, Joe Biden is widely expected to become the new president of the United States, who will be officially sworn in on January 20. 2021.
44 People in Oddar Meanchey Province Affected by the "Community of 28 November" Completion of Relocation Can Return to Normal Work
(Oddar Meanchey): Forty-four people living in Oddar Meanchey province involved in the "November 28 Community" event have been released and are able to return to work after 14 days of probation. Samples were tested for HIV 19 three times, all three of which were negative.
Dr. Khlok Huot, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Health Department, said on the morning of December 14, 2020 that the results of the third test for 19 cases of HIV in 44 people were negative, meaning that they were not infected with the virus. 19 No, they were allowed to return to normal work.
The Director of the Department further stated that based on the instruction of the Ministry of Health and the guidance of Mr. Pen Kosal, Governor of Oddar Meanchey Province, the team of the Department of Health still pays attention to strengthen the implementation of duties and responsibilities on a regular basis in the center and the border. .
He also called on the people of Oddar Meanchey province to continue to pay attention to the implementation of the Ministry of Health to protect their families from the virus 19, especially to eliminate the November 28 event.
