A man stabbed his wife to death in Peam Ro district, Prey Veng province due to jealousy.
(Prey Veng): Due to the fire of jealousy spread, a man decided to stab his wife with a sharp razor blade, causing serious injuries, and his relatives and family rushed him to the hospital. .
This incident caused a surprise on December 13, 2020 at the house of Nhes Touch, located in Prey Angkunh village, Prey Kandeang commune, Peam Ro district, Prey Veng province.
According to the Peam Ro District Police, the suspect was Im Ath, 29, a Cambodian farmer living in the commune. He was seriously injured and was taken to Prey Veng Provincial Hospital by his relatives.
The source said that the suspect, the husband, after stabbing his wife and holding a sharp razor blade, escaped before the police arrived.
Currently, the authorities are investigating to arrest the suspects to bring them to justice.
A group of young people raise money to buy food to distribute to cyclists, grandparents and poor children
(Phnom Penh): A group of young people took part in humanitarian work by mobilizing to raise money to buy food and supplies to distribute to grandparents, cyclists and poor children in public places.
Mr. Chea Ratha and Mr. Ouk Panharith, Representative of the Humanitarian Working Group, said that this group of humanitarian activities took place on December 12, 2020, with the working group distributing humanitarian donations to grandparents and cyclo riders. Fifty poor children in need in an effort to help the country during the Kovid-19 crisis.
The team distributed at Wat Botum Vatei Park, including rice, pure water, fish, noodles, fish sauce, soy sauce, fish sauce, scarf, medicine, cola oil, soap, hand gel, soap, hand gel, alcohol and Kovid-19 protective mask. The other 50 children received a sandwich, a bottle of water, a can of orange juice and a budget.
The team also prepared 50 packs of masks, 5 packs of 74 hand wash gel masks and 90 packs of 5,000 Riels to distribute to the people on the street.
In addition to distributing gifts, the team also educates people to maintain high hygiene, wear masks and wash their hands regularly, spray alcohol or gel, and if not necessary, do not walk to crowded places. The charity team would also like to thank all the donors who donated food and supplies and funds.
