(World): In the world today, there are only two regimes that are chosen to lead the country, the monarchy and the republic, but in these two regimes, there are two different doctrines: Democracy and socialism (communism). Do you know which country was the first to have democracy and communism?
Democracy was first established in the 6th century BC, after the overthrow of monarchies in the Greek world. This doctrine first appeared in the ancient Greek city of Athens, but it is not exactly the same as modern democracy.
The ancient Greeks believed that in order for their society to be a good society, they had to rely on the rule of law, and that the laws had to be tailored to the lives of the people, not actually under the king's decree. As before. They are of the opinion that "a good society must be governed by ethical principles."
Socialism, or communism, was the theory of social equality by the German philosopher Calmack (Jew), but it was applied in the Soviet Union.
Today, the largest socialist country is the People's Republic of China. After the collapse of the Soviet Union in 1991, the former communist empire was transformed into a pro-democracy Russian Federation.
Socialism, or communism, began to practice about 25 centuries after democracy. Director and Officer of Svay Rieng Provincial Public Works Department donated more than 5 million Riels and 870 USD to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to buy Kovid-19 vaccine
