Cambodian boy rescued by Thai navy after drowning, Koh Kong provincial commissioner thanks Thai authorities for taking care of Cambodian migrants
(Koh Kong): A Cambodian boy was swept away in the middle of the sea after the boy was playing on the beach in Khlong Yai district, Trat province. In this incident, the Thai Navy No. 182 launched a rescue operation. Cambodia was on time on December 13, 2020 yesterday.
In connection with this case, on December 14, 2020, Major General Kong Mono, Koh Kong Provincial Police Commissioner through Fresh News, thanked the Thai authorities for protecting the safety of Cambodians who went to sample. Districts in Khlong Yai district, Trat province, to do business in Khlong Yai district can not return to the country to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 infection.
Lt. Gen. Kong Mono emphasized: “About 200 Cambodian workers who came to stay in Thailand, Khlong Yai district, Trat province, lived there, which the Thai authorities did not allow them to cross the border to return to the country for protection. "The spread of Kovid-19 infection."
The lieutenant general, meanwhile, thanked the Thai navy for saving the life of a boy who sold water, almost unaware that he was alive. Under the boy, he went to visit the sea on the beach alone and was taken to the middle of the sea by the waves.
General Kong Mono added that after seeing the case of a child drowning, the Thai Navy No. 182 immediately swam to the rescue, regardless of their own safety. The child victim is now safe and in good health.
The General confirmed that the Cambodian and Thai authorities continue to maintain solidarity and communication, although the two authorities can not communicate directly, but the two sides are still communicating electronically to provide information to each other. On the other hand, the authorities on both sides must protect the safety of citizens on both sides who are not allowed to cross the border to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 infection.
