Two illegal trucks transporting chickens and pigs from Thailand were raided by Kampong Thom provincial authorities
(Kampong Thom): The director of the Kampong Thom Provincial Veterinary Production Office, together with the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, in cooperation with the Kampong Thom Provincial Economic Crime Planning Commission, cracked down on two trucks transporting illegal pigs and chickens from Thailand.
Tan Meng Chhang, director of the Kampong Thom Provincial Veterinary Production Office, said that after inspecting 450 chickens and 23 pigs transported from Thailand to the stop, there was no permit and no health certificate. The animals are suspected of carrying the bird flu and African swine fever, which can cause serious harm to humans and animals.
Mr. Tan Meng Chhang said that he had sent a professional chicken sample to the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production for inspection, unless the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production confirmed the health of chickens and pigs before deciding to take legal action. Legal procedures for chickens, pigs or other animals that pass through must have a certificate of animal health and a valid legal document to prevent infection.
