The installation of anti-archeological border posts is for the purpose of identifying archeological lands that need to be properly protected, prevent illegal occupation by land traders, and make it easy for people not to know that they are encroaching on farmland or living on temples. Ponds and other ancient structures without knowing because they also want to better protect those archeological sites.
