To better understand the mandated representatives, the FRESH NEWS Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, this week brings the topic of "Mandated Representatives" to the people. The following students:
In principle, a person who can become a representative by mandate has only a lawyer to protect the interests of the parties who are dependent in the lawsuit. Mandate representation in each case. The person to be represented must make a contract or a written letter to clearly define the rights of the representative.
However, in the event that the person is not a lawyer, acting on behalf of the mandate is illegal and the court must dismiss the person involved. However, Article 53 of the Code of Civil Procedure also recognizes persons who can be elected other than lawyers as their mandated representatives as follows:
A: Where this Code or other law allows a third party who is not a lawyer to act on behalf of a party. (B) Cases where a party is a state, a legal body, an administrative body or another state institution, and in which that institution or its representative appoints the staff of that institution as its representative. Lawyer in the case where the value of the lawsuit is less than 1,000,000 (one million) Riels.
In addition, in the event that the representative by the mandate is a lawyer, the parties may not limit the scope of the right of representation, except as provided in Article 54, point 3 of the Code of Civil Procedure, including: Withdrawal from the case, conciliation, waiver, claim, recognition of the claim, withdrawal from the complaint, submission of appeal to the High Court, withdrawal of appeal from the High Court and election of Deputy Representative.
In particular, in the case where the mandate representative is not a lawyer, the parties may limit the scope of the right to be a mandate representative and have the mandate representative represent only some of the litigation activities determined separately by the parties. However, the provisions of the above paragraph shall not apply to a representative authorized by law to act on behalf of a party.
In summary, a representative by mandate is made based on the will of the mandate through a contract or a written letter stating the extent of the rights, obligations and the exact period of representation with the mandate to carry out the appeal action. Take it.
