Large trees in the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Park were destroyed
(Phnom Penh): Large trees in the Royal Academy of Kampuchea Techo Sen Russey Trip Park in Preah Vihear province's Cheb district continue to be cut down.
Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, pointed out that on December 8, 2020, about 300 large trees in the park were cut down. Dr. Sok Touch expressed his fatigue at the efforts to protect the forest in the park because the defense did not win over the loggers.
Dr. Sok Touch expressed his feelings like this: "I am very tired after patrolling on one side of the park of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, Techo Sen Russey Trip, the perpetrators cut down 300 trees that the logger. Know that I have not patrolled for almost a month due to the busy schedule.
According to Dr. Sok Touch, 31 families have recently settled in the park illegally. He said that his team inspected the houses of the 31 families and found 15 families, all with trees that were cut down from the park.
He added that hundreds of different types of trees had been cut down and found in the homes of people living in the park.
However, according to Dr. Sok Touch, with the cooperation of the Preah Vihear Provincial Administration, the authorities have prepared to provide land to these 31 families. The land in that area has adequate infrastructure such as: schools, pagodas, villages and wells.
The President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia appealed to the competent authorities to expedite the implementation of measures and solutions for these 31 families as soon as possible.
