Military in Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province Detains 3 Suspects While Distributing Drugs and Seizes Some Items
(Banteay Meanchey): The Armed Forces of Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province arrested three suspects in connection with drug trafficking and use cases and confiscated some items at 9 pm on December 11, 2020 in Samaki Meanchey Village, Sangkat Poipet City. Poipet, Banteay Meanchey Province.
The operation to detain the three suspects was led by Colonel Nuon Ninaro, Commander of the Poipet City Gendarmerie. Colonel Nuon Ninaro said that the arrest of the suspects occurred after receiving information from residents that they were selling drugs at the above point, he led the force to the place and arrested both. 3 people at a time.
The three suspects are: First: Choeun Barang, male, 24 years old, Second: Him Phea, male, 38 years old, and third: Him Phean, living in Poipet City. Armed forces confiscated drug paraphernalia, 3 small bags of white gram powder and 5 tablets of yama.
Currently, the three suspects have been sent by the Municipal Armed Forces to the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie Headquarters to build a case and send it to the Provincial Court for legal proceedings.
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen has called on all developed countries to fulfill their pledges, including financial support and technology transfer, to address global climate change.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen pointed out that many countries have been directly affected, including Cambodia, which has just been affected by the recent floods. Although Cambodia contributes little to global greenhouse gas emissions, Cambodia remains highly committed to the resources and capacity to address this issue.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that the new goal also includes 25% of renewable energy generation in the Energy Mix by 2030. At the same time, climate change is an interconnected phenomenon that needs to be addressed in a comprehensive package on social, economic and environmental aspects.
He said that, in fact, solving the problems caused by climate change effectively will contribute significantly to sustainable socio-economic development and the environment in the future.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the night of December 12, 2020, delivered a keynote address at the Summit on Commitments on Climate Change held online.
On behalf of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that we have all agreed that climate change is real. Many countries have been directly affected, including Cambodia, which has recently been affected by the recent floods. Although Cambodia contributes little to global greenhouse gas emissions, Cambodia remains highly committed to the resources and capacity to address this issue.
In order for the implementation of this long-term strategy to be successful, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on behalf of Cambodia, calls on all developed countries to fully fulfill their promised obligations, including financial support and technology transfer.
