As of December 10, 2020, during the posting of the first voter list nationwide, there were a total of 141 complaints, of which 139 were at the Commune / Sangkat Council level and at the NEC level. Two complaints. Of the 139 complaints at the Commune / Sangkat Council level, 120 were forwarded to the NEC.
There were 139 complaints at the Commune / Sangkat Council level (2 complaints, 136 objections, 1 complaint and 1 request for conviction) received from:
* 112 complaints from the Coalition Party for Democracy * 26 complaints from citizens * 1 complaint from Commune / Sangkat Councilors
Of the 136 objections, 135 were for the delisting of names of people who did not have housing conditions and one was for the removal of one of the dead. Separately, two complaints were filed to keep the names of voters.
The results of resolving complaints at the Commune / Sangkat Council level are as follows:
1: Decided to agree on 5 complaints, including: * Complaint request to delete 3 names * Complaint to keep 2 names 2 Complaints: Decided to reject 130 complaints 3: Make a letter of rejection To the plaintiff (a criminal offense not related to the election law) 1 complaint 4: Spy rejection of complaints (complaints not related to the initial voter list or revocation of rights or complaints without sufficient information)
* 104 complaints from the Coalition Party for Democracy * 18 complaints from the people
The results of the resolution of complaints at the NEC level are as follows:
* Decided to reject 25 complaints, which are objections to the decision of the Commune / Sangkat Council (the plaintiffs have requested the removal of 789 voter names). * 97 cases are being resolved.
Please be informed that there are three stages in filing, receiving and resolving complaints during the initial voter list posting:
