(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on December 12, 2020, attended the "Summit on Commitments on Climate Change" via video. The meeting was held to celebrate the fifth anniversary of the Paris Agreement on Climate Change.
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Hun Sen's participation in this morning's meeting on climate change was made at the joint invitation of United Nations Secretary-General Antonio Guterres, British Prime Minister Boris Johnson, and Emmanuel. French President Francois Hollande, Chilean President Sebastian Pinera Ichenik and Italian Prime Minister José Pekonti.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Prime Minister will also give a keynote speech on climate issues. According to the agenda prepared, Samdech Techo Hun Sen will deliver a speech between 11:30 am and 12 pm on December 12 (Cambodian time).
In this keynote address, the Prime Minister will highlight the serious impact of climate change on the world's socio-economic development, which needs to be addressed through joint efforts.
He will also highlight Cambodia's commitment to combating climate change with clear and effective measures and strategies, although Cambodia has a small share in global greenhouse gas emissions.
