Chairman of Ba Phnom District Working Group inspected the construction of two school buildings donated by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng
(Prey Veng): Mr. Prum Sokha, Minister of Public Works and Chairman of Ba Phnom District Working Group, inspected the construction of two 11-room school buildings, which was a precious gift from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng to Wat Neak Rainsy and Wat Pong Puos Primary School. In Rong Damrey commune, Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province.
The inspection of the school building took place on the afternoon of December 11, 2020, with the participation of Ms. Kong Salon, Member of Prey Veng Constituency, Mr. Prum Santhor, Provincial Police Commissioner, Deputy Chairman of the District Working Group, Chairman. Council, governors and district officials, as well as the head of the district education office, school principals, teachers and many others.
A 6-room school building in Wat Neak Rainsy Primary School has been completed but has not yet been officially inaugurated due to the situation of Kovid 19.
Another five-room school building at Wat Pong Puos Primary School is under construction and will be completed in early 2021.
