Court orders detention of Thai ringleader after cracking down on 50 kg of drugs
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Seng Rithy, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on the evening of December 11, 2020, issued an order to temporarily detain the ringleader after the police cracked down and confiscated 50 drugs. Kg. This is according to Mr. Kuch Kimlong, Deputy Prosecutor and Spokesman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, told Fresh News.
It should be noted that the Special Forces (A9) of the Anti-Drug Department cracked down on drug trafficking across the border from Thailand to Cambodia, arrested a Thai man and confiscated 50 kilograms of drugs.
The operation to crack down on drugs took place near the Victory Monument in Sangkat Prek Ta Sek, Khan Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh, at 2:40 AM on December 6, 2020.
The crackdown was led by Brigadier General Yin Panharith, Deputy Director of the Department, and Colonel Dos Sovatanak, Director of the Office, and coordinated by Mr. Ou Sopheak, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The operation was carried out under the direction of General Santibandit, the National Police Commissioner, and General Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General of the Anti-Drug Crime Plan, under the direct command of Lt. Gen. Lek Vannak, Director of the Department of Anti-Drug Crimes.
(Siem Reap): The APSARA Authority has confirmed that the 34th Technical Meeting and the 27th Plenary Session of the International Committee for the Coordination of the Protection and Development of the Angkor Historic Site (ICC-Angkor) are scheduled to be held in mid-December. Is postponed to a later date.
The reason for the decision to postpone the video meeting scheduled for December 15 and 16 at the Sofitel Angkor Phokitra Hotel in Siem Reap is in line with the Royal Government of Cambodia's guidelines to prevent the spread of Kovid 19. There is also the approval of the relevant institutions from the two co-chairs (France and Japan), the UNESCO office in Phnom Penh and the APSARA Authority.
As for the new date for the above meeting, APSARA Authority will announce again later. General Knowledge: Where is the oldest rainforest in the world?
The Indo-Malay rainforest, located in Malaysia, is the oldest rainforest in the world, older than the rainforests of Africa and the Amazon of South America. .
While other ecosystems have undergone many ecological changes, the Indochina Jungle has remained intact for more than 130 million years, which has diversified the evolution of flora and fauna in the rainforest. More than anywhere else.
