Promoting access to safe, equitable and effective vaccines is a top priority for ADB's 19 response to the Kovid epidemic. Vaccination programs can stop the transmission of the virus, save lives and reduce the negative economic impact caused by the epidemic by restoring confidence in work, travel and safe social interactions.
APVAX provides a comprehensive framework and resources to support the development of two-component vaccines in Asia. The Quick Response component will provide timely support for key vaccine diagnoses, vaccine procurement and delivery of vaccines from point of sale to ADB member developing countries.
The Asian Development Bank (ADB) is also providing $ 500 million worth of vaccine imports to support the efforts of its developing member countries to obtain safe and effective vaccines, as well as facilities that support the distribution and distribution of vaccines. Get vaccinated. This approach is part of the ADB's trade and supply chain financing program.
