It should be noted that on the evening of December 7, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced the provision of 1 million doses for the purchase of free vaccines for the first 50 people. Ten thousand people. Jean Malin: Identifying Kovid-19 positive's past is not a violation of individual rights and privacy, but a necessary measure
Jean Malin considers measures to identify Kovid-19 positive test takers at the "Nov. 28 community" event not as a violation of the privacy and privacy rights of Kovid-19, but rather as a necessary measure. In researching other stakeholders, directly and indirectly, to prevent the spread of contagion into the community.
Jean Malin made the remarks after UN Special Rapporteur Rona Smith and other human rights activists on measures to identify positive Kovid-19 test takers at the government's Nov. 28 community event. Cambodia led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
In response to this criticism, Mr. Jean Malin mentioned the following four points:
* Second, this identification is not a persecution and discrimination against those who are positive Kovid-19, because this measure has the voluntary participation of them and the top leaders have also made a public message. Also, do not discriminate against them.
* Third: This measure does not preclude the voluntary testing of other stakeholders as alleged, but instead it involves the participation and support of compatriots across the country, which increases the number of visitors. Voluntary testing, both directly and indirectly involved, has been steadily increasing.
And fourth, in response to criticism of the prison situation in connection with the "November 28 Community" event, the government has put in place strict and drastic measures to prevent the entry into prisons, including testing both direct and indirect stakeholders, including prison officials and those involved. Detention, Chaktalisak measures and other health and hygiene measures, etc. And so far there is no sign or indication that there is a positive Kovid-19 detainee yet.
