Director of the Department of Health: The results of the second test on 44 people in Oddar Meanchey province show that "negative Kovid 19"
(Oddar Meanchey): The results of the second test on 44 people, mostly provincial prison officials, provincial military police, provincial police officers and military officers in Oddar Meanchey province, show "negative" Kovid-19 disease. This is according to Dr. Khlok Huot, Director of Oddar Meanchey Provincial Health Department, who told Fresh News reporters in the province on the morning of December 11, 2020.
Dr. Khlok Huot said, "According to the Department of Infectious Diseases of the Ministry of Health, 44 people in Oddar Meanchey province who tested for Kovid-19 for the second time got good results. "All the negatives."
The director of the department said that despite the second negative result of Kovid-19, all 44 people, most of whom were civil servants, continued to be vaccinated and followed the instructions of the Ministry of Health.
Dr. Khlok Huot also called on government officials, the armed forces and all people living in Oddar Meanchey province to continue to be vigilant to protect themselves and their families from Kovid 19, the main measures to be taken. Regularly as directed by the Ministry of Health.
