Ministry of Health emphasizes care for inmates to avoid Kovid 19 infection
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health has claimed that the Royal Government pays as much attention to those in prison as the general population to avoid and prevent the spread of Kovid 19 without leaving detainees. That.
The Ministry of Health added that since the outbreak of the "Community 28 November" event, the General Department of Prisons of the Ministry of Interior has been investigating cases related to this community event, and who have been involved in prisons and monitored your health. Detention more thoroughly.
A report by the General Department of Prisons shows that no one affected by the "November 28 Community Event" had any contact with detainees, and from December 1 to 10, 2020, the First Correctional Center did not exist. The flu was suspected to be involved in the transmission of the Kovid-19 virus among both 354 officers and 7,608 detainees.
In this press release, the Ministry of Health called on all relevant institutions to implement the measures of the Ministry of Health in the spirit of maintaining equality and solidarity to prevent the transmission of Kovid-19 disease.
