The following is the announcement of the Ministry of Culture: 45 families in Phnom Leap commune, Banteay Meanchey province received training in raising chickens, fish and small business.
(Banteay Meanchey): Banteay Meanchey provincial authorities have provided chicken and fish breeds to 45 families returning from work in Thailand in Phnom Leap commune, Preah Net Preah district, affected by the Kovid-19 crisis, after receiving skills training and increasing skills. Small business under the funding and materials through IOM, with the support of the Royal Government. The supply of chicken and fish breeds took place on December 11, 2020.
Mr. Ngor Mengchruon, Deputy Governor of Banteay Meanchey Province, encouraged the people who have been trained to receive chicken and fish breeds to work hard to participate in the implementation of the IOM project to participate in the prevention of Kovid 19 disease. As well as increase raising well to get more capital for business expansion and raising bigger.
At the same time, he added that through the implementation of this project is proud of Banteay Meanchey out of three provinces (Banteay Meanchey, Battambang and Siem Reap), which Preah Net Preah district, especially Phnom Leap commune was selected as a model commune for the implementation of the project in the first phase under Funding and materials from IOM.
Mr. Em Nouy, Phnom Leap commune chief, confirmed that 29 of them raised chickens, receiving 100 chickens for each family. Twelve families raise 1,300 catfish per family and four families sell small items.
He said that all these are the expenses of the IOM, which has provided funds to the Royal Government to improve the lives of families of people suffering during the crisis due to Kovid 19.
