A foreigner sends pieces of temple stone from England back to Cambodia after he removed it from Bayon temple in 2006
Chuk Chumnor, director of the Department of Tourism Product Development and a member of the APSARA Authority's board of directors, said that the foreigner initially sent a piece of temple stone with a letter to Tourism Minister Thong Khon via DHL. From the United Kingdom.
After the jewelery was brought to Cambodia, a team from the Ministry of Tourism led by Mr. Chuk Chumnor picked it up and handed it over to the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts through the Department of Museums.
According to the preliminary assessment of the experts of the Department of Museums, this stone fragment may be a stone part of the diamond pillars of Bayon temple. The expert team will continue to analyze and register at the Museum Department or forward to the APSARA Authority for further management.
