Results of Online Election Observation in Indonesia by NEC of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sik Bun Hok, National Election Committee of Cambodia (NEC) has assigned 15 senior NEC officials to participate in the online election observation program for the election of provincial governors and deputy governors. Municipalities, deputy governors, district governors and regional deputy governors of Indonesia during the Kovid-19 crisis.
During the two days of observation from the NEC office from December 8 to 9, 2020, Mr. Mok Dara, Deputy Secretary General of the NEC and Chairman of the Observers. Participating in online observation is an opportunity to observe and learn about good practices in the Kovid-19 elections and the interesting use of information technology.
He said the Indonesian NEC had used a program called "SIREKAP" to quickly compile the results and announce the provisional election results. Indonesia is one of the first countries in ASEAN to conduct online election observation.
Elections in the context of Kovid-19 have prompted the Indonesian NEC to pay close attention to measures to prevent and prevent the spread of the disease by washing hands, keeping social gaps, wearing masks and setting up special secret rooms. Voters with a temperature of 37.3oC and drops of indelible ink on the little finger.
Mr. Mok Dara mentioned some important figures related to this election as follows:
Please be informed that this is the second time that the NEC of Cambodia has participated in the online election observation after participating in the election observation in Bihar, India. This online international observation program, in addition to the participation of the Cambodian NEC, also includes observers from member countries of the Association of World Electoral Institutions (A-WEB) and the International Fund for Voting (IFES). Also.
