Cambodia, the territory of Southeast Asia, is no different from the rest of the world. Kovid 19 disease has hindered Cambodia's development, which is causing a lot of problems for the economy and livelihood of the Cambodian people.
Despite the difficult situation, over the past 11 months, it has been seen that the Royal Government led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen has introduced a number of measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and maintain socio-economic stability. Also. Samdech Techo Hun Sen dropped many national budget packages to help solve the problem of people's livelihood, job loss and lack of livelihood.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also dropped the budget package for business expansion and agribusiness, a sector that helped the Cambodian economy breathe during the 19-Kovid crisis. In addition, Samdech Techo also introduced a policy to ease the conditions to help companies and businesses in Cambodia to continue to operate and maintain some jobs for the people of Cambodia.
For the past 11 months, although Kovid 19 has made life difficult for Cambodia, it has been seen that the Cambodian economy is not in a state of stagnation and the fight against Kovid 19 has improved.
Unfortunately, despite Cambodia's efforts to prevent the disease, Kovid 19 contracted into the community on 28 November and the source and source of the infection have not been identified. This event has caused great regret from the Royal Government of Cambodia. However, the Royal Government has put in place a number of emergency measures in accordance with the Ministry of Health's rules to cut off community outbreaks.
Despite the difficulties of the war with Kovid 19, which Samdech Techo Hun Sen called "war with the enemy in disguise" or "war with the shadowless enemy", the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo, did not give up and fought hard. Do not withdraw your hand to maintain the survival of the Cambodian people and the breath of the national economy.
As some countries around the world announce the success of the Kovid 19 vaccine, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government, has a high responsibility for the national destiny and the people of Cambodia also announced plans to purchase the Kovid 19 vaccine. This is also available to the public for free.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that he plans to buy the first step vaccine, about 1 million doses, to give to about 500,000 people. Samdech Techo plans to buy up to 20 million doses of this vaccine to give to about 10 million people.
On December 7, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced the purchase plan for Kovid 19 vaccine, which exploded with strong support from the Cambodian people who have been suffering from this disease for almost a year. That.
The Cambodian people not only supported the ideology, they also voluntarily released their own funds to join the Royal Government to end the crisis caused by Kovid 19.
Monks, Khmer kings, queens, leaders of the nation's top institutions, government officials, the armed forces, tycoons, tycoons, businessmen, businessmen, students, people from all walks of life donated from $ 1, two dollars to millions of dollars. As of December 10, 2020, the mass movement to purchase vaccines against Kovid 19 has reached nearly $ 40 million.
The resurgence of the purchase of vaccines against Kovid 19 is a manifestation of the great strength of the Cambodian people to overcome the difficulties of the nation and a demonstration of the spirit of "Khmer help Khmer". The current fundraising movement is also a clear demonstration of the full and strong support of the Cambodian people for Samdech Techo Hun Sen's plan to address the Kovid 19 crisis in Cambodian society.
The hardships caused by Kovid 19 are not new to the Cambodian nation. Cambodia used to swim miserably due to the crisis of decades of war, but finally the Cambodian nation overcame all those difficulties under the force of strong unity and build a society that is as proud as it is today.
The spirit of unity and solidarity of the Khmer nation under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia's outstanding leader, is still firmly believed that Cambodia will solve and overcome the difficulties caused by 19 Kovid disease now.
