(Phnom Penh): The relics of the coffin of Samdech Norodom Sihanouk were allowed to leave the pavilion of Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Saturday Chanthol, the chief abbot of Wat Lanka, to return to the temple to be open to the public to worship.
Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Saturday Chanthol told Fresh News that the relics of His Majesty the King, who went out to sit on the temple, were fragments of the relics that Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, the Queen Mother of Cambodia, paid homage to. Presented to him to prepare to sit in the stone urn in the pavilion to be worshiped and recited to the great King Kosal every Sabbath.
Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Saor Chanthol said that because he wanted to spread and open to the public, all classes have the opportunity to bow down to the relics that are sitting in Wat Langka, so he left The pavilion was kept at Preah Moha Bosbok in the temple.
The Queen has already given her permission at the request of Samdech Preah Thommalikhit Saturday Chanthol. In addition to allowing the royal procession to stay in the pagoda of Wat Lanka, Her Majesty the Queen also grasped the royal gift of $ 5,000 to build a new shrine for the relics.
It should be noted that Samdech Preah Norodom Sihanouk, the father of the Khmer nation, passed away on October 15, 2012 at the age of 90 in a hospital in Beijing, China.
After his death, his body was laid to rest at the Royal Palace in the Royal Palace. Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk also volunteered to donate a portion of the relics to Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Saturday Chanthol to worship and bless the royal merit every Shabbat.
