Spokesman for the General Commission: On December 10, another 459 vehicles were inspected and fined
According to the spokesperson of the General Commissioner, during the 224 days of tightening the road traffic law by increasing the fine according to Sub-Decree No. 39, from May 1 to December 10, 2020, the traffic police throughout the country inspected and A total of 232,130 vehicles were fined, including 170,910 motorcycles and 61,220 vehicles of all types.
Notable offenses for motorcycles are mostly helmet overcrowding, no license plate, cell phone use and drunkenness. The offenses for cars are mostly speeding, drunken driving, drunk driving licenses, no seat belts and cell phone use.
