In October, all Chinese cotton mills were ordered to stop buying cotton from Australia, threatening trade worth about $ 672 million as tensions between the two countries escalated. Strong.
Australian farmers were not immediately affected as they had little cotton in stock to sell after the drought disrupted production. But since the rains began to fall off Australia's east coast, farmers are expected to produce up to 506,000 tonnes of cotton, the highest level since 2018. Exports to other markets instead of China.
The source noted that China normally buys about 60 percent of Australia's cotton products, but is now boosting exports to Vietnam, Thailand and other Asian countries. Australia will begin its cotton harvest in April 2021, giving exporters more time to target new customers.
