Preah Vihear Provincial Public Works Department Director Calls on Responsible Citizens to Dispose of Garbage in Public Places
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Samleang Try, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province, called on people to be responsible in packing their garbage properly and avoid throwing it in public places. Many of the garbage piles at the Dang Stung Sraem bridge in Sraem commune, Choam Ksan district, have been cleaned by the road maintenance team of the department.
Mr. Samleang Try said on the afternoon of December 10, 2020 that dumping garbage in public places, in addition to disturbing the order, is causing more serious damage to the environment. The health of travelers as well as the health of people living near the dump.
In the spirit of participating in cleaning the sanitation and the environment, which is the core duty of every citizen, the road maintenance team of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Preah Vihear Province, whose main task is to repair and maintain the road, volunteered to clean the garbage. People take it away for a long time at the Stung Sraem bridge, and the environment at that point is improved.
