Delegations of the National Bank of Cambodia and the Bank of Vietnam hold bilateral meetings to exchange views on the economic and banking situation of the two countries.
(Phnom Penh): The delegation of the National Bank of Cambodia led by Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia and the delegation of the State Bank of Vietnam to discuss and exchange views on the economic and banking situation of the two countries online.
Every year, bilateral meetings between the two central banks are held with the aim of strengthening cooperation and friendly relations between the two central banks.
The meeting was successful and fruitful as the two central bank leaders discussed and exchanged views on the economic and banking situation of the two countries and praised the progress of bilateral cooperation between the two central banks. Significant for the growth of the banking sector and the economy in both countries.
The meeting set priorities and continued cooperation under the Memorandum of Understanding, which was updated in February 2017, and expanded the scope of exchanges of experiences and information, strengthening cooperation on joint work, such as banking supervision. With cross-border operations in both countries and the development of payment system connectivity as well as human resource development.
The State Bank of Vietnam commends the Royal Government of Cambodia for maintaining macroeconomic stability by stabilizing prices and exchange rates, strengthening the banking system and controlling the spread of Kovid 19. Good.
