Banteay Meanchey Police Inspect to Prevent Illegal Cross-Border Labor and Human Trafficking
This activity took place at 7 pm on December 9, 2020, led by Lieutenant Colonel Teap Kimheng, Deputy Director of the Office of Anti-Human Trafficking and Protection of Minors of Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police.
The lieutenant colonel confirmed that the mission lasted for a full month, moving to the geographical targets along the border. He said that when meeting workers who cross the border to Thailand illegally to be interviewed, they look for a broker to build a case for procedural action. In particular, if they go up on their own or through relatives, the force must prevent and educate.
At the same time, he urged the local forces along the border to work together smoothly to achieve success in this mission.
In addition, the Lieutenant Colonel also called on all armed forces and the people to maintain good health, hygiene, the environment, wear the right mask, wash your hands often with soap or alcohol, especially to follow the instructions. Of the Ministry of Health to prevent Kovid 19 infection. Mr. Nuon Sambo donated 999,900 Riels to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to buy Kovid-19 vaccine
