(Phnom Penh): Celebrating the 72nd Anniversary of the International Human Rights Day on December 10, 2020 under the theme "Rights and Peace", Mr. Keo Remy, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee, stated that Cambodia is a country Leading in Asia, receiving eight out of nine major human rights instruments, while the Cambodian Constitution does not have the death penalty and allows the presence of the UN Special Rapporteur on Cambodia.
After the country was liberated from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot on January 7, 1979, the rights and freedoms of citizens were fully restored to this day. Rights and freedoms allow people to live and work, big or small, freely choose their religious beliefs and elect their favorite leaders, and freedom also makes Cambodia more prosperous.
Mr. Keo Remy emphasized, "Recently, Samdech Techo Prime Minister has authorized the extension of the term of office of the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights, which will expire in December. Therefore, I would like to inform Cambodia under the leadership of "Samdech Techo Hun Sen, we are highly willing to continue the presence of the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner every two years and the Special Rapporteur of the United Nations."
