The following is the Royal Decree: Major General Seng Thearin informs the Cambodian-Thai liaison team to inform the Thai side to remove the demining signs at border post 32-33.
(Banteay Meanchey): Major General Seng Thearin, Deputy Commander of the 5th Army Division, on the morning of December 9, 2020, led a working group to meet with Major General Prum Roeun and Major General Tim Tum, Deputy Chief of the Land Border Police Department to discuss and resolve. About the Thai side's demining activities between border post No. 32-33 in Samaki village, Kouk Romiet commune, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Major General Seng Thearin told the Cambodian-Thai border liaison team to inform the Thai side to remove all the mine signs within two days from today. If the demining signs are not dismantled in two days, the forces stationed there will dismantle themselves and all activities along the border, let the Thai side inform each other.
After the discussion, the working group inspected the actual Thai demining target at Samaki village, Kouk Romiet commune, Thmor Puok district, Banteay Meanchey province.
