(Prey Veng): Farmers in Prey Veng province harvested rain-fed rice in 2020 with better yields due to scattered rains throughout the province and due to the maze of canal infrastructure, making the province rain-fed. As of December 7, the total yield was 214,652 hectares and the yield was 692,302 tons, while the average yield was 3.23 tons per hectare.
He said that the rainfall level has also improved this year, increasing the rice yield from year to year, especially due to the infrastructure of canals, labyrinths and roads in the province, which led to the transport sector. Both waterways and landways make it easy to transport agricultural products to markets and neighboring countries.
For short-term cultivation of horticultural and industrial crops in the dry season, a total of 630 hectares were applied, including 630 hectares of all kinds of vegetables and 1,940 hectares of industrial crops, 1,380 hectares of red corn, 519 hectares of soybeans, 5 hectares of peanuts and sesame. 1 hectare of sugarcane, 3 hectares of lotus, 30 hectares.
