The call by the Supreme Leader of the Royal Government of Cambodia was made at the 9th Ayayawadi-Chao Phraya-Mekong Economic Cooperation Strategy Summit (ACMECS) on December 9, 2020. Samdech Techo Hun Sen is chairing this summit.
Under the theme "Partnership for Connectivity and Strength", ECMEC reaffirmed its firm commitment to fully tap the subregion's enormous economic potential. Develop action plans to achieve a more connected, intelligent, sustainable and strong ECM community based on the spirit of good neighborliness and traditional friendship in achieving peace, stability and prosperity.
ECMEC leaders commend Cambodia for its two-year presidency in advancing member states' common goal of achieving the prosperity and well-being of its people in the face of the challenges posed by the Kovid-19 pandemic and security issues. Non-traditions on livelihoods and socio-economic development in the subregion.
