The Ministry of Foreign Affairs states that the main results of the three summits are as follows:
Under the theme "Partnership for Connectivity and Resilience", ECMEC leaders reaffirmed their strong commitment to fully exploiting the subregion's enormous economic potential and to develop action plans to achieve this. Achieve a more connected, intelligent, sustainable and strong ECM community based on the spirit of good neighborliness and traditional friendship in achieving peace, stability and prosperity.
ECMEC leaders commend Cambodia for its two-year presidency in advancing member states' common goal of achieving the prosperity and well-being of its people in the face of the challenges posed by the Kovid-19 pandemic and security issues. Non-traditions on livelihoods and socio-economic development in the subregion.
In the fight against Kovid-19, the leaders agreed to continue to strengthen national efforts and enhance cooperation within the framework of the ASEAN-led mechanism with non-regional partners and international organizations, especially the World Health Organization. Provide vaccines as public goods and access to affordable medical services for the people.
With regard to socio-economic rehabilitation, the leaders discussed ways and principles for cooperation in which member countries can promote safe and secure multi-sectoral connectivity and address issues related to Kovid-19 on migration. And global value chains, as well as ensure adequate protection of society and affected people.
The leaders concluded the meeting by approving the Phnom Penh Declaration of the 9th ECEM Summit, which consisted of 3 documents as annexes: (1) the reference document on the ECEM Development Fund (2) the concept document on the mechanism The work of the ECMEC Coordinating Committee of the ECMEC Master Plan 2019-2023 and (3) the list of ECMIC priority projects.
Under the theme "Promoting Effective Connectivity for Regional Integration", CLMV leaders expressed satisfaction with the implementation of the outcome of the 9th CLMV Summit and reaffirmed the long-standing traditional friendly relations. Good neighbors and mutual interests among the four member countries also exchanged views on the future direction of CLMV cooperation, which is an important part of the ASEAN Community Building Process.
Leaders reiterated the importance of CLMV cooperation in narrowing the development gap in ASEAN, ensuring peace, stability, prosperity and improving the living standards of the people in the region, as well as making it an important element in multilateral efforts. To fight and recover from the Kovid-19 pandemic.
To address future challenges, the leadership highlighted the importance of the CLMV Action Plan (2021-2022), which was approved by the CLMV Minister of Economy on August 24, 2020, stating a clear direction for trade and economic cooperation. Invest in human resource development, implement regional commitments, post-Kovid 19 rehabilitation and framework for turning the region into a global business hub.
With the primary objective of the mechanism to deepen and accelerate ASEAN integration efforts, the leadership attaches great importance to the effective implementation of the ASEAN Connectivity 2025 Master Plan, which focuses on infrastructure, institutions, economies and People-to-people contacts, as well as the Fourth Action Plan of the ASEAN Integration Initiative (2021-2025).
The leaders of Cambodia, Laos, and Vietnam expressed their strong commitment to promoting the development of the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Triangle (CLV DTA) with the vision of accelerating economic growth, reducing poverty and socio-cultural progress. By harnessing the potential, strength and resources of each member country.
The leaders acknowledged that Kovid-19 has caused great harm to public health and socio-economic development, so strengthening all-round cooperation between the three member countries is important and necessary, focusing on traditional ties, solidarity and cooperation. Understand, trust, common interests and sustainable development.
During the meeting, the Prime Minister highlighted the need to continue cooperation between the CLV countries in the fight against human trafficking and drugs, transnational crime, forest crime and other transnational crimes, as well as Demining, as well as facilitating the crossing of borders for passengers.
