The National Bank of Cambodia is very proud that the management of the National Bank of Cambodia has received the "Future Payment System" award from the Center for Finance, Technology and Entrepreneurship and the Budapest Banking Institute.
In fact, seeing that the payment of banking and financial institutions in Cambodia is not yet able to make cross-institutional payments, most institutions have set up payment systems to serve only customers of their own institutions, while some institutions have cooperated. Provide bilateral payment services with its partners.
Bakong System is a core payment system infrastructure to enable member banking and financial institutions to conduct interoperability payments safely, efficiently, free of charge, transfer services, reduce transaction costs and promote Financial environment.
The Bakong system has been involved in the promotion of non-cash payments, which we have seen an increase in the demand for electronic payments in the countries affected by Kovid 19.
The launch of the Bakong system is another breakthrough that the National Bank of Cambodia has achieved in modernizing its payment systems in response to current economic and financial developments and contributing to the country's economic growth. The digital economy is in line with the Industrial Revolution 4.0 and the regional digital economy.
