(Pursat): An ISUZU pick-up truck and equipment including 2,000 bottles of alcohol gel and 50,000 masks), a precious gift from the Pursat Provincial Chamber of Commerce, were handed over to the Pursat City Police Inspectorate and the Pursat Provincial Administration. To be used in daily work and to meet the needs of the provincial administration in the fight against Kovid-19.
The handover ceremony was held at the Provincial Hall with the participation of Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of the Provincial Committee for Combating Kovid-19, Mr. Oknha Tuy Ky, President of the National Assembly. Provincial Chamber of Commerce, Ladies and Gentlemen, Provincial Councilors, Deputy Provincial Governors, Deputy Provincial Commissioners, Chiefs of the People's Office and many other members of the Provincial Chamber of Commerce.
