Senior Minister Ly Thuch Delivers Keynote Address at Seminar on "Digital Use of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia and Laos"
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ly Thuch, Chairman of the National Committee for ESCAP (NCCC) of the Royal Government of Cambodia, delivered a keynote address at the seminar on "Digital Use of Small and Medium Enterprises in Cambodia." And Laos ”co-organized by the Espec National Committee and the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (UNESCAP) on December 9, 2020 via video.
The purpose of this workshop was to raise awareness of the current situation, challenges and opportunities for the use of digital systems by small and medium enterprises in Cambodia and Laos, including government cash assistance programs and remittances. Both provide a forum for discussion and exchange of knowledge and experience between the private sector, the state and UN agencies, especially regional policy makers.
The workshop was attended by civil servants, representatives of small and medium enterprises in Cambodia, digital service providers, financial service providers, development organizations, NGOs, as well as experts in the field of digital economy and micro enterprise development. And medium.
On the topic of the seminar, Senior Minister Ly Thuch said that global experience shows that the Kovid 19 crisis has changed our way of communicating, working and living, and that industry and industry are facing challenges. With the supply and demand issues and the uncertain future of the world, we also observe that digital technology has played an important role in addressing these issues.
"Crisis" can be dangerous, but it can also be "opportunity", so we need to be optimistic and consider the Kovid 19 crisis as an opportunity to improve the way we work and do business, ”he said. Various.
The Senior Minister also mentioned some positive changes through digitalization during the 19-Kovid Crisis, such as:
On that occasion, the Senior Minister also mentioned the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia to prevent the spread and mitigation of the effects of Kovid 19 and the use of digital solutions in the "cash support program for poor and vulnerable families. Accident during Kovid 19 disease.
In addition, the Royal Government has decided to establish the "Cash Support Program for Poor and Vulnerable Families During Kovid 19", a special social assistance program aimed at helping the poor with equity cards (K-1 and K-). 2) In order to facilitate the lives of people living in poverty and affected by Kovid-19, including those who lost their jobs or lost their income to fall back into poverty. .
The launch of this program clearly shows that the Royal Government, if "dare to speak, dare to do" and do it with the utmost precision and caution. At the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia also uses digital solutions to increase the efficiency of the implementation of the program. This is by giving money to the beneficiaries through Wing Specialized Bank, which has a network of agents across the country.
He said that this is the first time that we can give money to the people who benefit a lot in a short time, and one of the factors of success in implementing this program is because the Royal Government of Cambodia has embraced the use of this new technology.
