Murder starts from a land dispute! Man stabbed to death in Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province
(Kampong Chhnang): A man was hacked to death immediately at the scene near a canal next to a red gravel road. This incident happened at 23:20 pm on December 6, 2020 at the point of Lral Krous Krahorm Road in Kok village, Peany commune, Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province.
Lieutenant Colonel Hang Socheat, Deputy Commander of Justice Planning of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Gendarmerie Command, told Fresh News on December 9, 2020 that the victim, 40-year-old Nhean Noy, lived in Spean Dek village. Thlok Vien Commune, Samaki Meanchey District, Kampong Chhnang Province. The victim was stabbed three times in the head, one in the right neck and one in the right arm.
In front of the police, the suspect confessed that before he decided to kill the victim, he first went to sleep at 11 pm on the day of the incident. The victim then took the knife to the victim, so the suspect fled on a motorcycle, but was followed by the victim on a motorcycle.
When he arrived at the scene, when the victim was riding a motorcycle, the suspect pulled out a knife and cut the victim, causing his death at the scene.
Fire at Furniture Processing Factory on National Road 21 in Sangkat Roka Khpos, Takhmao City
(Kandal): At around 10 am on December 9, 2020, a fire broke out at a furniture processing factory located along National Road 21 in Prek Samrong village, Roka Khpos commune, Takhmao city, Kandal province.
According to a report from Fresh News in Kandal province, after the fire, the specialized police force immediately intervened and so far can be completely controlled.
Separately, the fire trucks that came out to put out the fire included the vehicles of the Kandal Provincial Police, the bodyguard command and the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Department. However, for the cause of the fire, the authorities have not yet confirmed because it is researching.
